ath.md) — verification is construction; no project data in probe.\n- [Live-test on Mac](live-test-built-app-on-mac.md) — shared bundle id; second monitor; launch with open -n.\n- [zsh $VAR:path](zsh-var-colon-path-trap.md) — write `${U}:path` or git refs get mangled.\n- [Bash cwd resets](bash-cwd-resets-after-background.md) — cd explicitly or use absolute paths.\n- [Rebrand seams](jusprin-rebrand-seams.md) — 3 seams + 1 attachment point, logo overlay.\n- [Report outcomes](report-outcomes-not-obstacles.md) — skip solved-problem narration.\n- [Chip seams](jusprin-chip-orca-seams.md) — set_bed_type_accord_combox; no filament-preset call.\n- [Bitmap proof](render-widget-to-bitmap-for-visual-proof.md) — green checks hid two defects; render to PNG.\n- [Windows GUI VM](windows-gui-test-vm-gcp.md) — headless testing; Mesa, Defender, session traps.; [Windows VM build](windows-build-on-gcp-vm.md) — full build works; quote -m:6; kill by PID.; [Linux ARM build](linux-arm-docker-build.md) — deps build on aarch64 in 45 min; reuse Dockerfile.\n- [HeaderMenu](header-menu-closes-before-invoking.md) — callbacks outlive popup; controllers shared_ptr.\n- [Panel CSS](agent-panel-css-namespaces.md) — styles.css is global; `setup-*` is taken.\n- [Guard tests](prove-guard-tests-fail-first.md) — Vitest CSS imports are empty; inject a violation.\n- [Fake Moonraker](fake-moonraker-printer-sim.md) — NOT on jusprin-newui; enable_ssl_for_mqtt=false.; [Fake Bambu](fake-bambu-printer-sim.md) — on jusprin-newui; FakeBambuAgent replaces only the agent.; [Fake-printer cleanup](harness-fake-printer-cleanup.md) — deselect, erase record, or later checks stall.\n- [Branch check](verify-current-branch-before-memory-recall.md) — grep the tree before trusting a memory.\n- [Posted keys](drive-app-with-posted-key-events.md) — CGEvent keys work on a locked screen; mouse no.\n- [Subagent worktrees](subagent-worktrees-create-manually.md) — isolation cuts a stale base; make by hand.\n- [Mac popup capture](capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff.md) — app_screenshot takes a CGWindowID.\n- [PopupWindow crash](popupwindow-hovered-dangling-crash.md) — a96ea65081 wxWeakRef; MallocScribble repro.\n- [GUI lib over 4 GiB](liblibslic3r-gui-4gib-ar-limit.md) — Apple ar asserts; manual llvm-ar relink.\n- [Subagent waits](subagent-must-not-stop-to-wait.md) — ending a turn to wait kills it; block.\n- [Embedded setup](agent-setup-embedded-in-printer-dialog.md) — second AgentWebView, CallAfter teardown trap.\n- [Web bundles](web-bundles-committed-artifact-state.md) — CMake-built, gitignored; *_DEV_URL for HMR.\n- [Bash timeout](background-bash-timeout-kills-builds.md) — exit 130 is the timeout; nohup long builds.\n- [Harness post-init](workspace-harness-never-post-inits-on-mac.md) — exit via ExitMainLoop on Mac.\n- [Printer panel 19b](printer-conversation-panel-19b.md) — Home printers column becomes chat.\n- [Handoff docs](handoff-docs-not-committed.md) — read from main checkout; never commit.\n- [Web view delete](webview-destroyed-mid-handler-install.md) — never during is_adding_script_handler().\n- [Temp docs](temp-docs-stay-untracked-and-visible.md) — stay untracked; never hide via ignore files.\n- [Fake-host page](fake-host-page-fixture.md) — inject window.wx to drive AgentUI/HomeUI states.\n- [Printer-live traps](printer-live-harness-lessons.md) — chat-open ignores opens; key-holding data dirs.\n- [Screenshot files](screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture.md) — replay host state under Playwright.\n- [\"Connect\"](printer-setup-connect-means-verify-and-save.md) — means verify and save, not keep-alive.\n- [Bambu deviceIds](printer-prompt-card-wording-breaks-connect.md) — fixed by tool-call replay 115e2776bf.\n- [Worktree ownership](never-reuse-another-sessions-worktree.md) — clean + idle is not unowned; make your own.\n- [Closed panel](printer-live-null-host-fix-paused.md) — crash fixed 6a43afff90; check after close fails.\n- [Tool history replay](printer-chat-tool-history-replay.md) — saved callId, no item id, 16 KiB cap.\n- [Filament chip](filament-chip-no-spool-decisions.md) — Orca concepts only, swatches, no spools.\n- [Autosave design](autosave-design-research.md) — two \"modified\" trackers; Kenneth's three decisions.; [Autosave cost](autosave-save-cost-results.md) — mesh saves block ~2.3 µs/triangle of largest object.\n- [Full-disk save](orca-save-silent-corruption-disk-full.md) — export reports success, damages the 3MF.\n- [Mockup strings](mockup-strings-from-real-output.md) — use rule-generated strings, not typed ones.\n- [Print issues](persistent-print-issues-spike.md) — Ask AI / Resolve on Prepare; decisions, gaps.\n- [GL readback](harness-gl-readback-capture.md) — locked screen blanks blits; glReadPixels(GL_FRONT).\n- [Main checkout](worktree-session-cannot-write-main-checkout.md) — a hook refuses Write; use worktree root.\n- [Eval measurements](project-prompt-eval-sample-size.md) — stub rates (\"1 in 15\") are retracted.; [Live eval](live-eval-after-only-vs-baseline.md) — no same-day before run; results become baseline.; [Eval spend](prompt-eval-spend-budget.md) — no live-model tests without Kenneth approving a batch.; [Harness critique](project-prompt-harness-critique.md) — old renderer obsolete; port plan.; [Harness ported](project-prompt-harness-ported.md) — requests recorded by --project-prompt-requests.\n- [Report frame](investigation-report-four-part-frame.md) — problem / solution / tests / remaining; <500 words.\n- [Model-probe harness](model-probe-live-chat-harness.md) — uncommitted; drives the live chat from files.\n- [Manual MCP repro](manual-mcp-tool-repro-recipe.md) — --manual-mcp + probe.call, ~20 s, no model.\n- [Settings blacklist](settings-write-blacklist.md) — tools write all but 51 blocked keys.\n- [Token sync](design-token-sync-decisions.md) — Figma sizes: chip 28, rows 36, icon 32/26.; [Design source](design-source-is-claude-artifacts.md) — Claude artifacts; Figma is frozen.; [Design artifacts](jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact.md) — source of truth; direct-edit recipe.\n- [Edit questions](orca-edit-questions-forwarded.md) — preview warns `skipped_confirmation`; agent decides.\n- [Chrome extension](claude-in-chrome-lives-in-claude-profile.md) — needs a Chrome Profile 20 window.\n- [Deferral commit](jusprin-newui-deferral-commit-removed.md) — 491b56d26b only on feature/tool-deferral.\n- [No tool approval](tool-call-approval-removed.md) — valid calls start at once; never ask to approve.\n- [Write like a person](write-like-a-person.md) — full sentences; say what the person sees, no noun phrases.\n- [Ask decisions in full](ask-decisions-in-full.md) — what, why his, options, consequences, my pick.\n- [pgrep wait loop](pgrep-wait-loop-matches-itself.md) — matches itself; wait on the PID with kill -0.\n- [Ask AI = Resolve](ask-ai-same-tools-as-resolve.md) — same tools, only the sentence differs.\n- [Orca MessageDialog](use-orca-messagedialog.md) — never wxMessageDialog; file opens auto-answer.\n- [Action id collision](printer-panel-action-id-collision.md) — t-1 restart → false local_save_failed; fixed.\n- [Previews skip validate](printer-setup-bed-type-check.md) — Print::validate runs only at slice.\n- [Rare failures](rare-failures-get-a-generic-error.md) — one generic error, no per-cause handling.\n- [Tool result states](tool-result-states-method.md) — Kenneth’s test: a person stuck, false, right step hidden; eight of nine sweep fixes taken out; how the statement drifted.\n- [Forward the real error](forward-the-real-error-four-rules.md) — four rules for false results; no new checks, no OrcaSlicer files.\n- [Prompt sections](project-prompt-sections.md) — five sections; policy out of tool descriptions.; [Rule placement](rule-lives-next-to-what-it-governs.md) — one-tool rules in description, rest in prompt.; [Prompt channels](prompt-principles-vs-state-channels.md) — standing prompt = principles; the rest from the app.\n- [History trimming](history-trimming-by-size.md) — 64 KiB budget in three stages.\n- [Input tags](workspace-input-tags.md) — user message parts with <workspace>/<print_issue>.\n- [Print-setup cases](print-setup-prompt-cases.md) — print-this-no-purpose; recorder traps.\n- [Harness stall](harness-stalls-on-version-dialog.md) — Orca update dialog; fix in 87b3c50474.\n- [Every tool call runs](every-tool-call-runs.md) — parallel_tool_calls true; in order, not_run after failure.\n- [State guidance](state-driven-guidance-project-chat.md) — plate picture + note on file-open turn.\n- [File-loaded skill](skill-model-arrived.md) — skills loader, file_loaded, skill_read.; [Slice-failed skill](skill-slice-failed.md) — unmerged branch; per-plate slice_failure.; [Setup-changed skill](skill-setup-changed.md) — setup_changed trigger, intent reply facts.; [Print-issues skill](skill-print-issues.md) — chip + slice warnings, sliceWarnings.; [Skills integrated](skills-integrated-branch.md) — merged as 8913319cac, pushed.\n- [Restore temp edits](restore-temp-edits-from-a-copy.md) — from a copy, never `git checkout <file>`.\n- [Stated facts](state-fact-test-the-turns-after.md) — \"since X\" needs a reset rule, multi-turn test.\n- [Recorder noise](request-recorder-run-to-run-noise.md) — timestamps, PNG bytes, temp paths only.\n- [Normalize](normalize-derive-current-from-relations.md) — derive \"current\" from the active chat.\n- [DeepSeek images](live-app-deepseek-drops-images.md) — 404 on image input, shown as network_error.\n- [bed_exclude_area](orca-bed-exclude-area-rule.md) — 4 points per box; Kobra 3 makes all \"outside\".\n- [Harness data dirs](delete-only-your-harness-data-dir.md) — delete only yours, never the glob.\n- [Setup card headline](setup-card-headline-setup-record.md) — setup_record: purpose, flat plan, unverified.; [Setup card shape](setup-card-two-part-shape.md) — words above a rule, facts below; not implemented.\n- [Model pickers](composer-model-pickers.md) — per-chat provider/model/thinking; partly live-tested.\n- [WebKit click](webkit-click-does-not-focus-buttons.md) — no focus on click; blur menus lose clicks.\n- [All settings panel](all-settings-panel.md) — four decisions, settings_catalog, selection trap.\n- [ModelVolume copy](modelvolume-copy-keeps-object-id.md) — keeps ObjectID, breaks undo; use a new mesh.\n- [Add-printer form](add-printer-popup-feasibility.md) — merged f073fdba96; decisions, tests, Haiku runs.\n- [Turn activity](agent-turn-activity-proposal.md) — one TurnActivity line per turn, not 17 cards.\n- [Catalogue cost](printer-catalog-load-cost.md) — ~0.95 s per launch; panel opens ~50 ms.\n- [Calibration design](calibration-design-decisions.md) — own project, temp/flow/PA first.\n- [Artifact watch](artifact-watch-crosstalk.md) — publish arms auto-replies; stop it with two sessions.\n- [Saved API key](api-key-saved-state.md) — saved_keys, hint rule; \"rejected\" = a chat 401.\n- [Live host check](live-host-check-via-instrumented-dev-page.md) — JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL + injected logger.\n- [Shared Mac builds](pkill-cmake-build-leaves-ninja.md) — one at a time, -j4; pkill orphans ninja.; [Running ninja](check-for-running-ninja-before-nohup-build.md) — pgrep first; kill yours at turn end.; [Ninja bad record](ninja-deps-bad-record-repeat-rebuild.md) — ~780 recompiles; `ninja -t recompact`.\n- [Check print design](check-print-design-decisions.md) — slice_report panel; Legend + Moves toggles.; [Check print built](check-print-implementation.md) — ImGui display-size fix; harness --check-print.\n- [Tool errors](tool-error-contract.md) — one list in Agent/ToolErrors.hpp; busy fails.\n- [Canvas boards](canvas-boards-from-bundle-rules.md) — from bundle.css + app markup, not older boards.\n- [Calibration generators](calibration-generators-replace-project.md) — calib_* swap the project identity.\n- [Setup one flow](agent-setup-one-flow-decisions.md) — Preferences › Agent for every entry point.\n- [cmake edit rebuild](cmake-file-edit-forces-full-rebuild.md) — new file changes GIT_COMMIT_HASH everywhere.\n- [JusPrin Cloud](jusprin-cloud-provider.md) — live 2026-10-25, obi.4048; release + smoke recipe.\n- [Named platform](test-the-platform-kenneth-names.md) — \"skip Windows\" = stop Windows work, test the Mac.\n- [No \"arrive\"](no-arrive-jargon-for-files.md) — opened/imported/loaded/added; sweep by word stem.\n- [Auto slicing reverted](auto-slice-reverted.md) — a full slice that locked the header.\n- [Send via Orca](send-via-orca-dialog.md) — agent opens the dialog, never presses Send.\n- [Classic view return](classic-view-return-decisions.md) — banner + View-menu row, session-only.\n- [Print history](print-history-screen-design.md) — one record per G-code; no failure state; not built.\n- [UX walkthrough](ux-walkthrough-real-app-recipe.md) — scratch .app + datadir, full control for dialogs.\n- [File-printer switch](file-printer-switch-decisions.md) — Option 2: chip marked \"from the file\".\n- [Open a file](open-file-in-app-without-screen-control.md) — osascript by bundle path, not Finder.\n- [Show design in screen](show-design-in-the-screen.md) — boards are whole screens, not lone components.\n- [Chip statement](chip-states-selection-not-machine.md) — states selection, not the machine; four tests.\n- [Setup-changed entry](setup-changed-entry-point.md) — A+C+D; Check plan link, \"changed by hand\".\n- [Hidden pane](hidden-browser-pane-no-raf.md) — 0 rAF frames; use Playwright.\n- [Chat cost](per-chat-cost-estimate.md) — Opus 5.5 measured $0.30-0.56 per chat.\n- [Chat capture](jusprin-chat-capture-design.md) — every chat kept raw, no opt-out, no branches; vendor terms open.\n- [Pricing corrections](pricing-brainstorm-corrections.md) — low usage = low stickiness; Obico ~5%, ~77%.\n- [Live suite](live-suite-is-part-of-done.md) — model-text changes need it before merge.\n- [No forcing field](no-required-field-to-force-a-question.md) — when to ask belongs in the prompt.\n- [Rebuild a request](rebuild-wire-request-from-saved-chat.md) — from current-state.json + source.\n- [Connection skill](connection-skill-per-connection-type.md) — 2026-11-02 Kenneth's pick: one skill per connection type, added at connect time, honest tool states, PRs + opt-in reports.; [Skill explains](connection-skill-explains-not-lookup.md) — judge by guiding a stuck person; no state-to-step table, no patching one line.\n- [P1S incident](p1s-connect-incident-2026-10-31.md) — Kenneth's P1S in cloud mode; log path, timeline.\n- [Code -1](bambu-code-minus-one-not-wrong-code.md) — also with the right code on a slow network, and with no device there; MQTT login tells codes apart.\n- [Printer network harness](printer-network-check-harness.md) — not on MCP; real plug-in, no model.\n- [Reproduce for real](reproduce-on-real-app-not-fakes.md) — a failing fake test is no repro.\n- [Chat keeps its model](chat-keeps-its-model.md) — for now no mid-chat switch; docs and app still differ.\n- [Usage against quota](usage-against-quota-common-shape.md) — real screens of several products first; a bar per kind of credit, bought too.\n- [Get more credits](one-action-to-get-more-credits.md) — one action to a page that explains; no Buy vs Subscribe guess.\n- [v1 subscribers](v1-subscribers-grandfathered.md) — Hobby at their original price, not Workshop until term end; plan differs.\n- [\"1 credit\"](credit-price-needs-its-unit.md) — confusing alone; \"1 credit a message\".\n- [One kind of credit](credits-one-kind-no-ceiling.md) — 2026-11-02 evening: no Standard-only lot, no Workshop ceiling, credits only, bars by expiry, no New Standard chat.\n- [Show the board](show-the-board-when-asking-kenneth.md) — no bare \"6a\": say what the person sees, where it is, send the PNG.\n- [Credits only](balances-in-credits-only.md) — no message counts on a balance; every credit pays either tier; Workshop Standard costs 0; 50 free a month after the first month for accounts without a plan, pack holders too; lots expire a month from the grant.\n- [Board PNGs](render-canvas-boards-with-render-dc.md) — render_dc.py draws dc-imports; render.py leaves them blank.\n- [Sign-up reason](sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent.md) — the offer is the headline; the button names the reward.\n- [Print report placement](print-report-lives-on-history-entry.md) — on the history entry, not in chat; boards 8a-8d.\n- [Credits boards](credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages.md) — on their flows' canvas pages; LAYOUT table in the builder.\n- [AppConfig set trap](appconfig-set-const-char-goes-to-bool.md) — a const char* goes to the bool overload and saves \"true\".\n- [Signed-in real app](real-app-signed-in-without-screen-control.md) — conf keys, seeded printer, copied-binary kill, racing a 402.\n- [Live checks locally](live-checks-can-run-on-local-gateway.md) — blocked on staging? run the local gateway on real keys; send screenshots.\n- [Standard titles](standard-title-answers-instead.md) — 4 of 12 refused, the model answers instead; null default_effort crashes the app.\n- Retired, Figma gone 2026-10-20: [file](figma-jusprin-v2-file.md), [seats](figma-mcp-view-seat-limit.md), [add printer](add-printer-flow-figma-discrepancy.md)\n- Retired: [in-file agent](drive-figma-in-file-agent-via-chrome.md), [parity](figma-dump-then-measure-parity.md), [header values, superseded](header-menu-values-kenneth-kept.md)\n- [Blank project behind Home](blank-project-behind-home-inherited.md) — inherited; Kenneth's rule: save only with a model or if already saved, chats don't count.\n- [Printer suite traps](printer-suite-traps-usage-and-skill-rev.md) — no token log; --prompt-rev skips the skill; ~23k tokens a conversation.\n- [First-run boards](first-run-flow-boards.md) — variants A and B replacing the wizard, unruled; only A needs an anonymous token; the assumed printer needs a stored origin.\n- [First-run proposition](first-run-value-prop-decisions.md) — 2026-11-02: expert help, not simpler slicing; title \"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\"; split welcome, clip left, one primary + three free doors; 12 s stringing-Benchy clip with clean-boat ending; quick renders, no design session.\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): build-the-first-launch-c = local_dbced2fd-a752-4429-a46c-4f4bf4c6a8df (idle); find-a-cc-photo-of-a-rec = local_f72d2b0a-d628-44d2-acab-585b51e28763 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c\" from-name=\"JusPrin pricing goals and priorities\">\nKenneth asks you to revert the no-wizard first-run boards you published (variants A and B) and build the first-run design he has since decided, described in full below.\n\nHis words: \"tell the design agents to revert the work it did for the no wizard first run flow, and build what we just discussed here.\"\n\n1. Revert. Take the first-run-a-* and first-run-b-* boards off the \"On boarding experience\" page of the JusPrin v2 canvas and restore anything on that page you moved or edited to make room for them, so the page is as it was before your variants, plus the new boards below. Keep the builder script, but its page section for A/B goes. Do not touch other pages.\n\n2. What is decided (all on 2026-11-02, by Kenneth, from rendered comparisons; the reference renders are listed at the end):\n\n- Proposition: expert help with a failed print, now, from an AI that can see the person's file, settings and slice and fixes the settings, instead of waiting for a forum reply. Not \"simpler slicing\".\n- No wizard. One welcome screen on first launch, split: a looping silent clip on the LEFT, the words and doors on the RIGHT. Under about 30 words outside the clip.\n- Title: \"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\" (page-title). Subtitle (body, secondary): \"Show it a photo of what went wrong. The agent reads your file, your settings and your slice, changes the settings and slices again.\"\n- A label line directly above the doors: \"Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.\"\n- Doors, weighting \"one primary\": a selected card \"Your first month: 500 credits\" / \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Then paid, or your own key.\" / primary button \"Sign in for 500 credits\"; then two equal slim rows \"Your own API key\" with cost \"Free\" and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop\" with cost \"Free · MCP server\"; then the link \"Just slice for now\". Every free door shows its cost; nothing hidden. Never \"trial\", no dollar figure. Footer: \"Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.\"\n- The clip, about 12 s, silent, looping, four beats with one caption each: \"Show it what happened.\" / \"It reads your photo, your file and your slice.\" / \"It changes the settings for you.\" / \"And slices again. Tonight.\" Beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside a real photo of a stringing blue-and-white Benchy and the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" Beat 2: a short burst of agent text. Beat 3: two big before→after settings, \"Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm\" and \"Nozzle 220 → 200 °C\". Beat 4: a bar labelled \"Slicing NN%\" counting up; at 100 % the stringy thumbnail fades to a clean print of the same boat, a green check pops, and \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\". Motion only at beat changes, short holds, last frame held longest.\n- After the doors, nothing new is decided: each setup door opens Preferences › Agent as the 2026-10-23 one-flow decision says, and \"Just slice for now\" goes to Home with the printer order Kenneth decided earlier (3MF preset, else OrcaSlicer import, else a default the chip marks as assumed). Reuse your existing after-door boards only where they already match that; where they don't, leave them out and list the gap in your note rather than inventing a screen.\n\n3. Boards to publish on that page, as whole screens at the app's size, built from the token file through the usual recipes (no literals): the welcome screen with the clip at beat 1; the welcome screen with the clip at the final frame (the one peripheral vision sees most); and one storyboard board of the four clip beats with their captions. Strings are exactly the ones above; the agent's words in beat 2 are placeholders until a live run and the board should say so in a small note.\n\n4. Reference renders, all untracked under /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/: tagline/ai-a-ai-slicer.png (the welcome with the chosen title, clip at beat 1), animatic/welcome-stringing.png (the composite with the live clip), animatic/beats/stringing-beat-{1,2,3,4a,4}-*.png (the beat stills), animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4 (the clip), photo/benchy-stringing.jpg and photo/benchy-clean.jpg with photo/ATTRIBUTION.md (CC BY 2.0; the credit must appear somewhere, so put a small credit line on the storyboard board). The decision record is in memory at ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md. Update your note first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md at the repo root to say A/B are withdrawn and what replaced them; keep it untracked, commit nothing.\n\nWhen done, report the canvas version, the board names, and anything you left out, and send a PNG of the welcome board with SendUserFile.\n</cross-session-message>"}]}}
