ps -g pixelWidth -g pixelHeight photo/*.jpg tagline/ai-a-ai-slicer.png animatic/welcome-stringing.png 2>/dev/null | grep -v '^$'","description":"Read Kenneth's decision record and list the reference renders and photo credit"}},"apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgfJW4PvG87LRsVGvNEkd","requestRef":"398f1963-ef33-4965-a9d4-e77c3374de56","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d0744783-b7b8-48a9-af62-80ae0afac73b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:42:23.533Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"d0744783-b7b8-48a9-af62-80ae0afac73b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3302b766-bcdc-47a6-990a-3c389fab5338","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011SxnDqAQCpQHntYLJRQQbK","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: first-run-value-prop-decisions\ndescription: \"Kenneth's 2026-11-02 decisions on the first launch: the proposition is expert help with a failed print (not simpler slicing); title \\\"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\\\"; one split welcome screen, clip left, one primary door over three equal free doors; a 12 s four-beat clip on a stringing Benchy with a clean-boat ending; the wizard is dropped; quick renders beat a design session.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34\n  modified: 2026-11-03T00:07:16.607Z\n---\n\nDecided 2026-11-02 (late), in the session that critiqued the onboarding wizard against the pricing goals.\n\n- **Proposition:** expert help with a printing problem, now, from an agent that can see the person's file, settings and slice and fixes the settings, instead of waiting for a forum reply. Kenneth: \"I feel more strongly about expert help too.\" \"Simpler slicing\" was the other candidate; it is what keeps people, not what brings them.\n- **First launch:** one welcome screen, no wizard, split: the clip on the left, the headline and doors on the right.\n- **Title, chosen 2026-11-02 late evening (\"ok go with a\"):** \"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\" Kenneth's brief: the title must be short and say what JusPrin is for, and it must say AI; the earlier \"Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.\" lost because it named neither the slicer nor the AI. Subtitle for patient readers: \"Show it a photo of what went wrong. The agent reads your file, your settings and your slice, changes the settings and slices again.\" The line \"Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.\" sits as a label directly above the doors. The runner-up was F, \"Slice with AI. Fix failed prints tonight.\", the only one carrying the no-waiting comparison.\n- **Doors, Kenneth's pick \"One primary\":** the first-month offer card with \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on top, then two equal slim rows, \"Your own API key · Free\" and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop · Free · MCP server\", then \"Just slice for now\" as a link. Every free door shows its cost; nothing is hidden. Kenneth's worry was feeling pushed to the cloud; the answer is honest cost lines and the reversibility line, not equal pixel size.\n- **The clip:** about 12 s (Kenneth cut it from 25: \"nobody has the patience to wait for it to finish\"), silent, looping. Four beats, one caption each: \"Show it what happened.\" / \"It reads your photo, your file and your slice.\" / \"It changes the settings for you.\" / \"And slices again. Tonight.\" Motion only at beat changes, short holds, last frame longest. The failed print is a real CC BY 2.0 photo of a stringing blue-and-white 3DBenchy (Flickr 19273965123, #3DBenchy account; chosen over a peeled black hull because the strings are failure and cause in one picture); beat 1 shows the intact boat on the plate beside it; beat 3 shows two big settings, Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm and Nozzle 220 → 200 °C; beat 4 is a bar labelled \"Slicing NN%\" that, at 100 %, fades the stringy thumbnail to a clean print of the same boat (Flickr 19239738473, CC BY 2.0), then a green check and \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\". No confetti, no time-lapse. The agent's words and the setting values are placeholders until a live run is recorded for this photo; the shipped clip is a recording of the real app. Photos, crops and credit text: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/ATTRIBUTION.md` (CC BY needs a visible credit somewhere in the app).\n- **Wall of text:** under about 30 words outside the clip. The transcript panel that duplicated the clip was the failure.\n- **Method:** Kenneth stopped the design session (\"a lot more effective if we explore this way\"): render a few 1280×800 screens from the app's tokens with headless Chrome, send PNGs, iterate. Renders, clips and generators: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked: `tagline/`, `animatic/`, `photo/`) and the session scratchpads `vp/build*.py`, `tag/build4.py`, `tag/build5.py`.\n\n**Why:** the wizard asked for commitment before showing value; the proposition decides the headline, the proof and the door order, so it had to be settled first.\n\n**How to apply:** the canvas boards from [[first-run-flow-boards]] (variants A and B) predate these decisions; variant B's welcome is the nearer one but its headline, weighting and proof must follow this note. Say \"AI\" to a first-time visitor and introduce \"the agent\" in the subtitle; keep \"Agent\" explained, never \"trial\", no dollar figure on the offer. Related: [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]], [[show-the-board-when-asking-kenneth]], [[mockup-strings-from-real-output]].\n./animatic/animatic-stringing.gif\n./animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-1-show-it.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-2-it-reads.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-3-it-changes.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-4-slices-again.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-4a-slicing.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-all-beats.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-1.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-2.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-3.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-4.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-4a.png\n./animatic/src/animatic.html\n./animatic/src/benchy-model.png\n./animatic/src/benchy-sliced.png\n./animatic/src/check-words.py\n./animatic/src/composite.py\n./animatic/src/fonts/HarmonyOS_Sans_SC_Bold_latin.woff\n./animatic/src/fonts/HarmonyOS_Sans_SC_Regular_latin.woff\n./animatic/src/photo-clean.jpg\n./animatic/src/photo-stringing.jpg\n./animatic/src/photo-thick.jpg\n./animatic/src/render_benchy.py\n./animatic/src/shoot.js\n./animatic/src/shoot2.js\n./animatic/src/strings.js\n./animatic/src/tokens.css\n./animatic/src/vp8/build.py\n./animatic/src/vp8/build2.py\n./animatic/src/vp8/build3.py\n./animatic/src/vp8/home-src.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-1.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-2.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-3.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-4.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-4a.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-stringing.html\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/animatic-too-thick-layers.gif\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/animatic-too-thick-layers.mp4\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-1-show-it.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-2-it-reads.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-3-it-changes.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-4-slices-again.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-all-beats.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-1.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-2.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-3.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-4.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/welcome-too-thick-layers.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-1-show-it.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-2-it-reads.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-3-it-changes.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-4-slices-again.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/first-launch-clip-animatic.gif\n./animatic/superseded-vase/first-launch-clip-animatic.mp4\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-all-beats.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-beat-1.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-beat-2.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-beat-3.png\n# Attribution for the Benchy photos\n\nAll three photos are from the #3DBenchy account on Flickr and are licensed CC BY 2.0, which allows commercial use and changes as long as the credit below is shown and changes are stated. They were downloaded on 2026-11-02 at their original size with Kenneth's approval: two failed prints, and one clean print used as the \"after\". This folder is untracked and is never committed.\n\n## benchy-too-thick-layers-original.jpg\n\n- **Title:** \"#3DBency made with too thick layers - 3DBenchy.com\" (the misspelling \"3DBency\" is in the author's title)\n- **Author:** #3DBenchy (Flickr account `3dbenchy`)\n- **Source:** https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/20146074666/\n- **Downloaded from:** https://live.staticflickr.com/390/20146074666_011f518736_o.jpg (734,956 bytes as served)\n- **Also on Wikimedia Commons:** https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:-3DBency_made_with_too_thick_layers_-_3DBenchy.com_(20146074666).jpg, where Commons' licence-review bot recorded CC BY 2.0 on 2025-02-16\n- **Licence:** CC BY 2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\n- **Changes made to this file:** GPS metadata removed. The image pixels are unchanged, and the file is now 734,706 bytes.\n- **Edited copy for use:** `benchy-too-thick-layers.jpg`, 3200×2250. The red caption in the top left is painted out by filling it from the surrounding out-of-focus background (no other pixels touched), and the bottom 118 px with the grey \"3DBenchy.com\" band are cropped off. Metadata is not carried over. The script is `edit_photos.py` in the animatic session's scratchpad; its logic is described here because the scratchpad is temporary.\n- **Credit text:** \"#3DBency made with too thick layers\" by #3DBenchy, https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/20146074666/, CC BY 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/). Caption removed and cropped.\n\n## benchy-stringing-original.jpg\n\n- **Title:** \"Dual extrusion 3D printed #3DBenchy v01\"\n- **Author:** #3DBenchy (Flickr account `3dbenchy`)\n- **Source:** https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19273965123/\n- **Downloaded from:** https://live.staticflickr.com/411/19273965123_281ccf5382_o.jpg (1,908,208 bytes as served)\n- **Also on Wikimedia Commons:** https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dual_extrusion_3D_printed_-3DBenchy_v01_(19273965123).jpg, where Commons' licence-review bot recorded CC BY 2.0 on 2025-02-16\n- **Licence:** CC BY 2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\n- **Changes made to this file:** GPS metadata removed. The image pixels are unchanged, and the file is now 1,907,958 bytes.\n- **Edited copy for use:** `benchy-stringing.jpg`, 3200×2240. The bottom 128 px (5.4%) with the white overlay text \"#3DBenchy - Dual extrusion - 3DBenchy.com\" are cropped off, which also trims the tips of some strings below the hull. No other change. Metadata is not carried over.\n- **Credit text:** \"Dual extrusion 3D printed #3DBenchy v01\" by #3DBenchy, https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19273965123/, CC BY 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/). Cropped.\n\n## benchy-clean-original.jpg\n\n- **Title:** \"Dual-print multi-part color 3D print of #3DBenchy v13\"\n- **Author:** #3DBenchy (Flickr account `3dbenchy`)\n- **Source:** https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19239738473/\n- **Downloaded from:** https://live.staticflickr.com/3746/19239738473_a887a15ae6_o.jpg (1,672,390 bytes as served, 4608×2592)\n- **Also on Wikimedia Commons:** no. Commons has no copy of this photo, so the licence comes from the Flickr page alone.\n- **Licence:** CC BY 2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\n- **Changes made to this file:** none. It had no GPS metadata to remove, so the file is byte-for-byte as served, 1,672,390 bytes. Its metadata holds the camera (Samsung EK-GC100), the capture time, and the camera's software version.\n- **Edited copy for use:** `benchy-clean.jpg`, 3200×2240. Cropped to the region x 829–4086, y 200–2480 of the original (3257×2280, the same aspect as `benchy-stringing.jpg`), then scaled down 1.8% to exactly 3200×2240 so it lines up with the stringing photo in a crossfade. The crop frames the boat the way the stringing photo frames its boat, and it removes the small \"#3DBenchy - 3DBenchy.com\" text along the bottom edge (it starts at y 2548). No other change. Metadata is not carried over.\n- **Credit text:** \"Dual-print multi-part color 3D print of #3DBenchy v13\" by #3DBenchy, https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19239738473/, CC BY 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/). Cropped and resized.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Update the \"Changes made\" line and the credit text of each photo if the file that ships is edited differently from what is described here.\n- The licence was read from each Flickr page and from Commons' bot review. That confirms what Flickr showed. It does not confirm who took the photo.\n- What remains in the metadata of the two failed-print originals: the camera make and model (LGE Nexus 5), the capture time, and an XMP tag that names the phone's HDR+ software. None of these identify a place. The edited copies carry no metadata.\n- The model shown is 3DBenchy, licensed CC0 (https://www.3dbenchy.com/license/), and the app already has it at `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc`.\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-clean-original.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 4608\n  pixelHeight: 2592\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-clean.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2240\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-stringing-original.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2368\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-stringing.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2240\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-too-thick-layers-original.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2368\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-too-thick-layers.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2250\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/tagline/ai-a-ai-slicer.png\n  pixelWidth: 2560\n  pixelHeight: 1600\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/welcome-stringing.png\n  pixelWidth: 2560\n  pixelHeight: 1600","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"80e830f8-c057-42d7-8950-e3dc267d9e4d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:42:27.874Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: first-run-value-prop-decisions\ndescription: \"Kenneth's 2026-11-02 decisions on the first launch: the proposition is expert help with a failed print (not simpler slicing); title \\\"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\\\"; one split welcome screen, clip left, one primary door over three equal free doors; a 12 s four-beat clip on a stringing Benchy with a clean-boat ending; the wizard is dropped; quick renders beat a design session.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: e997298c-6edf-4c7d-8994-08bc7e301a34\n  modified: 2026-11-03T00:07:16.607Z\n---\n\nDecided 2026-11-02 (late), in the session that critiqued the onboarding wizard against the pricing goals.\n\n- **Proposition:** expert help with a printing problem, now, from an agent that can see the person's file, settings and slice and fixes the settings, instead of waiting for a forum reply. Kenneth: \"I feel more strongly about expert help too.\" \"Simpler slicing\" was the other candidate; it is what keeps people, not what brings them.\n- **First launch:** one welcome screen, no wizard, split: the clip on the left, the headline and doors on the right.\n- **Title, chosen 2026-11-02 late evening (\"ok go with a\"):** \"The AI slicer that fixes failed prints.\" Kenneth's brief: the title must be short and say what JusPrin is for, and it must say AI; the earlier \"Your print failed. Ask someone who can see why.\" lost because it named neither the slicer nor the AI. Subtitle for patient readers: \"Show it a photo of what went wrong. The agent reads your file, your settings and your slice, changes the settings and slices again.\" The line \"Pick how the agent should think. Change it any time in Preferences › Agent.\" sits as a label directly above the doors. The runner-up was F, \"Slice with AI. Fix failed prints tonight.\", the only one carrying the no-waiting comparison.\n- **Doors, Kenneth's pick \"One primary\":** the first-month offer card with \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on top, then two equal slim rows, \"Your own API key · Free\" and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop · Free · MCP server\", then \"Just slice for now\" as a link. Every free door shows its cost; nothing is hidden. Kenneth's worry was feeling pushed to the cloud; the answer is honest cost lines and the reversibility line, not equal pixel size.\n- **The clip:** about 12 s (Kenneth cut it from 25: \"nobody has the patience to wait for it to finish\"), silent, looping. Four beats, one caption each: \"Show it what happened.\" / \"It reads your photo, your file and your slice.\" / \"It changes the settings for you.\" / \"And slices again. Tonight.\" Motion only at beat changes, short holds, last frame longest. The failed print is a real CC BY 2.0 photo of a stringing blue-and-white 3DBenchy (Flickr 19273965123, #3DBenchy account; chosen over a peeled black hull because the strings are failure and cause in one picture); beat 1 shows the intact boat on the plate beside it; beat 3 shows two big settings, Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm and Nozzle 220 → 200 °C; beat 4 is a bar labelled \"Slicing NN%\" that, at 100 %, fades the stringy thumbnail to a clean print of the same boat (Flickr 19239738473, CC BY 2.0), then a green check and \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\". No confetti, no time-lapse. The agent's words and the setting values are placeholders until a live run is recorded for this photo; the shipped clip is a recording of the real app. Photos, crops and credit text: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/ATTRIBUTION.md` (CC BY needs a visible credit somewhere in the app).\n- **Wall of text:** under about 30 words outside the clip. The transcript panel that duplicated the clip was the failure.\n- **Method:** Kenneth stopped the design session (\"a lot more effective if we explore this way\"): render a few 1280×800 screens from the app's tokens with headless Chrome, send PNGs, iterate. Renders, clips and generators: `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked: `tagline/`, `animatic/`, `photo/`) and the session scratchpads `vp/build*.py`, `tag/build4.py`, `tag/build5.py`.\n\n**Why:** the wizard asked for commitment before showing value; the proposition decides the headline, the proof and the door order, so it had to be settled first.\n\n**How to apply:** the canvas boards from [[first-run-flow-boards]] (variants A and B) predate these decisions; variant B's welcome is the nearer one but its headline, weighting and proof must follow this note. Say \"AI\" to a first-time visitor and introduce \"the agent\" in the subtitle; keep \"Agent\" explained, never \"trial\", no dollar figure on the offer. Related: [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]], [[show-the-board-when-asking-kenneth]], [[mockup-strings-from-real-output]].\n./animatic/animatic-stringing.gif\n./animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-1-show-it.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-2-it-reads.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-3-it-changes.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-4-slices-again.png\n./animatic/beats/stringing-beat-4a-slicing.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-all-beats.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-1.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-2.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-3.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-4.png\n./animatic/peripheral/stringing-half-beat-4a.png\n./animatic/src/animatic.html\n./animatic/src/benchy-model.png\n./animatic/src/benchy-sliced.png\n./animatic/src/check-words.py\n./animatic/src/composite.py\n./animatic/src/fonts/HarmonyOS_Sans_SC_Bold_latin.woff\n./animatic/src/fonts/HarmonyOS_Sans_SC_Regular_latin.woff\n./animatic/src/photo-clean.jpg\n./animatic/src/photo-stringing.jpg\n./animatic/src/photo-thick.jpg\n./animatic/src/render_benchy.py\n./animatic/src/shoot.js\n./animatic/src/shoot2.js\n./animatic/src/strings.js\n./animatic/src/tokens.css\n./animatic/src/vp8/build.py\n./animatic/src/vp8/build2.py\n./animatic/src/vp8/build3.py\n./animatic/src/vp8/home-src.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-1.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-2.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-3.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-4.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-half-stringing-4a.html\n./animatic/src/welcome-stringing.html\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/animatic-too-thick-layers.gif\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/animatic-too-thick-layers.mp4\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-1-show-it.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-2-it-reads.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-3-it-changes.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/beats/too-thick-layers-beat-4-slices-again.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-all-beats.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-1.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-2.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-3.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/peripheral/too-thick-layers-half-beat-4.png\n./animatic/superseded-too-thick-layers/welcome-too-thick-layers.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-1-show-it.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-2-it-reads.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-3-it-changes.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/beats/beat-4-slices-again.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/first-launch-clip-animatic.gif\n./animatic/superseded-vase/first-launch-clip-animatic.mp4\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-all-beats.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-beat-1.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-beat-2.png\n./animatic/superseded-vase/peripheral/half-beat-3.png\n# Attribution for the Benchy photos\n\nAll three photos are from the #3DBenchy account on Flickr and are licensed CC BY 2.0, which allows commercial use and changes as long as the credit below is shown and changes are stated. They were downloaded on 2026-11-02 at their original size with Kenneth's approval: two failed prints, and one clean print used as the \"after\". This folder is untracked and is never committed.\n\n## benchy-too-thick-layers-original.jpg\n\n- **Title:** \"#3DBency made with too thick layers - 3DBenchy.com\" (the misspelling \"3DBency\" is in the author's title)\n- **Author:** #3DBenchy (Flickr account `3dbenchy`)\n- **Source:** https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/20146074666/\n- **Downloaded from:** https://live.staticflickr.com/390/20146074666_011f518736_o.jpg (734,956 bytes as served)\n- **Also on Wikimedia Commons:** https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:-3DBency_made_with_too_thick_layers_-_3DBenchy.com_(20146074666).jpg, where Commons' licence-review bot recorded CC BY 2.0 on 2025-02-16\n- **Licence:** CC BY 2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\n- **Changes made to this file:** GPS metadata removed. The image pixels are unchanged, and the file is now 734,706 bytes.\n- **Edited copy for use:** `benchy-too-thick-layers.jpg`, 3200×2250. The red caption in the top left is painted out by filling it from the surrounding out-of-focus background (no other pixels touched), and the bottom 118 px with the grey \"3DBenchy.com\" band are cropped off. Metadata is not carried over. The script is `edit_photos.py` in the animatic session's scratchpad; its logic is described here because the scratchpad is temporary.\n- **Credit text:** \"#3DBency made with too thick layers\" by #3DBenchy, https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/20146074666/, CC BY 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/). Caption removed and cropped.\n\n## benchy-stringing-original.jpg\n\n- **Title:** \"Dual extrusion 3D printed #3DBenchy v01\"\n- **Author:** #3DBenchy (Flickr account `3dbenchy`)\n- **Source:** https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19273965123/\n- **Downloaded from:** https://live.staticflickr.com/411/19273965123_281ccf5382_o.jpg (1,908,208 bytes as served)\n- **Also on Wikimedia Commons:** https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dual_extrusion_3D_printed_-3DBenchy_v01_(19273965123).jpg, where Commons' licence-review bot recorded CC BY 2.0 on 2025-02-16\n- **Licence:** CC BY 2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\n- **Changes made to this file:** GPS metadata removed. The image pixels are unchanged, and the file is now 1,907,958 bytes.\n- **Edited copy for use:** `benchy-stringing.jpg`, 3200×2240. The bottom 128 px (5.4%) with the white overlay text \"#3DBenchy - Dual extrusion - 3DBenchy.com\" are cropped off, which also trims the tips of some strings below the hull. No other change. Metadata is not carried over.\n- **Credit text:** \"Dual extrusion 3D printed #3DBenchy v01\" by #3DBenchy, https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19273965123/, CC BY 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/). Cropped.\n\n## benchy-clean-original.jpg\n\n- **Title:** \"Dual-print multi-part color 3D print of #3DBenchy v13\"\n- **Author:** #3DBenchy (Flickr account `3dbenchy`)\n- **Source:** https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19239738473/\n- **Downloaded from:** https://live.staticflickr.com/3746/19239738473_a887a15ae6_o.jpg (1,672,390 bytes as served, 4608×2592)\n- **Also on Wikimedia Commons:** no. Commons has no copy of this photo, so the licence comes from the Flickr page alone.\n- **Licence:** CC BY 2.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/\n- **Changes made to this file:** none. It had no GPS metadata to remove, so the file is byte-for-byte as served, 1,672,390 bytes. Its metadata holds the camera (Samsung EK-GC100), the capture time, and the camera's software version.\n- **Edited copy for use:** `benchy-clean.jpg`, 3200×2240. Cropped to the region x 829–4086, y 200–2480 of the original (3257×2280, the same aspect as `benchy-stringing.jpg`), then scaled down 1.8% to exactly 3200×2240 so it lines up with the stringing photo in a crossfade. The crop frames the boat the way the stringing photo frames its boat, and it removes the small \"#3DBenchy - 3DBenchy.com\" text along the bottom edge (it starts at y 2548). No other change. Metadata is not carried over.\n- **Credit text:** \"Dual-print multi-part color 3D print of #3DBenchy v13\" by #3DBenchy, https://www.flickr.com/photos/3dbenchy/19239738473/, CC BY 2.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0/). Cropped and resized.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Update the \"Changes made\" line and the credit text of each photo if the file that ships is edited differently from what is described here.\n- The licence was read from each Flickr page and from Commons' bot review. That confirms what Flickr showed. It does not confirm who took the photo.\n- What remains in the metadata of the two failed-print originals: the camera make and model (LGE Nexus 5), the capture time, and an XMP tag that names the phone's HDR+ software. None of these identify a place. The edited copies carry no metadata.\n- The model shown is 3DBenchy, licensed CC0 (https://www.3dbenchy.com/license/), and the app already has it at `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc`.\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-clean-original.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 4608\n  pixelHeight: 2592\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-clean.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2240\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-stringing-original.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2368\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-stringing.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2240\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-too-thick-layers-original.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2368\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/photo/benchy-too-thick-layers.jpg\n  pixelWidth: 3200\n  pixelHeight: 2250\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/tagline/ai-a-ai-slicer.png\n  pixelWidth: 2560\n  pixelHeight: 1600\n/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/welcome-stringing.png\n  pixelWidth: 2560\n  pixelHeight: 1600","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d0744783-b7b8-48a9-af62-80ae0afac73b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
