{"parentUuid":"979e0ce2-10fb-42d4-ab1e-32a5d83f8be1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfJyVjAp9wEzWpwEdmrG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":337430,"output_tokens":3378,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":110},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3378,"cache_read_input_tokens":337430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1209,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgfJyVSoJJ4nmtmdW9quB","requestRef":"60a7138a-3016-4e16-9b00-eeb2afa5cc89","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f64556e-7169-49a3-8ec1-e86c27007578","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:11.677Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"3f64556e-7169-49a3-8ec1-e86c27007578","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfJyVjAp9wEzWpwEdmrG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WqAWEDidoEJmVwu91mXY5K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md","content":"# First launch: one welcome screen, 2026-11-02\n\nThe two no-wizard first-run variants (A: no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn and a sign-in prompt on Send; B: a welcome screen with three equal doors) are withdrawn. On 2026-11-02 Kenneth chose a different first launch from rendered comparisons: one split welcome screen with a looping clip on the left and the words and doors on the right, built around expert help with a failed print. That screen is now on the JusPrin v2 canvas. No code has changed, and nothing here is committed.\n\nThe decision record is the memory note `first-run-value-prop-decisions.md`. The reference renders it was chosen from are in `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked).\n\n## What is on the canvas now\n\nThe JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 87 (`1793677670-03be`):\n\n| Board | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1` | The welcome screen with the clip at beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside the photo of the stringing Benchy, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\" On the right are the title, the subtitle, the line above the doors, the first-month offer as the one primary door, the two free rows with their costs, \"Just slice for now\", and the footer. |\n| `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame` | The same screen with the clip's final frame: the clean boat in the thumbnail, a green check, \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\", and the sliced boat on the plate. |\n| `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard` | The four beats with their captions and timings, a note on which parts are placeholders, and the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. Beat 4 is shown with the bar at 68 %, since the final frame is on 02. |\n\nTwo canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nEvery string comes from Kenneth's choice or the animatic's `strings.js`. Colours, radii, type and spacing come from the token file, and the boards contain no colour literals.\n\n## How the revert was done\n\nMy variants touched only their own entries on the page. I compared the index saved before my first publish (version `1793658772-45ce`) with the live one: apart from the 24 `first-run-a-*` and `first-run-b-*` boards and their 4 notes, every board, note and page entry was identical. Version 87 removes exactly those and adds the three welcome boards and two notes. The builder, `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`, now draws only the welcome boards. A copy of the A/B version is in this session's scratchpad.\n\nThe images I uploaded for the variants stay in the canvas's asset store, unreferenced: the plate captures, and the empty-plate capture made for the withdrawn headline change. I did not delete them, because deleting assets needs Kenneth to confirm each one.\n\n## What is placeholder\n\n- The agent's words in beat 2 are the opening of a real reply about a different print, the vase in journey `j3-opus-photo`. They stay until a live run on this photo is recorded.\n- The two settings in beat 3 (Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm, Nozzle 220 → 200 °C) are textbook fixes for stringing, not agent output.\n- The boats on the plate are the animatic's renders of the bundled 3DBenchy, standing in for the app's own view. The clip that ships is meant to be a recording of the real app.\n- The header shows \"JusPrin › Agent\" and \"Agent not connected\", copied from the reference render. Whether the welcome screen sits under the Agent crumb was not part of the decision.\n\n## What I left out, and the gaps\n\n- **Display type size.** The reference animatic drew the two settings, the \"Slicing NN%\" line and the bar's label at 36 to 48 px. The type scale's largest token is page-title (24 px), so the boards use that, and the settings read smaller than in the reference. If Kenneth wants the reference size, the token file needs a display size first.\n- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.\n- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.\n- **The clip in motion.** The canvas holds still frames only. The moving reference is `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4`.\n\n## Findings from the variant work that still apply\n\nThese came from reading the code for the withdrawn variants and still matter for \"Just slice for now\" and the printer order Kenneth decided:\n\n- The \"from the file\" chip would mislabel an assumed default. The rule behind it (`printer_from_file`, which tests `!is_named_printer`) cannot tell the two cases apart, so the assumed mark needs a stored origin.\n- An empty data folder has no printers (`presets_list` returned 0), so the default printer has to be installed at first run. The A1 mini was only the example in Kenneth's sentence.\n- The project chat cannot add a printer. `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest belong to the printer conversation only.\n- Home has no agent pane: `ShellController.cpp:1913` keeps the pane collapsed on Home.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":337430,"output_tokens":3378,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":110},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3378,"cache_read_input_tokens":337430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WqAWEDidoEJmVwu91mXY5K":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md","content":"# First launch: one welcome screen, 2026-11-02\n\nThe two no-wizard first-run variants (A: no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn and a sign-in prompt on Send; B: a welcome screen with three equal doors) are withdrawn. On 2026-11-02 Kenneth chose a different first launch from rendered comparisons: one split welcome screen with a looping clip on the left and the words and doors on the right, built around expert help with a failed print. That screen is now on the JusPrin v2 canvas. No code has changed, and nothing here is committed.\n\nThe decision record is the memory note `first-run-value-prop-decisions.md`. The reference renders it was chosen from are in `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked).\n\n## What is on the canvas now\n\nThe JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 87 (`1793677670-03be`):\n\n| Board | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1` | The welcome screen with the clip at beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside the photo of the stringing Benchy, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\" On the right are the title, the subtitle, the line above the doors, the first-month offer as the one primary door, the two free rows with their costs, \"Just slice for now\", and the footer. |\n| `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame` | The same screen with the clip's final frame: the clean boat in the thumbnail, a green check, \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\", and the sliced boat on the plate. |\n| `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard` | The four beats with their captions and timings, a note on which parts are placeholders, and the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. Beat 4 is shown with the bar at 68 %, since the final frame is on 02. |\n\nTwo canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nEvery string comes from Kenneth's choice or the animatic's `strings.js`. Colours, radii, type and spacing come from the token file, and the boards contain no colour literals.\n\n## How the revert was done\n\nMy variants touched only their own entries on the page. I compared the index saved before my first publish (version `1793658772-45ce`) with the live one: apart from the 24 `first-run-a-*` and `first-run-b-*` boards and their 4 notes, every board, note and page entry was identical. Version 87 removes exactly those and adds the three welcome boards and two notes. The builder, `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`, now draws only the welcome boards. A copy of the A/B version is in this session's scratchpad.\n\nThe images I uploaded for the variants stay in the canvas's asset store, unreferenced: the plate captures, and the empty-plate capture made for the withdrawn headline change. I did not delete them, because deleting assets needs Kenneth to confirm each one.\n\n## What is placeholder\n\n- The agent's words in beat 2 are the opening of a real reply about a different print, the vase in journey `j3-opus-photo`. They stay until a live run on this photo is recorded.\n- The two settings in beat 3 (Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm, Nozzle 220 → 200 °C) are textbook fixes for stringing, not agent output.\n- The boats on the plate are the animatic's renders of the bundled 3DBenchy, standing in for the app's own view. The clip that ships is meant to be a recording of the real app.\n- The header shows \"JusPrin › Agent\" and \"Agent not connected\", copied from the reference render. Whether the welcome screen sits under the Agent crumb was not part of the decision.\n\n## What I left out, and the gaps\n\n- **Display type size.** The reference animatic drew the two settings, the \"Slicing NN%\" line and the bar's label at 36 to 48 px. The type scale's largest token is page-title (24 px), so the boards use that, and the settings read smaller than in the reference. If Kenneth wants the reference size, the token file needs a display size first.\n- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.\n- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.\n- **The clip in motion.** The canvas holds still frames only. The moving reference is `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4`.\n\n## Findings from the variant work that still apply\n\nThese came from reading the code for the withdrawn variants and still matter for \"Just slice for now\" and the printer order Kenneth decided:\n\n- The \"from the file\" chip would mislabel an assumed default. The rule behind it (`printer_from_file`, which tests `!is_named_printer`) cannot tell the two cases apart, so the assumed mark needs a stored origin.\n- An empty data folder has no printers (`presets_list` returned 0), so the default printer has to be installed at first run. The A1 mini was only the example in Kenneth's sentence.\n- The project chat cannot add a printer. `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest belong to the printer conversation only.\n- Home has no agent pane: `ShellController.cpp:1913` keeps the pane collapsed on Home.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgfJyVSoJJ4nmtmdW9quB","requestRef":"60a7138a-3016-4e16-9b00-eeb2afa5cc89","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8044edbb-11bc-4461-b9e6-b40f8dd0dc2b","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:31.236Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"8044edbb-11bc-4461-b9e6-b40f8dd0dc2b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3302b766-bcdc-47a6-990a-3c389fab5338","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WqAWEDidoEJmVwu91mXY5K","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e5e7be70-4135-4ef5-84ac-b5a2a3e936e2","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:31.275Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md","content":"# First launch: one welcome screen, 2026-11-02\n\nThe two no-wizard first-run variants (A: no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn and a sign-in prompt on Send; B: a welcome screen with three equal doors) are withdrawn. On 2026-11-02 Kenneth chose a different first launch from rendered comparisons: one split welcome screen with a looping clip on the left and the words and doors on the right, built around expert help with a failed print. That screen is now on the JusPrin v2 canvas. No code has changed, and nothing here is committed.\n\nThe decision record is the memory note `first-run-value-prop-decisions.md`. The reference renders it was chosen from are in `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked).\n\n## What is on the canvas now\n\nThe JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 87 (`1793677670-03be`):\n\n| Board | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1` | The welcome screen with the clip at beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside the photo of the stringing Benchy, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\" On the right are the title, the subtitle, the line above the doors, the first-month offer as the one primary door, the two free rows with their costs, \"Just slice for now\", and the footer. |\n| `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame` | The same screen with the clip's final frame: the clean boat in the thumbnail, a green check, \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\", and the sliced boat on the plate. |\n| `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard` | The four beats with their captions and timings, a note on which parts are placeholders, and the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. Beat 4 is shown with the bar at 68 %, since the final frame is on 02. |\n\nTwo canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nEvery string comes from Kenneth's choice or the animatic's `strings.js`. Colours, radii, type and spacing come from the token file, and the boards contain no colour literals.\n\n## How the revert was done\n\nMy variants touched only their own entries on the page. I compared the index saved before my first publish (version `1793658772-45ce`) with the live one: apart from the 24 `first-run-a-*` and `first-run-b-*` boards and their 4 notes, every board, note and page entry was identical. Version 87 removes exactly those and adds the three welcome boards and two notes. The builder, `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`, now draws only the welcome boards. A copy of the A/B version is in this session's scratchpad.\n\nThe images I uploaded for the variants stay in the canvas's asset store, unreferenced: the plate captures, and the empty-plate capture made for the withdrawn headline change. I did not delete them, because deleting assets needs Kenneth to confirm each one.\n\n## What is placeholder\n\n- The agent's words in beat 2 are the opening of a real reply about a different print, the vase in journey `j3-opus-photo`. They stay until a live run on this photo is recorded.\n- The two settings in beat 3 (Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm, Nozzle 220 → 200 °C) are textbook fixes for stringing, not agent output.\n- The boats on the plate are the animatic's renders of the bundled 3DBenchy, standing in for the app's own view. The clip that ships is meant to be a recording of the real app.\n- The header shows \"JusPrin › Agent\" and \"Agent not connected\", copied from the reference render. Whether the welcome screen sits under the Agent crumb was not part of the decision.\n\n## What I left out, and the gaps\n\n- **Display type size.** The reference animatic drew the two settings, the \"Slicing NN%\" line and the bar's label at 36 to 48 px. The type scale's largest token is page-title (24 px), so the boards use that, and the settings read smaller than in the reference. If Kenneth wants the reference size, the token file needs a display size first.\n- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.\n- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.\n- **The clip in motion.** The canvas holds still frames only. The moving reference is `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4`.\n\n## Findings from the variant work that still apply\n\nThese came from reading the code for the withdrawn variants and still matter for \"Just slice for now\" and the printer order Kenneth decided:\n\n- The \"from the file\" chip would mislabel an assumed default. The rule behind it (`printer_from_file`, which tests `!is_named_printer`) cannot tell the two cases apart, so the assumed mark needs a stored origin.\n- An empty data folder has no printers (`presets_list` returned 0), so the default printer has to be installed at first run. The A1 mini was only the example in Kenneth's sentence.\n- The project chat cannot add a printer. `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest belong to the printer conversation only.\n- Home has no agent pane: `ShellController.cpp:1913` keeps the pane collapsed on Home.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":140,"newStart":1,"newLines":48,"lines":["-# First-run flow design: two variants, 2026-11-02","+# First launch: one welcome screen, 2026-11-02"," ","-This is a design proposal for what replaces the onboarding wizard, and no code has changed. In variant A, a new person lands on Home, opens a part, and the app talks about that part before asking for anything. In variant B, one welcome screen comes first and asks how they want to run the agent. Both are drawn so Kenneth can compare them, and neither has been ruled on.","+The two no-wizard first-run variants (A: no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn and a sign-in prompt on Send; B: a welcome screen with three equal doors) are withdrawn. On 2026-11-02 Kenneth chose a different first launch from rendered comparisons: one split welcome screen with a looping clip on the left and the words and doors on the right, built around expert help with a failed print. That screen is now on the JusPrin v2 canvas. No code has changed, and nothing here is committed."," ","-- Boards: the JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 85, under the existing boards. Boards 00 to 18 and Welcome 1b to 1d are still there.","-- PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`, with `a-` and `b-` prefixes.","-- Plates are captured from the real app. The agent's words were written for the boards and are not model output, because I ran no live model.","+The decision record is the memory note `first-run-value-prop-decisions.md`. The reference renders it was chosen from are in `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked)."," ","-## The comparison","+## What is on the canvas now"," ","-Screens and clicks run from launch to the agent's first words about the person's own part. A drop or a file pick counts as one action.","+The JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 87 (`1793677670-03be`):"," ","-| Kind of person | Variant A | Variant B |","-| --- | --- | --- |","-| Own API key | 2 screens (Home, Prepare), 1 action (open the part). They haven't given a key yet, so these words run on the app's device token. | 3 screens (Welcome, Home, Prepare), 2 actions (paste the key, open the part), plus getting a key elsewhere if they don't have one to hand. |","-| Hosted | 2 screens, 1 action, the same as above. Sign-in comes later, on their first Send. | 3 screens plus the browser, 2 actions in the app (the sign-in button, open the part), plus the sign-in itself. |","-| MCP (Claude Code or Claude Desktop) | 2 screens, 1 action, but the words come from the app's own turn and not from their tool. Connecting their tool takes gear, Preferences › Agent, Connect…, and A never asks them to. | 3 screens plus their own tool. 3 clicks (Copy, Go to Home, open the part), then they run the command or restart Claude Desktop, then ask in their tool. \"Add it for me\" replaces Copy and running the command. The first words appear in their tool only when they ask. |","-","-| | Variant A | Variant B |","-| --- | --- | --- |","-| Model cost per install | One app-funded turn for every install that opens a file, before we know who it is. It also needs abuse limits on the device token. | Nothing for own key, MCP or Just slice. Hosted pays the same turn, but only after sign-in. |","-| What it needs built first | An anonymous device token, which doesn't exist in the code. | Nothing of that kind. The doors use key checking and MCP setup that exist, plus sign-in. |","-| Sees which kind of person this is | At the gate, for those who reach it: sign-in or key. MCP people show up only if they find Preferences. | At launch: the door they chose, and how many leave Welcome. Just slice counts as a stated choice. |","-| Cannot see | Who someone is before the gate, or what kind of person left after hearing the agent. Whether an MCP person exists at all. | Whether hearing the agent first would have changed the choice. An MCP door click doesn't prove the client connected. |","-","-The one measured number for model cost is $0.030 for a single file-opened turn on Opus 5.5: one request, in one run, the Bunny journey in `journey-cost-2026-10.md`. That run read 15,512 tokens from cache. A true first turn may find a cold cache and cost more, and I did not calculate by how much. Under the rule Kenneth set on 2026-11-02 in `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md`, this turn runs on the Expert alias and costs 0 credits, so the app pays it in both variants.","-","-`McpStatusPayload` and the connection list exist, and I did not check whether they can report that a client actually connected. That decides whether variant B can count MCP people or only MCP door clicks.","-","-## The printer, in both variants","-","-Kenneth decided the order on 2026-11-02: the printer preset in a 3MF, else an import from OrcaSlicer when a configuration is on the machine, else a default the chip marks as assumed and the agent's first words name. A silent default is never allowed. The assumed state is drawn once, on board `a-03b`: the chip reads \"assumed\", the agent starts with \"I've assumed a Bambu A1 mini; tell me if it's something else.\", and Slice is enabled.","-","-## Variant A: no welcome screen","-","-| Board | What the person sees |","+| Board | What it shows |"," | --- | --- |","-| 01a Home, OrcaSlicer found | An empty project area with \"Drop a model or project to start\" and \"Try the example\". In the right column, the offer card \"Your first month: 500 credits\", \"An Expert message is 5 credits. Your own API key stays free.\", and the button \"Sign in for 500 credits\". One quiet row offers to import OrcaSlicer's printers and presets. Nothing blocks the screen. |","-| 01b Home, nothing to import | The same screen without the import row. |","-| 02a Own model opened | Prepare with their part on the plate, the chat panel open, and \"Working on it…\" with Stop. |","-| 02b Example opened | The bundled 3DBenchy on the plate. The agent says what it is and why it's there. |","-| 03a Speaks on the part | With an imported printer, the agent describes the hook, says it fits the printer, names the risk in how it sits, and asks what it will hang. No account has been asked for. |","-| 03b Assumed printer | The same turn on the assumed default. The agent's first sentence names the assumption and the turn still ends with one question. |","-| 04a Send is the gate | They typed \"A heavy winter coat.\" and pressed Send. A band above the box offers \"Sign in for 500 credits to send this\" with \"Paste an API key\" beside it. The text stays in the box. |","-| 04b Gate on a printer correction | The same gate when they typed \"It's a Prusa MK4, actually.\", plus the printer list as the way to change it with no account. |","-| 04c Browser round trip | The browser is open on sign-in. The band reads \"Finish signing in in your browser, then come back here.\" with \"Open browser again\" and \"Cancel\". The browser page is representative, not the real one. |","-| 04d Back in the same chat | The same chat with the same text in the box, Send active, the Expert and thinking pickers visible, and \"You're signed in, and 500 first-month credits are yours.\" |","-| 05 Ordinary flow | The agent proposes in words and they reply \"Do that and slice\". The changes run, the plate slices, and the header's button becomes Print. The numbers (~21 min, 5.3 g) come from a real slice. Boards 13 to 16 cover the rest. |","-| 06 Turn could not run | \"JusPrin couldn't look at your part\": the AI service was unreachable, the project is open and nothing is lost, with Retry and Continue locally. |","-| 07 Own key door | \"Paste an API key\" opens Preferences › Agent at the existing key rows. Their text is still in the box behind it. |","+| `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1` | The welcome screen with the clip at beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside the photo of the stringing Benchy, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\" On the right are the title, the subtitle, the line above the doors, the first-month offer as the one primary door, the two free rows with their costs, \"Just slice for now\", and the footer. |","+| `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame` | The same screen with the clip's final frame: the clean boat in the thumbnail, a green check, \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\", and the sliced boat on the plate. |","+| `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard` | The four beats with their captions and timings, a note on which parts are placeholders, and the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. Beat 4 is shown with the bar at 68 %, since the final frame is on 02. |"," ","-## Variant B: one welcome screen","+Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`."," ","-Variant B differs from A only before Home, plus what follows from having chosen. There is no anonymous turn and no sign-in gate, because the person already chose a door. After Home, A's boards apply: 02a, 03a or 03b, 05 and 06, with the model picker in the box where A draws it bare.","+Every string comes from Kenneth's choice or the animatic's `strings.js`. Colours, radii, type and spacing come from the token file, and the boards contain no colour literals."," ","-| Board | What the person sees |","-| --- | --- |","-| 01 Welcome | \"OrcaSlicer's workflow, with an AI agent that plans the print.\" and \"Choose how to run the agent. Each way is one step, and you can change it later in Preferences.\" Three cards side by side: own API key, first-month offer, MCP. Under them, \"Just slice for now\" and \"Everything works without the agent. It's here when you want it.\" |","-| 02a Key verified | \"This key works: it replied in 0.8 s.\" and \"Saved to Preferences › Agent. Taking you to Home…\" |","-| 02b Key rejected | \"Anthropic turned this key down, so nothing was saved.\" The field keeps the key and the other doors stay open. |","-| 03 Browser round trip | The same browser step as A, waiting inside the offer card. |","-| 04a MCP command copied | Claude Code tab, the real command, \"Copied\", and \"Go to Home\". |","-| 04b MCP settings copied | Claude Desktop tab, the real settings JSON, \"Copied\", and \"Go to Home\". |","-| 05a Home, own key | \"The agent is ready\", with the key's masked hint. |","-| 05b Home, signed in | \"The agent is ready\", with 500 credits. |","-| 05c Home, MCP | \"Claude Code can connect\" and \"Show the command again\". It doesn't say connected, because copying a command doesn't prove it ran. JusPrin has to stay open, because the server runs in the app. |","-| 05d Home, Just slice | The three doors again, small. |","-| 06 Prepare, Just slice | The chip reads \"assumed\", with \"JusPrin assumed a Bambu A1 mini, because this file doesn't name a printer. Change it from the menu at the top.\", small doors, and no message box. |","+## How the revert was done"," ","-The MCP command and settings are the real shape from `Mcp/McpConnections.hpp`, with a placeholder home folder and an assumed `/Applications` install. Windows and Linux paths differ. I assumed the MCP person's Prepare pane shows the doors like board 06, because the app starts no turn for them, and I did not draw it separately.","+My variants touched only their own entries on the page. I compared the index saved before my first publish (version `1793658772-45ce`) with the live one: apart from the 24 `first-run-a-*` and `first-run-b-*` boards and their 4 notes, every board, note and page entry was identical. Version 87 removes exactly those and adds the three welcome boards and two notes. The builder, `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`, now draws only the welcome boards. A copy of the A/B version is in this session's scratchpad."," ","-## The open code question: can the file-opened turn run with no printer selected?","+The images I uploaded for the variants stay in the canvas's asset store, unreferenced: the plate captures, and the empty-plate capture made for the withdrawn headline change. I did not delete them, because deleting assets needs Kenneth to confirm each one."," ","-Yes as far as printers go, but I read that part of the code and did not run the turn, because live model tests need Kenneth's approval.","+## What is placeholder"," ","-- From the code: `on_file_loaded` (`AgentHost.cpp:1577`) has no printer check. It starts the turn when the agent is available and ready, no other tool profile is active, and a `file_loaded` skill exists.","-- Observed on the real build with an empty data folder, through MCP tools with no model: a project opens on the placeholder \"Default Printer\" with a 200×200×100 bed, and the load report says `printerOrigin:\"default\"` and `setupPrinters:[]`.","-- What stops the turn today is having no model. With no key and no sign-in there is no agent, and I found no anonymous device token in the code. Variant A can't run before its gate without one. Variant B's doors don't need it.","+- The agent's words in beat 2 are the opening of a real reply about a different print, the vase in journey `j3-opus-photo`. They stay until a live run on this photo is recorded.","+- The two settings in beat 3 (Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm, Nozzle 220 → 200 °C) are textbook fixes for stringing, not agent output.","+- The boats on the plate are the animatic's renders of the bundled 3DBenchy, standing in for the app's own view. The clip that ships is meant to be a recording of the real app.","+- The header shows \"JusPrin › Agent\" and \"Agent not connected\", copied from the reference render. Whether the welcome screen sits under the Agent crumb was not part of the decision."," ","-## What building either variant would run into","+## What I left out, and the gaps"," ","-Both variants:","+- **Display type size.** The reference animatic drew the two settings, the \"Slicing NN%\" line and the bar's label at 36 to 48 px. The type scale's largest token is page-title (24 px), so the boards use that, and the settings read smaller than in the reference. If Kenneth wants the reference size, the token file needs a display size first.","+- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.","+- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.","+- **The clip in motion.** The canvas holds still frames only. The moving reference is `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4`."," ","-1. **\"From the file\" would mislabel an assumed default.** I opened the Benchy `.drc` on a scratch data folder whose A1 mini is not a named printer, and the chip showed \"⚠ Bambu Lab A1 mini · 0.4 · from the file\". The rule behind it, `printer_from_file`, tests `!is_named_printer`, so the chip can't tell the two cases apart. The assumed mark needs a stored origin.","-2. **The default printer has to be installed at first run.** `presets_list` returned 0 printers on empty data. The A1 mini is the example in Kenneth's sentence, and I found no decision saying it is the default.","-3. **The project chat can't add a printer.** `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest are printer-conversation only, and `printer_setup` only switches installed presets. So \"tell me if it's something else\" needs a way through. My pick is handing off to the printer conversation (`ShellController::open_printer_conversation`), carrying their answer. The alternative is exposing those tools in the project chat.","-4. **The file-loaded skill has to state the assumption.** It would also need the assumed origin as a fact it can read.","-5. **There is no bundled example and no OrcaSlicer import.** `resources/handy_models/3DBenchy.drc` opens fine and is what I drew. `V1Import` handles JusPrin v1 only.","-6. **Not-set-up strings get replaced.** \"No agent connected\", \"Set up the agent\", \"Chatting here needs an agent.\" and the raw model id in the box all go.","-7. **The sign-in address is drawn as `app.obico.io/o/authorize`.** That comes from `CloudAccount.cpp`, and the domain question is still open before desktop ships.","-8. **`use_chat_model` stores the first choice on any turn.** `pricing-implementation-plan-2026-11.md` already says it must change, so the app's turn leaves the pickers live.","+## Findings from the variant work that still apply"," ","-Variant A:","+These came from reading the code for the withdrawn variants and still matter for \"Just slice for now\" and the printer order Kenneth decided:"," ","-9. **The device token needs building, with abuse limits.** Nothing exists yet.","-10. **Board 04b assumes the printer list works offline.** I did not verify that it opens and works with no model and no network.","-","-Variant B:","-","-11. **Detecting the provider from a pasted key needs building.** It reverses the `key_prefixes` table in `AgentSetup.cpp:26-30`, where `sk-` falls to OpenAI. Today Preferences has a row per provider.","-12. **\"Add it for me\" reuses the Preferences Connect… path** in `Shell/McpSetupCommand.cpp`. It works only where the client's CLI is present, and the door has to fall back to Copy.","-13. **The 0.8 s check string comes from memory of 2026-09.** Key checking exists in `ProviderKeySetup`, and I didn't recheck the current wording.","-","-## Conflicts between the two briefs for you to settle","-","-- **Home has no agent pane.** The brief says the pane on Home is already live or shows the doors. In the app, `ShellController.cpp:1913` keeps the pane collapsed on Home. I drew those states at the top of the Printers column. The alternative is showing the pane on Home for first run, which changes Home for everyone.","-- **The offer's sentence.** The first message said \"An Expert message is 5 credits.\" and the later one adds \"Your own API key stays free.\" I used the longer one everywhere. On the welcome card it sits right beside the own-key door, so it says the same thing twice.","-- **\"Differs in exactly one place\".** The later message says that, and the earlier one says no anonymous turn and no gate. I drew no gate in B, since nobody who took a door can hit it, and someone who chose Just slice has no message box.","-","-## Decisions I made that Kenneth hasn't ruled on","-","-Printer:","-- The import stays a one-click row on Home. If they skip it and open a file, they get the assumed default. The alternative is importing automatically, which would make the assumed state rarer for people coming from OrcaSlicer.","-","-Home and the offer:","-- The offer card sits at the top of the Printers column, with a primary button alongside the primary \"Open…\". The alternatives are a secondary button, or the card above the drop zone.","-- The offer stays until they sign in or add a key, and it has no dismiss.","-- \"Agent\" is explained once, in Home's drop-zone text in A and on the welcome headline in B.","-","-The gate, variant A:","-- It appears when they press Send, not before, and an X closes it and keeps their text.","-- Reply choices and printer corrections go through the same gate, so there is one rule.","-- The message is not sent automatically on return, following the 2026-10-23 rule. They press Send themselves.","-- Before an account or key exists, the box shows only + and Send, with no model picker.","-- A failed turn does not count as the one free turn.","-- **Not drawn and not decided:** what happens when someone with no account opens a second file. `on_file_loaded` would start another turn, so the device token's limit has to answer this.","-","-Board 05:","-- \"Proposes, person applies\" is drawn as the agent asking in words and the person replying, because valid tool calls start at once and there is no approval step. Boards 13 to 16 are older and still show Apply and slice, so they disagree with this board.","-","-Left undrawn:","-- Import results (existing board 18 covers partial results).","-- Sign-in failure and cancel beyond the Cancel link (existing board 05 covers a blocked return).","-","-## Checks and leftovers","-","-- All 24 boards were rendered and inspected in light. Dark was checked on `a-01a`, `a-04b`, `a-05`, `b-01` and `b-05d`, and the tokens hold apart from the plate capture, which stays light.","-- Everything comes from tokens except three things. The filament swatch `#1E8A7A` is filament data, not a UI colour. The printer icon on the chip is drawn with 1px radii, and the chip's internal gaps and 26px height are copied from the published credits boards.","-- Network finds are Bambu only, from the 2026-10-20 add-printer notes and not rechecked. The agent's words on these boards no longer offer to look on the network.","-- Of the canvas's 14 comment threads, I listed 9 and none are on first-run boards. The other 5 were not listed. I acted on none.","+- The \"from the file\" chip would mislabel an assumed default. The rule behind it (`printer_from_file`, which tests `!is_named_printer`) cannot tell the two cases apart, so the assumed mark needs a stored origin.","+- An empty data folder has no printers (`presets_list` returned 0), so the default printer has to be installed at first run. The A1 mini was only the example in Kenneth's sentence.","+- The project chat cannot add a printer. `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest belong to the printer conversation only.","+- Home has no agent pane: `ShellController.cpp:1913` keeps the pane collapsed on Home."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8044edbb-11bc-4461-b9e6-b40f8dd0dc2b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"e5e7be70-4135-4ef5-84ac-b5a2a3e936e2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfJyVjAp9wEzWpwEdmrG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qomp7RLN2msqqg44wEAAYP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-flow-boards.md","content":"---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87); builder build_first_run_page.py.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`. The untracked note is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root, and the PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nGaps the note lists: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip.\n\nFacts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane.\n\n**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current.\n\n**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":337430,"output_tokens":3378,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":110},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3378,"cache_read_input_tokens":337430,"cache_creation_input_tokens":847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":847},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Qomp7RLN2msqqg44wEAAYP":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-flow-boards.md","content":"---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87); builder build_first_run_page.py.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`. The untracked note is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root, and the PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nGaps the note lists: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip.\n\nFacts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane.\n\n**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current.\n\n**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgfJyVSoJJ4nmtmdW9quB","requestRef":"60a7138a-3016-4e16-9b00-eeb2afa5cc89","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f4479f44-aca5-4012-a30c-fc95463c2512","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:37.039Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"f4479f44-aca5-4012-a30c-fc95463c2512","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3302b766-bcdc-47a6-990a-3c389fab5338","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qomp7RLN2msqqg44wEAAYP","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-flow-boards.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"6d714840-1e3d-4d48-bf76-272037949b5c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:37.068Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-flow-boards.md","content":"---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87); builder build_first_run_page.py.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438\n  modified: 2026-11-03T03:48:37.053Z\n---\n\n2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`. The untracked note is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root, and the PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nGaps the note lists: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip.\n\nFacts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane.\n\n**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current.\n\n**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":23,"newStart":1,"newLines":19,"lines":[" ---"," name: first-run-flow-boards","-description: \"First-run boards replacing the onboarding wizard, two variants (first-run-a-*, first-run-b-* on the canvas onboarding page, version 85, 2026-11-02); proposal awaiting Kenneth's choice, nothing built.\"","+description: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87); builder build_first_run_page.py.\""," metadata:","   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","-  modified: 2026-11-02T23:44:43.501Z","+  modified: 2026-11-03T03:48:37.053Z"," ---"," ","-2026-11-02: Kenneth is comparing two first-run flows, on the JusPrin v2 canvas, page \"On boarding experience\", built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`. Variant A has no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn, and a gate on Send. Variant B has one welcome screen with three doors (own key, first-month offer, MCP) and Just slice. The note with each board, the comparison and every unruled decision is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root (untracked); PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.","+2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`. The untracked note is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root, and the PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`."," ","-Kenneth decided the printer order the same day: 3MF preset, else OrcaSlicer import, else a default the chip marks as assumed and the agent's first words name. Never silent.","+Gaps the note lists: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip."," ","-Facts found that will surprise whoever builds this:","-- `on_file_loaded` has no printer check (read, not run). No model is what stops the turn, and no anonymous device token exists, so only variant A needs one built.","-- `printer_from_file` tests `!is_named_printer`, so an assumed default would show \"from the file\". The mark needs a stored origin.","-- The project chat can't add a printer: `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest are printer-conversation only.","-- Home has no agent pane (`ShellController.cpp:1913`), so door states are drawn in the Printers column.","+Facts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane."," ","-**Why:** Kenneth hasn't reviewed these, so treat them as a proposal, not as decided design.","+**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current."," ","-**How to apply:** check whether Kenneth has picked a variant and ruled on the note's decision list before building from these boards. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]], [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]], [[file-printer-switch-decisions]].","+**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]]."]}],"originalFile":"---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-run boards replacing the onboarding wizard, two variants (first-run-a-*, first-run-b-* on the canvas onboarding page, version 85, 2026-11-02); proposal awaiting Kenneth's choice, nothing built.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438\n  modified: 2026-11-02T23:44:43.501Z\n---\n\n2026-11-02: Kenneth is comparing two first-run flows, on the JusPrin v2 canvas, page \"On boarding experience\", built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`. Variant A has no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn, and a gate on Send. Variant B has one welcome screen with three doors (own key, first-month offer, MCP) and Just slice. The note with each board, the comparison and every unruled decision is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root (untracked); PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nKenneth decided the printer order the same day: 3MF preset, else OrcaSlicer import, else a default the chip marks as assumed and the agent's first words name. Never silent.\n\nFacts found that will surprise whoever builds this:\n- `on_file_loaded` has no printer check (read, not run). No model is what stops the turn, and no anonymous device token exists, so only variant A needs one built.\n- `printer_from_file` tests `!is_named_printer`, so an assumed default would show \"from the file\". The mark needs a stored origin.\n- The project chat can't add a printer: `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest are printer-conversation only.\n- Home has no agent pane (`ShellController.cpp:1913`), so door states are drawn in the Printers column.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth hasn't reviewed these, so treat them as a proposal, not as decided design.\n\n**How to apply:** check whether Kenneth has picked a variant and ruled on the note's decision list before building from these boards. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]], [[sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent]], [[file-printer-switch-decisions]].\n","userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f4479f44-aca5-4012-a30c-fc95463c2512","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
