{"parentUuid":"eafa82c6-a145-4bf3-91e5-a7ef9bb8f725","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/MEMORY.md","snippet":""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f8a8aa80-cc38-4e3c-ad00-1144f65acd17","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:39.964Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/MEMORY.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"f8a8aa80-cc38-4e3c-ad00-1144f65acd17","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Plain"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"62df17c2-d29a-412f-b798-9995da90e7c8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:39.964Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPlain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","hash":"189bf2c7a007c471ad821e529c0c0aa83afe4d0ded8cf2f44d1b042616ab33c6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WqAWEDidoEJmVwu91mXY5K","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md","content":"# First launch: one welcome screen, 2026-11-02\n\nThe two no-wizard first-run variants (A: no welcome screen, an anonymous first turn and a sign-in prompt on Send; B: a welcome screen with three equal doors) are withdrawn. On 2026-11-02 Kenneth chose a different first launch from rendered comparisons: one split welcome screen with a looping clip on the left and the words and doors on the right, built around expert help with a failed print. That screen is now on the JusPrin v2 canvas. No code has changed, and nothing here is committed.\n\nThe decision record is the memory note `first-run-value-prop-decisions.md`. The reference renders it was chosen from are in `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/` (untracked).\n\n## What is on the canvas now\n\nThe JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 87 (`1793677670-03be`):\n\n| Board | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1` | The welcome screen with the clip at beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside the photo of the stringing Benchy, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\" On the right are the title, the subtitle, the line above the doors, the first-month offer as the one primary door, the two free rows with their costs, \"Just slice for now\", and the footer. |\n| `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame` | The same screen with the clip's final frame: the clean boat in the thumbnail, a green check, \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\", and the sliced boat on the plate. |\n| `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard` | The four beats with their captions and timings, a note on which parts are placeholders, and the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. Beat 4 is shown with the bar at 68 %, since the final frame is on 02. |\n\nTwo canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nEvery string comes from Kenneth's choice or the animatic's `strings.js`. Colours, radii, type and spacing come from the token file, and the boards contain no colour literals.\n\n## How the revert was done\n\nMy variants touched only their own entries on the page. I compared the index saved before my first publish (version `1793658772-45ce`) with the live one: apart from the 24 `first-run-a-*` and `first-run-b-*` boards and their 4 notes, every board, note and page entry was identical. Version 87 removes exactly those and adds the three welcome boards and two notes. The builder, `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`, now draws only the welcome boards. A copy of the A/B version is in this session's scratchpad.\n\nThe images I uploaded for the variants stay in the canvas's asset store, unreferenced: the plate captures, and the empty-plate capture made for the withdrawn headline change. I did not delete them, because deleting assets needs Kenneth to confirm each one.\n\n## What is placeholder\n\n- The agent's words in beat 2 are the opening of a real reply about a different print, the vase in journey `j3-opus-photo`. They stay until a live run on this photo is recorded.\n- The two settings in beat 3 (Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm, Nozzle 220 → 200 °C) are textbook fixes for stringing, not agent output.\n- The boats on the plate are the animatic's renders of the bundled 3DBenchy, standing in for the app's own view. The clip that ships is meant to be a recording of the real app.\n- The header shows \"JusPrin › Agent\" and \"Agent not connected\", copied from the reference render. Whether the welcome screen sits under the Agent crumb was not part of the decision.\n\n## What I left out, and the gaps\n\n- **Display type size.** The reference animatic drew the two settings, the \"Slicing NN%\" line and the bar's label at 36 to 48 px. The type scale's largest token is page-title (24 px), so the boards use that, and the settings read smaller than in the reference. If Kenneth wants the reference size, the token file needs a display size first.\n- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.\n- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.\n- **The clip in motion.** The canvas holds still frames only. The moving reference is `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4`.\n\n## Findings from the variant work that still apply\n\nThese came from reading the code for the withdrawn variants and still matter for \"Just slice for now\" and the printer order Kenneth decided:\n\n- The \"from the file\" chip would mislabel an assumed default. The rule behind it (`printer_from_file`, which tests `!is_named_printer`) cannot tell the two cases apart, so the assumed mark needs a stored origin.\n- An empty data folder has no printers (`presets_list` returned 0), so the default printer has to be installed at first run. The A1 mini was only the example in Kenneth's sentence.\n- The project chat cannot add a printer. `printer_identify`, `printer_add` and the rest belong to the printer conversation only.\n- Home has no agent pane: `ShellController.cpp:1913` keeps the pane collapsed on Home.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qomp7RLN2msqqg44wEAAYP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/first-run-flow-boards.md","content":"---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87); builder build_first_run_page.py.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`. The untracked note is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root, and the PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nGaps the note lists: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip.\n\nFacts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane.\n\n**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current.\n\n**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RKQdCrHd5nFPtLQ4pmE418","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory; python3 - <<'E'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('MEMORY.md'); s=p.read_text()\nold=[l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith('- [First-run boards](first-run-flow-boards.md)')]\nassert len(old)==1, old\ns=s.replace(old[0],'- [First-run boards](first-run-flow-boards.md) — A/B withdrawn; welcome boards 01-03 at canvas v87; no display type token; no boards after Just slice.')\np.write_text(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"first-run\" MEMORY.md; grep -n -i \"trial\" /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md || echo 'no banned word'","description":"Update the memory index line and scan the note for banned words"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
