{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","id":"06d86e82-3e1e-4a18-8b03-3ae93867add8","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:48:43.840Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"bff64f584e76dde5905ac869063524d1691d4c70b01471a8cf6409c120a72a2c","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"571e9f17-188d-4bab-8204-19126e713312","keep":158,"tail":["2b0a90015362d62fcba362b9df72562781ff37a54d4b58cb09ec630137bd2364","294184250af6568927bda05dc82b3c51f9c2466e1832d5ff2f088c9727064435","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",160,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"7d758d8519d355fe9c14e4f5c85e44c939b8b6b7197523455e0621674a5777e1"}
{"parentUuid":"d8299685-7790-47ee-a5d7-ceb0069771b0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfK1zizFsoK6jiXoSbCE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Variants A and B are off the JusPrin v2 canvas, and Kenneth's one-screen first launch is on it in their place. The canvas is now at version 87 (`1793677670-03be`), page \"On boarding experience\". Before publishing I checked the page: my variants had changed nothing there except their own 24 boards and 4 notes. Those are the only things removed.\n\n**New boards:**\n- `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`: the welcome screen with the clip at beat 1. It shows the stringing Benchy photo, the intact boat on the plate, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\"\n- `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame`: the same screen with the clip's last frame. It shows the clean boat, a green check and \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\".\n- `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard`: the four beats with their captions and timings, plus the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. It carries a small note saying the agent's words in beat 2 and the two settings in beat 3 are placeholders until a live run.\n\nEvery string on the boards is the wording Kenneth chose, colours and sizes come from the design tokens, and I checked board 01 in dark mode. I sent all three PNGs to Kenneth.\n\n**Left out or not matching the reference:**\n- **Smaller big settings in the clip.** The reference clip drew the two settings and the \"Slicing\" line at 36 to 48 px. The largest text size in the design tokens is 24 px, so they're drawn at that and read smaller. Matching the reference needs a larger size added to the tokens first.\n- **No screens after the doors.** Nothing new was decided there, and my old variant boards don't match the new door wording, so I reused none. An existing board on the same page, `credits-01a-agent-setup`, already shows Preferences › Agent opening on first launch. I didn't check its offer wording against the new card.\n- **\"Just slice for now\" leads nowhere yet.** No board shows Home after that link. The only board showing the printer chip marked \"assumed\" was one of the withdrawn variant boards, so nothing on the canvas shows that state now.\n- **Stand-in boats.** The boats on the plate are the animatic's renders of the bundled 3DBenchy, not captures from the app.\n- **Header copied from the reference.** It reads \"JusPrin › Agent\" with \"Agent not connected\". Whether the welcome screen belongs under the Agent heading wasn't part of Kenneth's decision.\n- **Unused images.** The images I uploaded for the variants are still in the canvas's image store, unused. Deleting them needs Kenneth to confirm each one.\n\nThe note at [first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md](first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md) now says A and B are withdrawn and lists what replaced them. It also keeps the code findings that still apply to \"Just slice for now\" and the printer order. It stays untracked. The PNGs are in [design-captures/first-run-2026-11/](design-captures/first-run-2026-11/)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_read_input_tokens":342275,"output_tokens":1041,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":594,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1041,"cache_read_input_tokens":342275,"cache_creation_input_tokens":594,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":594},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011C