{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-03T04:47:49.489Z","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): build-the-first-launch-c = local_dbced2fd-a752-4429-a46c-4f4bf4c6a8df (idle); find-a-cc-photo-of-a-rec = local_f72d2b0a-d628-44d2-acab-585b51e28763 (idle). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c\" from-name=\"JusPrin pricing goals and priorities\">\nThree edits to the three first-run-welcome boards on the canvas, from Kenneth's review tonight; the clip and the storyboard content do not change.\n\n1. Remove the shell header (the \"JusPrin › Agent\" breadcrumb and the \"Agent not connected\" status). The welcome is a full-window screen with no shell chrome; the breadcrumb and status made no sense before a choice.\n2. Remove the footer sentence \"Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.\" The door rows already show the costs.\n3. Add the brand lockup as a corner anchor top-left of the window: the original horizontal lockup artwork, resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg (the JusPrin lockup; the file name is kept for the overlay), 180×64 viewBox, drawn 43 px tall so it is 120 px wide, the design system's minimum, at space-24 from the left and space-16 from the top, with its clear space, on the plain canvas. Nothing else moves; the content stays centred as it is. Kenneth chose this over a 24 px mark with text after seeing how Stripe, Dropbox, Zoom, Canva and Figma anchor their logo top-left on split sign-in screens. His word: \"Lockup\".\n\nA rendered reference of the exact result is /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/tagline/logo-d-corner-lockup.png (its generator, build7.py in the same folder, shows the CSS). Apply it to first-run-welcome-01 and -02; the storyboard board 03 has no header or footer to remove and gets no logo. Dark variant too if you keep one. Re-publish, update the PNGs in design-captures/first-run-2026-11/ and the note, commit nothing, and send the new welcome-01 PNG with SendUserFile.\n</cross-session-message>"}
