9c94","7b2c5f71-8a56-4bca-99b2-de22974162e9","09ab1eb8-c2d9-4f61-a378-e3431db90382","2c4c8940-42a5-4bd3-aed2-21f51d3ac8be","ff6ca1a1-b155-4606-ad5c-c0a6a9f084c3","d9e63409-b435-4dac-be63-c48d95102c0f","565fa941-29eb-4731-8930-8a860110aa41","aea5dfd0-2a05-44e6-9ecf-c7cb3128f991","234a1739-9023-4cdc-831f-9caf7682daf1","0e5f0bae-edc0-4ecb-b89b-1cf9e9ec6d93","92cd313e-cccc-4e38-b819-f95a5c99eeee","84a234ce-7f6d-4c81-9cae-de41d22b7c38"]},"runningTurnSends":{"uuids":["940ff927-d82a-4eba-899d-f0e8ad5696c6"],"openerUuid":"940ff927-d82a-4eba-899d-f0e8ad5696c6"}},"uuid":"792ae4be-4987-4d2e-ba18-df9322472151","timestamp":"2026-11-03T04:50:15.041Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"792ae4be-4987-4d2e-ba18-df9322472151","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/CLAUDE.md","type":"User","content":"# Global Claude Code Rules\n\n## Git Commit Policy\n\nWhen the user asks to commit changes:\n\n1. Run `git status` and `git diff` to review the changes.\n2. If you are confident that both the changes are correct and the proposed commit message accurately describes them, proceed with git commit without asking for confirmation.\n3. If you have any uncertainty about either, stop and ask the user for explicit confirmation before committing.\n\nWhen the user asks to revert or amend commits:\n1. Explain what will be reverted/amended\n2. Ask for confirmation before executing any `git revert`, `git reset`, or `git commit --amend` commands\n3. Only proceed after explicit user approval\n4. Never revert commits without explicit user confirmation.\n\nThis applies to all git operations that modify commit history.\n\n## Submodule Policy\n\n**Never commit or attempt to commit submodule updates.**\n\nWhen `git status` shows modified submodules (e.g., `modified: some-submodule (new commits)`):\n- Do not stage or commit the submodule change\n- Do not include submodules when running `git add`\n- Leave submodule management to the user\n\n## Testing Principles\n\n1. Always test your code change unless the change is not testable.\n\n2. If the change is not testable, highlight the reason why it's not testable to get the user's attention.\n\n3. By default, do end-to-end testing on everything that may potentially be impacted by your change on the local dev environment.\n\n4. Search for how the dev environment should be started if it's not obvious.\n\n5. Look for README files in the project for related info.\n\n6. Check if the local dev is already running before you try to start it again.\n\n## Bug Fix Policy\n\n**Never apply a fix for a bug you cannot reproduce.**\n\nBefore writing any fix:\n1. Reproduce the bug first in the local dev environment.\n2. If the bug cannot be reproduced locally (e.g., only manifests in release mode, requires specific device conditions, or the debug framework masks the crash), stop and tell the user — do not apply the fix.\n3. A fix is only valid if you can demonstrate the broken behavior before the fix and the correct behavior after.\n\n## Epistemic Discipline — Root Cause of Repeated Errors\n\n**The core failure mode: confusing \"generating a plausible explanation\" with \"knowing the answer.\"**\n\nCoherent ≠ true. A narrative that feels right because it's internally consistent is not a verified fact.\n\nRules to follow every time:\n\n1. **Search before asserting, not after being challenged.** The internet is always available. Use it proactively, not reactively as damage control.\n\n2. **Explicitly label inference vs. verified fact.** If it hasn't been confirmed by a source, say \"my hypothesis is...\" or \"I'd expect...\" — never state it as fact.\n\n3. **\"I don't know yet\" is a complete and correct answer.** Saying it is more helpful than fabricating a confident-sounding explanation.\n\n## Problem Definition Before Search\n\n**A well-defined problem statement is more valuable than a clever hypothesis.**\n\nThe discipline:\n1. **Define the problem precisely first.** Strip out assumptions one by one until the statement contains only what is actually known. Remove irrelevant context (e.g. subscription type if it doesn't affect the symptom).\n2. **Search for the problem directly** — not for your hypothesis. People who already solved the same problem will surface the real root cause.\n3. **Let the search results form the conclusion.** Don't search to confirm what you already believe.\n4. **Be flexible about scope.** Start with the most likely affected area (e.g. Discord) but stay open to other channels or systems being equally or more affected.\n\nSearching to validate a hypothesis finds confirmation of whatever you already believed. Searching for the problem finds answers.\n\n\n## GCP / kubectl Credential Policy\n\nAlways use the service account `ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com` for all `gcloud` and `kubectl` operations. Before running any such command, switch to it:\n\n```bash\ngcloud config set account ai-agent@tsdtechnology.iam.gserviceaccount.com\n```\n\nThe personal account `k@obico.io` is reserved for the user's own interactive CLI use and its OAuth tokens expire — do not rely on it.\n\n## Sentry Access\n\n- Instance: `sentry.obico.io`\n- API base: `https://sentry.obico.io/api/0/`\n- Auth token: `REDACTED`\n- Usage: `curl -H \"Authorization: Bearer <token>\" <api_url>`"},{"path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"@AGENTS.md"},{"path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/AGENTS.md","type":"Project","content":"# CLAUDE.md\n\nJusPrin — a long-lived fork of OrcaSlicer (open-source C++17 3D slicer, wxWidgets GUI, CMake build system).\n\n## Upstream vs. fork attribution\n\nThis checkout holds two codebases: upstream OrcaSlicer (the `upstream` remote, SoftFever/OrcaSlicer) and the JusPrin fork's changes on top of it. Fork changes include everything under `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/` and the seams the fork added inside OrcaSlicer-owned files.\n\n- Say \"OrcaSlicer does X\" only for behavior upstream ships. Behavior added by a fork commit is \"JusPrin does X\", even when it lives in an OrcaSlicer-owned file.\n- Check before attributing; the file path is not enough. Run `git blame` on the line, then `git branch -r --contains <sha> 'upstream/*'`. No upstream branch containing the commit means the fork owns it. Run `git fetch upstream` first if the remote may be stale.\n- If you have not checked, say it is unverified whether the behavior is upstream or fork.\n\n## Error handling discipline\n\n- Do not catch an error merely because it can be caught. Catch only when the code can recover, translate the error at an abstraction boundary, or add context that is essential for diagnosis. Logging alone is not recovery.\n- Represent expected states with normal control flow, not exceptions.\n- Never turn an invariant violation or an \"impossible\" state into success or a silent no-op. Fix the invalid transition at the layer that owns the decision and let unexpected failures propagate to Sentry.\n- Avoid duplicating defensive checks across layers. Keep lower-level operations strict, with their preconditions enforced by the caller that owns the workflow.\n- If concurrency makes an invalid state reachable, fix the ordering or synchronization instead of suppressing the resulting error.\n- Suppress an error only when it is genuinely expected and safely recoverable; document the reason and cover it with a test. Never broadly swallow unexpected errors.\n- Prefer removing the root cause over reducing the visibility of its symptoms. Tests should encode valid transitions and assert that invalid ones remain visible.\n\n## Build Commands\n\n```bash\n# macOS\ncmake --build build/arm64 --config RelWithDebInfo --target all --\n\n# Linux\ncmake --build build --config RelWithDebInfo --target all --\n\n# Windows (replace %build_type% with Debug/Release/RelWithDebInfo)\ncmake --build . --config %build_type% --target ALL_BUILD -- -m\n```\n\nNode/npm is required to build the Agent and Home pages, or configure with `-DJUSPRIN_BUILD_WEB=OFF` and supply the bundles.\n\n### Building on a shared machine\n\nSeveral agent sessions build on the same Mac at once. Without a limit, ninja runs one compile job per core plus two, so every build you start can take the whole machine. In 2026-10 one session stacked four builds in one build directory: 56 clang processes on 12 cores. It kept restarting its build to change targets and never limited the job count.\n\n- Before starting a build, check `uptime` and `pgrep -fl ninja`. If the load is already above the core count, wait or build less.\n- Limit jobs: `cmake --build … -- -j4`.\n- Decide the full target list before starting. Never restart a running build to add or change targets: let it finish, then build the rest.\n- Run one build per build directory. Two ninja processes in one directory compete and can leave its records inconsistent.\n- Stopping a build means stopping ninja. `pkill -f \"cmake --build …\"` kills only the cmake wrapper, and ninja keeps compiling. Start long builds in their own process group (`perl -e 'setpgrp(0,0); exec @ARGV' cmake --build …`) and stop them with `kill -- -<pgid>`. Then confirm with `pgrep -fl ninja` before building again.\n- When a build is slow, count your own compile processes before blaming the load on other sessions.\n- Reuse an existing build where the task allows. Ask before configuring a fresh full-app build the task does not require.\n\n## Testing\n\nCatch2 framework. Tests in `tests/` directory.\n\n```bash\ncd build && ctest --output-on-failure           # all tests\nctest --test-dir ./tests/libslic3r              # individual suite\nctest --test-dir ./tests/fff_print\n```\n\nPrinter UI without hardware: `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Testing/README.md` (Bambu in-process fake). Isolated `--datadir`; do not drive another JusPrin instance.\n\n## Code Style\n\n- C++17, selective C++20. PascalCase classes, snake_case functions/variables\n- `#pragma once` for headers. Smart pointers and RAII preferred\n- Parallelization via TBB — be mindful of shared state\n- Wording: a file or object is \"opened\", \"imported\", \"loaded\" or \"added\", never \"arrived\". \"Arrive\" is fine for messages, responses, events and lists. `AgentUI/src/wording.test.ts` guards the text the model reads.\n- Wording the model reads calls the product \"the app\", never Orca or OrcaSlicer: the model speaks as the app, and a second name reads as a second program. `AgentUI/src/wording.test.ts` guards this too. Throws and log lines may name Orca; they never reach the model.\n\n## Key Entry Points\n\n- App startup: `src/OrcaSlicer.cpp`\n- Slicing pipeline: `src/libslic3r/Print.cpp`\n- All print/printer/material settings: `src/libslic3r/PrintConfig.cpp`\n- GUI: `src/slic3r/GUI/`\n- Core algorithms: `src/libslic3r/` (GCode/, Fill/, Support/, Geometry/, Format/, Arachne/)\n- Printer profiles: `resources/profiles/[manufacturer].json`\n\n## JusPrin Production UI\n\n- Start with `agent-docs/jusprin/README.md` for the canonical product definition, production architecture, verification method, Orca integration guidance, and design system.\n- Before editing any file outside `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/`, read `agent-docs/jusprin/fork-stewardship.md`. Every line changed in an OrcaSlicer-owned file is a line this fork re-resolves at every rebase, so those changes must be small, product-neutral, additive where possible, and accompanied by the rebase evidence that document requires.\n- Experimental plans, probes, screenshots, logs, and temporary UI code remain on `jusprin-v2-poc`. Use `agent-docs/jusprin/poc-reference.md` for exact commit and path pointers; do not cherry-pick the POC wholesale.\n- Curated brand and semantic UI assets live under `resources/jusprin/`.\n- Before writing or changing any UI code, native or Agent page, follow \"Writing UI code\" in `agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md`: every color, radius, font, and control size comes from the token file through `ShellTheme`, the shell recipes, or the CSS variables. A value with no token gets a token and a guard first, never a literal.\n- Temporary working docs (handoffs, findings, plans written for another agent) stay untracked: never commit them, and never add them to `.gitignore` or `.git/info/exclude`. Untracked files in `git status` are how Kenneth tracks work that isn't finished.\n\n## Critical Constraints\n\n- **Backward compatibility required** for .3mf project files and printer profiles\n- **Cross-platform** — all changes must work on Windows, macOS, and Linux\n- Profile/format changes need version migration handling\n- Dependencies built separately in `deps/build/`, then linked to main app\n\n## Code review focus areas\n\n- Changes must not cause regressions in existing functionality, defaults, profiles, or project compatibility.\n- Features gated by options must not affect existing behavior when those options are disabled.\n- Changes should follow the existing code style and architecture. Architectural changes should be justified in code comments and the PR description.\n- Add helper functions or utilities only when existing code cannot reasonably be reused. Avoid duplication.\n- Changes to OrcaSlicer-owned files must be additive where possible. Rewriting an upstream function, or reimplementing upstream behavior beside it, needs explicit justification in the PR description.\n- When an upstream line is deleted or relocated, say where it went and what a future rebase must carry into the new home.\n- Keep code concise and clear. Manually simplify AI generated bloated codes before review.\n- Include targeted tests or documented verification for behavior changes, especially in slicing logic, profiles, formats, and GUI defaults."},{"path":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem","content":"- [Before running or concluding](evidence-before-handing-kenneth-a-decision.md) — **write the question and who holds the answer first: search, logs, one observation; experiments last.**\n- [Trace a rule to Kenneth's words](trace-a-rule-to-kenneths-words.md) — briefs reword rules stricter; find his words and why before saying \"your rule\".\n- [POC branch](jusprin-v2-poc-rebase-not-merge.md) — rebase the fork's commits, never merge.\n- [Rebase risk](fork-rebase-risk-verify-before-claiming.md) — three checks before claiming it.\n- [Shell phase 1](jusprin-shell-phase-1-design.md) — hide the tab strip, don't reparent Plater.\n- [Teardown crash](orca-inherited-teardown-crash.md) — exit segfault in ~GLCanvas3D; inherited.\n- [Worktree build](jusprin-worktree-build.md) — configure line reusing deps; use /Applications/CMake.app.\n- [Bridge phase 2](agent-bridge-phase-2.md) — page, protocol locations; bundle rebuild rule.; [Bridge phase 3](agent-bridge-phase-3.md) — ToolExecutionCoordinator, staleness, idempotency.; [Bridge phase 4](agent-bridge-phase-4.md) — persistence, aux-dir healing, checkpoint traps.; [Bridge phase 5](agent-bridge-phase-5.md) — attachments: blob storage, revert copy-forward.\n- [Protocol version](protocol-version-only-at-compat-boundary.md) — no bump; use capabilities.\n- [Wall-clock](track-wall-clock-on-background-work.md) — check long tasks really progress.\n- [API-key setup](agent-setup-api-key-path.md) — verification is construction; no project data in probe.\n- [Live-test on Mac](live-test-built-app-on-mac.md) — shared bundle id; second monitor; launch with open -n.\n- [zsh $VAR:path](zsh-var-colon-path-trap.md) — write `${U}:path` or git refs get mangled.\n- [Bash cwd resets](bash-cwd-resets-after-background.md) — cd explicitly or use absolute paths.\n- [Rebrand seams](jusprin-rebrand-seams.md) — 3 seams + 1 attachment point, logo overlay.\n- [Report outcomes](report-outcomes-not-obstacles.md) — skip solved-problem narration.\n- [Chip seams](jusprin-chip-orca-seams.md) — set_bed_type_accord_combox; no filament-preset call.\n- [Bitmap proof](render-widget-to-bitmap-for-visual-proof.md) — green checks hid two defects; render to PNG.\n- [Windows GUI VM](windows-gui-test-vm-gcp.md) — headless testing; Mesa, Defender, session traps.; [Windows VM build](windows-build-on-gcp-vm.md) — full build works; quote -m:6; kill by PID.; [Linux ARM build](linux-arm-docker-build.md) — deps build on aarch64 in 45 min; reuse Dockerfile.\n- [HeaderMenu](header-menu-closes-before-invoking.md) — callbacks outlive popup; controllers shared_ptr.\n- [Panel CSS](agent-panel-css-namespaces.md) — styles.css is global; `setup-*` is taken.\n- [Guard tests](prove-guard-tests-fail-first.md) — Vitest CSS imports are empty; inject a violation.\n- [Fake Moonraker](fake-moonraker-printer-sim.md) — NOT on jusprin-newui; enable_ssl_for_mqtt=false.; [Fake Bambu](fake-bambu-printer-sim.md) — on jusprin-newui; FakeBambuAgent replaces only the agent.; [Fake-printer cleanup](harness-fake-printer-cleanup.md) — deselect, erase record, or later checks stall.\n- [Branch check](verify-current-branch-before-memory-recall.md) — grep the tree before trusting a memory.\n- [Posted keys](drive-app-with-posted-key-events.md) — CGEvent keys work on a locked screen; mouse no.\n- [Subagent worktrees](subagent-worktrees-create-manually.md) — isolation cuts a stale base; make by hand.\n- [Mac popup capture](capture-mac-popups-for-platform-diff.md) — app_screenshot takes a CGWindowID.\n- [PopupWindow crash](popupwindow-hovered-dangling-crash.md) — a96ea65081 wxWeakRef; MallocScribble repro.\n- [GUI lib over 4 GiB](liblibslic3r-gui-4gib-ar-limit.md) — Apple ar asserts; manual llvm-ar relink.\n- [Subagent waits](subagent-must-not-stop-to-wait.md) — ending a turn to wait kills it; block.\n- [Embedded setup](agent-setup-embedded-in-printer-dialog.md) — second AgentWebView, CallAfter teardown trap.\n- [Web bundles](web-bundles-committed-artifact-state.md) — CMake-built, gitignored; *_DEV_URL for HMR.\n- [Bash timeout](background-bash-timeout-kills-builds.md) — exit 130 is the timeout; nohup long builds.\n- [Harness post-init](workspace-harness-never-post-inits-on-mac.md) — exit via ExitMainLoop on Mac.\n- [Printer panel 19b](printer-conversation-panel-19b.md) — Home printers column becomes chat.\n- [Handoff docs](handoff-docs-not-committed.md) — read from main checkout; never commit.\n- [Web view delete](webview-destroyed-mid-handler-install.md) — never during is_adding_script_handler().\n- [Temp docs](temp-docs-stay-untracked-and-visible.md) — stay untracked; never hide via ignore files.\n- [Fake-host page](fake-host-page-fixture.md) — inject window.wx to drive AgentUI/HomeUI states.\n- [Printer-live traps](printer-live-harness-lessons.md) — chat-open ignores opens; key-holding data dirs.\n- [Screenshot files](screenshots-to-files-via-page-fixture.md) — replay host state under Playwright.\n- [\"Connect\"](printer-setup-connect-means-verify-and-save.md) — means verify and save, not keep-alive.\n- [Bambu deviceIds](printer-prompt-card-wording-breaks-connect.md) — fixed by tool-call replay 115e2776bf.\n- [Worktree ownership](never-reuse-another-sessions-worktree.md) — clean + idle is not unowned; make your own.\n- [Closed panel](printer-live-null-host-fix-paused.md) — crash fixed 6a43afff90; check after close fails.\n- [Tool history replay](printer-chat-tool-history-replay.md) — saved callId, no item id, 16 KiB cap.\n- [Filament chip](filament-chip-no-spool-decisions.md) — Orca concepts only, swatches, no spools.\n- [Autosave design](autosave-design-research.md) — two \"modified\" trackers; Kenneth's three decisions.; [Autosave cost](autosave-save-cost-results.md) — mesh saves block ~2.3 µs/triangle of largest object.\n- [Full-disk save](orca-save-silent-corruption-disk-full.md) — export reports success, damages the 3MF.\n- [Mockup strings](mockup-strings-from-real-output.md) — use rule-generated strings, not typed ones.\n- [Print issues](persistent-print-issues-spike.md) — Ask AI / Resolve on Prepare; decisions, gaps.\n- [GL readback](harness-gl-readback-capture.md) — locked screen blanks blits; glReadPixels(GL_FRONT).\n- [Main checkout](worktree-session-cannot-write-main-checkout.md) — a hook refuses Write; use worktree root.\n- [Eval measurements](project-prompt-eval-sample-size.md) — stub rates (\"1 in 15\") are retracted.; [Live eval](live-eval-after-only-vs-baseline.md) — no same-day before run; results become baseline.; [Eval spend](prompt-eval-spend-budget.md) — no live-model tests without Kenneth approving a batch.; [Harness critique](project-prompt-harness-critique.md) — old renderer obsolete; port plan.; [Harness ported](project-prompt-harness-ported.md) — requests recorded by --project-prompt-requests.\n- [Report frame](investigation-report-four-part-frame.md) — problem / solution / tests / remaining; <500 words.\n- [Model-probe harness](model-probe-live-chat-harness.md) — uncommitted; drives the live chat from files.\n- [Manual MCP repro](manual-mcp-tool-repro-recipe.md) — --manual-mcp + probe.call, ~20 s, no model.\n- [Settings blacklist](settings-write-blacklist.md) — tools write all but 51 blocked keys.\n- [Token sync](design-token-sync-decisions.md) — Figma sizes: chip 28, rows 36, icon 32/26.; [Design source](design-source-is-claude-artifacts.md) — Claude artifacts; Figma is frozen.; [Design artifacts](jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact.md) — source of truth; direct-edit recipe.\n- [Edit questions](orca-edit-questions-forwarded.md) — preview warns `skipped_confirmation`; agent decides.\n- [Chrome extension](claude-in-chrome-lives-in-claude-profile.md) — needs a Chrome Profile 20 window.\n- [Deferral commit](jusprin-newui-deferral-commit-removed.md) — 491b56d26b only on feature/tool-deferral.\n- [No tool approval](tool-call-approval-removed.md) — valid calls start at once; never ask to approve.\n- [Write like a person](write-like-a-person.md) — full sentences; say what the person sees, no noun phrases.\n- [Ask decisions in full](ask-decisions-in-full.md) — what, why his, options, consequences, my pick.\n- [pgrep wait loop](pgrep-wait-loop-matches-itself.md) — matches itself; wait on the PID with kill -0.\n- [Ask AI = Resolve](ask-ai-same-tools-as-resolve.md) — same tools, only the sentence differs.\n- [Orca MessageDialog](use-orca-messagedialog.md) — never wxMessageDialog; file opens auto-answer.\n- [Action id collision](printer-panel-action-id-collision.md) — t-1 restart → false local_save_failed; fixed.\n- [Previews skip validate](printer-setup-bed-type-check.md) — Print::validate runs only at slice.\n- [Rare failures](rare-failures-get-a-generic-error.md) — one generic error, no per-cause handling.\n- [Tool result states](tool-result-states-method.md) — Kenneth’s test: a person stuck, false, right step hidden; eight of nine sweep fixes taken out; how the statement drifted.\n- [Forward the real error](forward-the-real-error-four-rules.md) — four rules for false results; no new checks, no OrcaSlicer files.\n- [Prompt sections](project-prompt-sections.md) — five sections; policy out of tool descriptions.; [Rule placement](rule-lives-next-to-what-it-governs.md) — one-tool rules in description, rest in prompt.; [Prompt channels](prompt-principles-vs-state-channels.md) — standing prompt = principles; the rest from the app.\n- [History trimming](history-trimming-by-size.md) — 64 KiB budget in three stages.\n- [Input tags](workspace-input-tags.md) — user message parts with <workspace>/<print_issue>.\n- [Print-setup cases](print-setup-prompt-cases.md) — print-this-no-purpose; recorder traps.\n- [Harness stall](harness-stalls-on-version-dialog.md) — Orca update dialog; fix in 87b3c50474.\n- [Every tool call runs](every-tool-call-runs.md) — parallel_tool_calls true; in order, not_run after failure.\n- [State guidance](state-driven-guidance-project-chat.md) — plate picture + note on file-open turn.\n- [File-loaded skill](skill-model-arrived.md) — skills loader, file_loaded, skill_read.; [Slice-failed skill](skill-slice-failed.md) — unmerged branch; per-plate slice_failure.; [Setup-changed skill](skill-setup-changed.md) — setup_changed trigger, intent reply facts.; [Print-issues skill](skill-print-issues.md) — chip + slice warnings, sliceWarnings.; [Skills integrated](skills-integrated-branch.md) — merged as 8913319cac, pushed.\n- [Restore temp edits](restore-temp-edits-from-a-copy.md) — from a copy, never `git checkout <file>`.\n- [Stated facts](state-fact-test-the-turns-after.md) — \"since X\" needs a reset rule, multi-turn test.\n- [Recorder noise](request-recorder-run-to-run-noise.md) — timestamps, PNG bytes, temp paths only.\n- [Normalize](normalize-derive-current-from-relations.md) — derive \"current\" from the active chat.\n- [DeepSeek images