{"parentUuid":"a4ac9590-acc5-430c-bebb-4f7d4f1e4220","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5b66d6f5-8ce2-4906-a8ad-e3561c0e2014","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016bKEbKi1sL5EhvFiaxXwuH","type":"tool_result","content":"ok\ntracked changes above (none expected)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ede5d0eb-f5db-4f49-9fb2-26efa1b93f3d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T04:51:33.553Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok\ntracked changes above (none expected)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":true,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":16,"newStart":6,"newLines":18,"lines":[" "," ## What is on the canvas now"," ","-The JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 87 (`1793677670-03be`):","+The JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 88 (`1793681477-27e8`):"," "," | Board | What it shows |"," | --- | --- |","-| `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1` | The welcome screen with the clip at beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside the photo of the stringing Benchy, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\" On the right are the title, the subtitle, the line above the doors, the first-month offer as the one primary door, the two free rows with their costs, \"Just slice for now\", and the footer. |","+| `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1` | The welcome screen with the clip at beat 1: the intact 3DBenchy on the plate beside the photo of the stringing Benchy, the message \"I printed it and it failed. What went wrong? Photo attached.\" and the caption \"Show it what happened.\" On the right are the title, the subtitle, the line above the doors, the first-month offer as the one primary door, the two free rows with their costs, and \"Just slice for now\". |"," | `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame` | The same screen with the clip's final frame: the clean boat in the thumbnail, a green check, \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\", and the sliced boat on the plate. |"," | `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard` | The four beats with their captions and timings, a note on which parts are placeholders, and the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. Beat 4 is shown with the bar at 68 %, since the final frame is on 02. |"," "," Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`."," ","+The welcome screen fills the whole window with no shell chrome. Version 88 (Kenneth's review, same evening) removed the \"JusPrin › Agent\" header with \"Agent not connected\" and the footer sentence \"Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.\", because the door rows already show the costs. In their place the JusPrin lockup sits top-left as a corner anchor: the original artwork `resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg` (the `_dark` file in dark mode), drawn 43 px tall so it is 120 px wide, the design system's minimum, at space-24 from the left and space-16 from the top. The content is centred in the full 800 px window and the clip is unchanged. The reference render was `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/tagline/logo-d-corner-lockup.png`; the new board 01 matches its layout. The storyboard board 03 has no lockup.","+"," Every string comes from Kenneth's choice or the animatic's `strings.js`. Colours, radii, type and spacing come from the token file, and the boards contain no colour literals."," "," ## How the revert was done"]},{"oldStart":29,"oldLines":7,"newStart":31,"newLines":6,"lines":[" - The agent's words in beat 2 are the opening of a real reply about a different print, the vase in journey `j3-opus-photo`. They stay until a live run on this photo is recorded."," - The two settings in beat 3 (Retraction 0.8 → 2 mm, Nozzle 220 → 200 °C) are textbook fixes for stringing, not agent output."," - The boats on the plate are the animatic's renders of the bundled 3DBenchy, standing in for the app's own view. The clip that ships is meant to be a recording of the real app.","-- The header shows \"JusPrin › Agent\" and \"Agent not connected\", copied from the reference render. Whether the welcome screen sits under the Agent crumb was not part of the decision."," "," ## What I left out, and the gaps"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a4ac9590-acc5-430c-bebb-4f7d4f1e4220","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
