 own API key / Claude Code or Claude Desktop: Preferences › Agent opens modal on that section over the welcome. Saving a verified key, or Done on the MCP section, closes it and advances to step 2. Closing it unfinished returns to the welcome with nothing chosen. Preferences never navigates; it only closes.\n- Just slice for now: advances to step 2 at once. It skips the detour, not the sequence.\n\nStep 2, Printers. The app needs at least one printer (an empty data folder has none). One of three screens, decided by what the app finds:\n- OrcaSlicer folder on this machine: \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" listing its printers by name and a filament count, with Import (primary) and Start fresh. Import copies the user presets the way the v1 import does, but asked rather than silent, because the folder belongs to another program and includes printer access codes. Then Home. Start fresh goes to the add-printer screen.\n- JusPrin v1 on this machine: step skipped; the existing welcome-back window shows over Home (already designed, onboarding-v1-01…03).\n- Neither: the existing add-printer form (search by model, merged f073fdba96) as this step, with a \"Skip, use a default\" link that installs the default printer and marks the chip as assumed.\n- A Back link on this step returns to the welcome; anything finished there stays finished (the card shows signed in, a saved key stays saved).\n- A 3MF opened by double-click on first launch still shows the welcome, then skips this step because the file carries its printer; the chip says \"from the file\".\n\nStep 3, Home, first-run state reflecting the choices:\n- After sign-in: the agent column shows the connection and the 500-credit balance once (reuse the credits boards' balance treatment).\n- After Just slice: the same three doors collapsed into the agent column under \"Set up the agent\", so the choice stays one click away.\n- The Printers column lists what was imported, added, or the assumed default with its mark.\nOnboarding is marked done only when Home is reached; quitting earlier shows the welcome again next launch with finished detours reflected on its card.\n\nBOARDS TO ADD (whole screens at the app's size, tokens only, strings exactly as above; name them first-run-NN-…):\n04 welcome, sign-in waiting state; 05 welcome, signed-in card just before advancing; 06 Preferences › Agent modal over the welcome, key section (reuse the prefs boards); 07 OrcaSlicer import screen; 08 add-printer step with the skip link; 09 Home after sign-in; 10 Home after Just slice with the collapsed doors and the assumed chip; 11 a flow board: the three steps as boxes, each door's path as an arrow that returns to step 2, the three Printers branches, Back, and the quit rule, with the two code facts as footnotes. Keep the three welcome boards as they are.\n\nThe old wizard boards (onboarding-00 to -20) contradict this flow. Do not delete them; add one note beside them saying they are superseded by first-run-01…11 as of 2026-11-02, and move them to the bottom of the page if the builder allows.\n\nReference: the printer-order decision and the chip-origin finding are in your own note; the credits balance treatment is on the credits boards. Publish, update design-captures/first-run-2026-11/ and first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md, commit nothing, and send the flow board PNG and board 07 with SendUserFile when done, with the canvas version and anything you left out.\n</cross-session-message>"},"uuid":"7a14d2cf-1be9-4fb0-b9a3-eab889f8b103","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:05:15.465Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","promptSource":"sdk","turnOrigin":"sdk","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":8},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
