{"parentUuid":"b82b05cc-0f43-4a8d-9002-863d57364022","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3dbd4941-397f-4f1f-b100-534960d73c43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DHWJfrmCUuVHTSEbGfBxvN","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: add-printer-popup-feasibility\ndescription: \"2026-10-20 feasibility of the canvas 3-step \\\"Add a printer\\\" popup replacing run_wizard in the printer chat; what Orca can and can't supply, 5 decisions asked of Kenneth.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 2e4c8ad1-82aa-46c8-8b45-2bdab5d28d27\n  modified: 2026-10-20T22:28:20.500Z\n---\n\nWorktree `.claude/worktrees/add-printer-popup` (removed 2026-10-21), branch `claude/add-printer-popup` off jusprin-newui 1cbce387d8. Feasibility reported 2026-10-20; nothing built until Kenneth answers.\n\nVerified facts (file:line in the report):\n- Network finds are Bambu only. `discover_printers()` hides LAN printers with no access code (upstream `get_my_machine_list` filter); the fuller list is `get_local_machinelist()`. SSDP needs the plug-in AND the Bambu agent active (only when a Bambu preset is selected). Non-Bambu scans (Bonjour/_octoprint, Creality, Flashforge) run only from PhysicalPrinterDialog's Browse.\n- `add_printer` accepts a device_id and records the link, but nothing passes one. Nozzle unknown before connecting.\n- Plate: `curr_bed_type` is project-level. Orca remembers `printer_settings[<name>].curr_bed_type` per printer name, then falls back to hidden `default_bed_type` (numeric only; text falls back to High Temp). Plate dropdown only for Bambu or `support_multi_bed_types` (MK4 and Ender 3 V2: off). No \"Satin\"/\"Smooth PEI\".\n- Filament: \"Common on\" has no data; `default_materials` is the closest (MK4 = 10 Prusa Generic). Prusament profiles are compatible only with CORE One. Tray sync needs a connected printer.\n- Catalog: 64 brands / 383 models; nozzle sets vary (1 to 8 sizes), so no fixed 4-button control; SecKit/Seckit brand split.\n- The design boards draw no Back/Next/Cancel, and their examples conflict (Ender 3 V2 vs MK4).\n\nRecommended (pending Kenneth): passive Bambu-only list; plate step only where Orca offers plates, saved via `select_bed_type`; step 3 = \"Which filament do you want to start with?\" + \"Suggested for the <model>\"; controls added in code first; the native error fallback keeps run_wizard.\n\nRelated: [[filament-chip-no-spool-decisions]], [[jusprin-chip-orca-seams]], [[design-source-is-claude-artifacts]], [[printer-conversation-panel-19b]].\n\n**Built 2026-10-20 (uncommitted, worktree above):** Kenneth took all 5 recommendations, then approved the filament-step redesign (design session's artifact https://claude.ai/artifact/Kytv8cHPVQdN1ajW2K96N1; canvas v38 + Design System v29 updated to match). Step 3 = \"Your filaments\" / \"Suggested for the <model>\" (profile default first) / \"Every filament for the <model>\"; at the end a \"Show filaments made for other printers\" tick box (picking one saves an OrcaSlicer clone_presets_for_filament copy \"<alias> @<printer>\" into slot 1) and \"Create a filament preset…\" (adds the printer, fires EVT_CREATE_FILAMENT, puts the new preset in slot 1). Options come from SetupOptionsLoader (scratch PresetBundle via the new neutral seam PresetBundle::load_system_vendor_from_dir; upstream's later load_vendors does the same, see the comment at the site). Native page-failure fallback keeps run_wizard (action orca_printer_list).\nHarness `--printer-setup` verify_printer_form covers it end to end; `--manual-unconfigured --fake-printer` is the hands-on launch. Create-filament path is tested only with a fake backend (modal window).\n\n**Merged 2026-10-21:** one squashed commit f073fdba96 (amended from 9c59c90480 to fix the stale elegoo check, now live_elegoo_mars_offers_the_full_list) on jusprin-newui, pushed to origin; worktree removed 2026-10-21 (branch claude/add-printer-popup kept). Live harness: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` + `REDACTED` runs `--printer-live` on Haiku 5.5 (~$0.10-0.15 a run); last run 109 pass, 1 stale check (`live_elegoo_mars_suggests_manual_setup` wants the word \"manual\" the prompt no longer asks for).\n----\n---\nname: credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages\ndescription: \"Kenneth, 2026-11-02: credits boards sit on the canvas pages of their flows, not one dedicated page; only the pricing page, states overview and rules stay on Credits & plans.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nDecided after Kenneth's review, relayed by the pricing session: canvas version 69. 1a to 1d, 6a, 6b on \"On boarding experience\"; 2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; 4a to 4c on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; 8a to 8d on \"Print history\"; 0 (five rules), 5a, 5b, 9 on \"Credits & plans\".\n\n**How to apply:** new credits boards go on their flow's page through the `LAYOUT` table in `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_credits_page.py`, with \"Credits\" in the canvas name so a search finds the set. Related: [[print-report-lives-on-history-entry]].\n----\nfigma-mirror/work-first-run/ref/prefs-12-over-prepare.png\nfigma-mirror/work-first-run/ref/credits-01b-welcome.png","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4e958657-bf69-4567-99a2-60007708c5f4","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:05:45.807Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: add-printer-popup-feasibility\ndescription: \"2026-10-20 feasibility of the canvas 3-step \\\"Add a printer\\\" popup replacing run_wizard in the printer chat; what Orca can and can't supply, 5 decisions asked of Kenneth.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 2e4c8ad1-82aa-46c8-8b45-2bdab5d28d27\n  modified: 2026-10-20T22:28:20.500Z\n---\n\nWorktree `.claude/worktrees/add-printer-popup` (removed 2026-10-21), branch `claude/add-printer-popup` off jusprin-newui 1cbce387d8. Feasibility reported 2026-10-20; nothing built until Kenneth answers.\n\nVerified facts (file:line in the report):\n- Network finds are Bambu only. `discover_printers()` hides LAN printers with no access code (upstream `get_my_machine_list` filter); the fuller list is `get_local_machinelist()`. SSDP needs the plug-in AND the Bambu agent active (only when a Bambu preset is selected). Non-Bambu scans (Bonjour/_octoprint, Creality, Flashforge) run only from PhysicalPrinterDialog's Browse.\n- `add_printer` accepts a device_id and records the link, but nothing passes one. Nozzle unknown before connecting.\n- Plate: `curr_bed_type` is project-level. Orca remembers `printer_settings[<name>].curr_bed_type` per printer name, then falls back to hidden `default_bed_type` (numeric only; text falls back to High Temp). Plate dropdown only for Bambu or `support_multi_bed_types` (MK4 and Ender 3 V2: off). No \"Satin\"/\"Smooth PEI\".\n- Filament: \"Common on\" has no data; `default_materials` is the closest (MK4 = 10 Prusa Generic). Prusament profiles are compatible only with CORE One. Tray sync needs a connected printer.\n- Catalog: 64 brands / 383 models; nozzle sets vary (1 to 8 sizes), so no fixed 4-button control; SecKit/Seckit brand split.\n- The design boards draw no Back/Next/Cancel, and their examples conflict (Ender 3 V2 vs MK4).\n\nRecommended (pending Kenneth): passive Bambu-only list; plate step only where Orca offers plates, saved via `select_bed_type`; step 3 = \"Which filament do you want to start with?\" + \"Suggested for the <model>\"; controls added in code first; the native error fallback keeps run_wizard.\n\nRelated: [[filament-chip-no-spool-decisions]], [[jusprin-chip-orca-seams]], [[design-source-is-claude-artifacts]], [[printer-conversation-panel-19b]].\n\n**Built 2026-10-20 (uncommitted, worktree above):** Kenneth took all 5 recommendations, then approved the filament-step redesign (design session's artifact https://claude.ai/artifact/Kytv8cHPVQdN1ajW2K96N1; canvas v38 + Design System v29 updated to match). Step 3 = \"Your filaments\" / \"Suggested for the <model>\" (profile default first) / \"Every filament for the <model>\"; at the end a \"Show filaments made for other printers\" tick box (picking one saves an OrcaSlicer clone_presets_for_filament copy \"<alias> @<printer>\" into slot 1) and \"Create a filament preset…\" (adds the printer, fires EVT_CREATE_FILAMENT, puts the new preset in slot 1). Options come from SetupOptionsLoader (scratch PresetBundle via the new neutral seam PresetBundle::load_system_vendor_from_dir; upstream's later load_vendors does the same, see the comment at the site). Native page-failure fallback keeps run_wizard (action orca_printer_list).\nHarness `--printer-setup` verify_printer_form covers it end to end; `--manual-unconfigured --fake-printer` is the hands-on launch. Create-filament path is tested only with a fake backend (modal window).\n\n**Merged 2026-10-21:** one squashed commit f073fdba96 (amended from 9c59c90480 to fix the stale elegoo check, now live_elegoo_mars_offers_the_full_list) on jusprin-newui, pushed to origin; worktree removed 2026-10-21 (branch claude/add-printer-popup kept). Live harness: `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` + `REDACTED` runs `--printer-live` on Haiku 5.5 (~$0.10-0.15 a run); last run 109 pass, 1 stale check (`live_elegoo_mars_suggests_manual_setup` wants the word \"manual\" the prompt no longer asks for).\n----\n---\nname: credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages\ndescription: \"Kenneth, 2026-11-02: credits boards sit on the canvas pages of their flows, not one dedicated page; only the pricing page, states overview and rules stay on Credits & plans.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nDecided after Kenneth's review, relayed by the pricing session: canvas version 69. 1a to 1d, 6a, 6b on \"On boarding experience\"; 2a to 2c, 3a to 3d, 7a to 7c on \"Compositions\" beside the Composer; 4a to 4c on \"Agent setup & Preferences\"; 8a to 8d on \"Print history\"; 0 (five rules), 5a, 5b, 9 on \"Credits & plans\".\n\n**How to apply:** new credits boards go on their flow's page through the `LAYOUT` table in `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_credits_page.py`, with \"Credits\" in the canvas name so a search finds the set. Related: [[print-report-lives-on-history-entry]].\n----\nfigma-mirror/work-first-run/ref/prefs-12-over-prepare.png\nfigma-mirror/work-first-run/ref/credits-01b-welcome.png","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b82b05cc-0f43-4a8d-9002-863d57364022","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
