7-419d-98a5-e54db2896fbe","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:06:22.719Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"9a1f54ce-86b7-419d-98a5-e54db2896fbe","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3dbd4941-397f-4f1f-b100-534960d73c43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015ZCv3iphCixxyD2XVavh1M","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: printer-conversation-panel-19b\ndescription: Decisions (2026-09-17) for replacing the native Add-printer dialog with the 19b Home printers-column conversation panel driven by the real agent\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 613b3efa-bbf4-455f-a26c-5f5c07391e2c\n  modified: 2026-09-17T17:45:32.002Z\n---\n\nKenneth chose wireframe 19b (Claude Design project d981c5e2-20db-445f-9047-fa9e9a12522e, file \"Orca Printer Setup Wireframes.dc.html\", ids 19b and 19b-add; its CLAUDE.md holds the design rules) on 2026-09-17:\n\n- Home printers column swaps for a conversation panel for both Add (\"+ Add printer\") and Change (a printer's \"Printer settings…\" drops into it).\n- Add flow = open conversation with the REAL agent (not the old PrinterSetupController state machine / direct OpenAI recogniser).\n- Delete the old native PrinterSetupDialog.\n- No agent set up → the same embedded agent-setup page/flow the old dialog used.\n- Keep existing styles; only layout/flow changes.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth expects prompting the agent per context to replace the scripted flow. Reality check given: still needs printer tools (catalog search, network finds, add, access code, edit a saved printer — none exist), a non-persisted Home session with its own prompt/tool set (prompt is hard-coded, registry fixed, sessions persist into the .3mf), and structured cards in the thread (tool results render only as generic rows).\n\n**How to apply:** Check the current branch for progress before assuming any of this is built. Related: [[agent-setup-embedded-in-printer-dialog]], [[add-printer-flow-figma-discrepancy]], [[agent-bridge-phase-5]].\n\n2026-09-18 (printer-agent-tools handoff build): \"Browse the list\" in that handoff is NOT a new in-panel list — Kenneth said it is the existing \"Set it up myself\" link (OrcaSlicer's printer wizard). The model points there when more than three printers fit.\nmemory/first-run-flow-sequence.md:13:- **Home:** first-run state reflects the choices: agent connected and the 500 credits shown once, or the three doors collapsed in the agent column after Just slice; the Printers column lists imported/added/assumed.\nmemory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md:19:- **After the welcome:** an OrcaSlicer import belongs on a conditional screen right after the door, asked (not silent like the v1 import in `V1Import/`), shown only when an OrcaSlicer folder exists; the same action lives later in Home's Printers column and the add-printer form. Follow-up screens per door: sign-in in the browser then Home with the agent connected; own key and MCP open Preferences › Agent; Just slice goes to Home with the doors collapsed in the agent column. Not yet drawn: Home after Just slice, the assumed-printer chip.\ncanvas.json\ncomp-agent-group-keys.dc.html\ncomp-agent-group-tools.dc.html\ncomp-agent-row-account.dc.html\ncomp-agent-row-provider.dc.html\ncomp-agent-row-tool.dc.html\ncomp-agent-tool-connect.dc.html\ncomp-chat-header.dc.html\ncomp-composer.dc.html\ncomp-pinned-setup-card.dc.html\ncomp-prefs-window.dc.html\ncomp-printer-card.dc.html\ncomp-project-card.dc.html\ncredits-00-rules.dc.html\ncredits-01a-agent-setup.dc.html\ncredits-01b-welcome.dc.html\ncredits-01c-welcome-back.dc.html\ncredits-01d-welcome-back-v1-subscriber.dc.html\ncredits-02a-balance-hover.dc.html\ncredits-02b-tier-picker.dc.html\ncredits-02c-pickers-greyed-tooltip.dc.html\ncredits-03a-low-notice.dc.html\ncredits-03b-send-with-basic.dc.html\ncredits-03c-failed-card.dc.html\ncredits-03e-picture-in-standard-chat.dc.html\ncredits-04a-account-over-prepare.dc.html\ncredits-04b-account-first-month.dc.html\ncredits-04c-account-workshop.dc.html\ncredits-05a-pricing.dc.html\ncredits-05b-pricing-obico.dc.html\ncredits-06a-first-month-ended.dc.html\ncredits-06b-first-month-ended-picker.dc.html\ncredits-07a-alert-hobby.dc.html\ncredits-07b-alert-hobby-sums.dc.html\ncredits-08a-report-button.dc.html\ncredits-08b-report-form.dc.html\ncredits-08c-report-sent.dc.html\ncredits-08d-home-way-in.dc.html\ncredits-09-states.dc.html\nds\nfile-printer-01-prepare-one-second.dc.html\nhistory-01-all-prints.dc.html\nhistory-02-project-garage-bracket.dc.html\nhistory-05-ways-in.dc.html\nmain-03-home.dc.html\nmain-08-home-first-run.dc.html\nonboarding-00-welcome.dc.html\nonboarding-01-account-entry.dc.html\nonboarding-v1-01-imported.dc.html\nonboarding-v1-03-sign-in-expired.dc.html\nprefs-02-agent-setup-one-door.dc.html\nprefs-04-agent.dc.html\nprefs-09-account-signed-out.dc.html\nprefs-12-over-prepare.dc.html","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7670eb3e-e047-4e71-8819-fae599d74c89","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:06:22.845Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: printer-conversation-panel-19b\ndescription: Decisions (2026-09-17) for replacing the native Add-printer dialog with the 19b Home printers-column conversation panel driven by the real agent\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 613b3efa-bbf4-455f-a26c-5f5c07391e2c\n  modified: 2026-09-17T17:45:32.002Z\n---\n\nKenneth chose wireframe 19b (Claude Design project d981c5e2-20db-445f-9047-fa9e9a12522e, file \"Orca Printer Setup Wireframes.dc.html\", ids 19b and 19b-add; its CLAUDE.md holds the design rules) on 2026-09-17:\n\n- Home printers column swaps for a conversation panel for both Add (\"+ Add printer\") and Change (a printer's \"Printer settings…\" drops into it).\n- Add flow = open conversation with the REAL agent (not the old PrinterSetupController state machine / direct OpenAI recogniser).\n- Delete the old native PrinterSetupDialog.\n- No agent set up → the same embedded agent-setup page/flow the old dialog used.\n- Keep existing styles; only layout/flow changes.\n\n**Why:** Kenneth expects prompting the agent per context to replace the scripted flow. Reality check given: still needs printer tools (catalog search, network finds, add, access code, edit a saved printer — none exist), a non-persisted Home session with its own prompt/tool set (prompt is hard-coded, registry fixed, sessions persist into the .3mf), and structured cards in the thread (tool results render only as generic rows).\n\n**How to apply:** Check the current branch for progress before assuming any of this is built. Related: [[agent-setup-embedded-in-printer-dialog]], [[add-printer-flow-figma-discrepancy]], [[agent-bridge-phase-5]].\n\n2026-09-18 (printer-agent-tools handoff build): \"Browse the list\" in that handoff is NOT a new in-panel list — Kenneth said it is the existing \"Set it up myself\" link (OrcaSlicer's printer wizard). The model points there when more than three printers fit.\nmemory/first-run-flow-sequence.md:13:- **Home:** first-run state reflects the choices: agent connected and the 500 credits shown once, or the three doors collapsed in the agent column after Just slice; the Printers column lists imported/added/assumed.\nmemory/first-run-value-prop-decisions.md:19:- **After the welcome:** an OrcaSlicer import belongs on a conditional screen right after the door, asked (not silent like the v1 import in `V1Import/`), shown only when an OrcaSlicer folder exists; the same action lives later in Home's Printers column and the add-printer form. Follow-up screens per door: sign-in in the browser then Home with the agent connected; own key and MCP open Preferences › Agent; Just slice goes to Home with the doors collapsed in the agent column. Not yet drawn: Home after Just slice, the assumed-printer chip.\ncanvas.json\ncomp-agent-group-keys.dc.html\ncomp-agent-group-tools.dc.html\ncomp-agent-row-account.dc.html\ncomp-agent-row-provider.dc.html\ncomp-agent-row-tool.dc.html\ncomp-agent-tool-connect.dc.html\ncomp-chat-header.dc.html\ncomp-composer.dc.html\ncomp-pinned-setup-card.dc.html