The same gate when they correct the printer', assumed(band(gate(printer_way), box(TYPED_PRINTER, typed=True, focus=True))), 3, 1),\n384:    A('06-turn-could-not-run', '06 · The free look could not run: stays on the project', prepare(A1, VP_A1, HOOK_ALT, pane(HOOK_HEAD, setup_card(A1_CARD), [opened(FILE), stopped()], band(box(REPLY))), mark=ASSUMED_MARK), 4, 1),\n397:    B('06-prepare-just-slice', '06 · Prepare after Just slice: no agent turn, the assumption stated, the doors', prepare_slice, 6, 1),\n448:            'The printer, in both variants: the one inside a 3MF (the “from the file” chip on the file-printer boards, page Printer & Material Settings), else OrcaSlicer’s printers imported from this computer, else a default the chip marks as assumed and the agent’s first words name. Never a silent default.\\n\\n'\n449:            'Top row: someone who imported OrcaSlicer’s printers. Bottom row: no OrcaSlicer, so the assumed default (03b, drawn once for both variants), the example, and the two doors out. Plates are captured from the real app; the agent’s words are written for these boards, not model output.'}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2e6aa265-6281-414b-bf67-d9c23c9079cb","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:07:20.197Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"38:ASSUMED = 'I’ve assumed a Bambu A1 mini; tell me if it’s something else.'\n39:HOOK_ASSUMED = (ASSUMED + ' This looks like a wall hook, about 45 mm long with one countersunk screw hole, and it fits that printer. Printed the way it sits, '\n41:BENCHY_ASSUMED = (ASSUMED + ' This is 3DBenchy, the little boat people print to test a printer. It’s here so you can see how this works without a file of your own. '\n178:            + text('body-small', 'The printer is an assumption, a Bambu A1 mini. If yours is different, change it in the menu at the top; that list works without the AI service.', '--text-secondary')\n252:ASSUMED_MARK = 'assumed'\n260:def assumed(band_html):\n261:    return prepare(A1, VP_A1, HOOK_ALT, pane(HOOK_HEAD, setup