{"parentUuid":"42d0e857-60b6-4978-89a8-0e23c5d0a323","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfRbdA7Lb21u1JWJd7VZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":949,"cache_read_input_tokens":312960,"output_tokens":2906,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":949,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2906,"cache_read_input_tokens":312960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":949},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2265,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgfRbcsVMFqV45ah4MMeE","requestRef":"0c510a0b-700b-4cc3-91b1-d1ae96d2800a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d3695c3-4a42-417a-be46-e87fbc705f2f","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:15:03.893Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"2d3695c3-4a42-417a-be46-e87fbc705f2f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfRbdA7Lb21u1JWJd7VZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016swjs1bYJUah9FwYV9WuxF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:80]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nsub('page \"On boarding experience\", version 88 (`1793681477-27e8`):', 'page \"On boarding experience\", version 89 (`1793682894-b7bf`):')\nsub(\"\"\"Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\n## The flow after the welcome (version 89)\n\nKenneth approved the full first-run flow on 2026-11-02 (\"Draw them\"); the decision is the memory note `first-run-flow-sequence.md`. Onboarding is a sequence, Welcome → Printers → Home, owned by a controller, and every door on the welcome is a detour that comes back into it. Version 89 adds eight boards in three rows under the welcome row, one row per step, and the flow board beside the welcome row:\n\n| Board | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `first-run-04-welcome-sign-in-waiting` | The welcome after \"Sign in for 500 credits\": the offer card reads \"Finish signing in in your browser\" with a spinner and Cancel; the two free rows and \"Just slice for now\" are dimmed. |\n| `first-run-05-welcome-signed-in` | The card flipped to \"Signed in as kenneth@example.com · 500 credits\" (a placeholder address), the moment before the controller moves to step 2. |\n| `first-run-06-preferences-over-welcome` | Preferences › Agent, modal over the welcome, signed out with the first-month offer, no keys yet, and the Anthropic key being entered. Drawn the way credits board 1a draws it over Home. |\n| `first-run-07-orcaslicer-import` | \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" with two printers and a filament count each, the OrcaSlicer folder path, Import, Start fresh, and Back. |\n| `first-run-08-add-printer` | Step 1 of the add-printer form (copied from board printer-14) on the first-run frame, with Back and \"Skip, use a default\" under it. |\n| `first-run-09-home-after-sign-in` | Home after sign-in and an OrcaSlicer import: an Agent group showing \"JusPrin account · Connected\", 500 credits left and the first-month bar (the credits boards' balance treatment), with a dismiss button because it shows once; the imported printers below. |\n| `first-run-10-home-after-just-slice` | Home after Just slice: \"Set up the agent\" with the three doors collapsed, and the default printer with the \"assumed\" mark (the chip's triangle and word). |\n| `first-run-11-flow` | The three steps as boxes, an arrow from each door to step 2, the four Printers cases, Back, the quit rule, and the two code facts as footnotes. |\n\nBoth code facts on the flow board were checked in the source: the sign-in callback port is `kCloudCallbackPort = 41172` (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/CloudAccount.hpp:40`), and the shell opens Preferences with `ShowModal()` and carries on when it closes (`Shell/ShellController.cpp:1438`). PNGs of all eight boards, plus the flow board in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nThe old onboarding wizard, boards `onboarding-00` to `onboarding-20` with `10a`, `11a` and `19a` (24 boards), contradicts the flow. None was deleted. They moved 9,300 px down to the bottom of the page, under a title and a purple note saying they are superseded by first-run-01 to first-run-11 as of 2026-11-02. Nothing else on the page moved, and the JusPrin v1 welcome-back boards (`onboarding-v1-01` to `03`) stay where they are because the flow uses them.\n\n### Choices I made that the decision did not cover\n\n- **Home has no agent column today.** Boards 09 and 10 put an \"AGENT\" group above \"PRINTERS\" in Home's right column. If Kenneth meant a separate column, these two boards change.\n- **Board 05 keeps the other doors dimmed** until the controller moves on. Whether they come back when the person returns with Back is not decided; I'd expect the free doors to come back, since someone signed in may still add a key.\n- **Board 06 shows the Anthropic key being entered** with the window at the top of the Agent section, not scrolled to the key group; the key form is visible either way.\n- **The words I added:** the import screen's line \"JusPrin copies these printers with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\" (a printer preset carries its connection, per `V1Import.cpp`), the folder path `~/Library/Application Support/OrcaSlicer`, the Home card heading \"JusPrin account · Connected\", and board 10's drop-zone line \"JusPrin slices it for your Bambu Lab A1 mini.\" (the usual line promises the agent, which isn't set up there). The Home printer card's mark reads \"assumed\", the chip's word.\n- **Examples, not data:** the printers (Bambu Lab P1S, Prusa MK4), the filament counts (9 and 5), the default printer (Bambu Lab A1 mini) and the filament swatch colours, which are the only colour literals on the boards.\n- **The add-printer form is brand and model menus, each with a search** (`AddPrinterForm.tsx`), not one search by model; board 08 draws it as merged in f073fdba96.\"\"\")\nsub(\"\"\"- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.\n- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.\n\"\"\", \"\"\"- **Not drawn in the flow:** the Claude Code or Claude Desktop door's Preferences state (06 draws the key door only), Home after a 3MF opened on first launch, the assumed mark on Prepare's printer chip (10 draws it on Home's printer card), the add-printer form's steps 2 and 3, and the welcome after a quit with a finished detour (it looks like 05 without the advance).\n- **The v1 title note** on this page still reads \"(shown after 00, replaces 01–09)\", which names wizard boards. I left it, since the brief was to add one note and move the boards.\n- **Credits board 1a's offer line** reads \"Your own API key stays free.\" where the welcome card reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" Board 06 uses the welcome card's wording.\n\"\"\")\np.write_text(s); print('ok')\nPYEOF\ngrep -n \"1b to 1d\\|not drawn\\|Header shows\" /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md | head","description":"Update the untracked first-run note for version 89"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":949,"cache_read_input_tokens":312960,"output_tokens":2906,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":949,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2906,"cache_read_input_tokens":312960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":949,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":949},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016swjs1bYJUah9FwYV9WuxF":{"command":"python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md'); s = p.read_text()\ndef sub(a, b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a) == 1, a[:80]\n    s = s.replace(a, b)\nsub('page \"On boarding experience\", version 88 (`1793681477-27e8`):', 'page \"On boarding experience\", version 89 (`1793682894-b7bf`):')\nsub(\"\"\"Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\"\"\",\n\"\"\"Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\n## The flow after the welcome (version 89)\n\nKenneth approved the full first-run flow on 2026-11-02 (\"Draw them\"); the decision is the memory note `first-run-flow-sequence.md`. Onboarding is a sequence, Welcome → Printers → Home, owned by a controller, and every door on the welcome is a detour that comes back into it. Version 89 adds eight boards in three rows under the welcome row, one row per step, and the flow board beside the welcome row:\n\n| Board | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `first-run-04-welcome-sign-in-waiting` | The welcome after \"Sign in for 500 credits\": the offer card reads \"Finish signing in in your browser\" with a spinner and Cancel; the two free rows and \"Just slice for now\" are dimmed. |\n| `first-run-05-welcome-signed-in` | The card flipped to \"Signed in as kenneth@example.com · 500 credits\" (a placeholder address), the moment before the controller moves to step 2. |\n| `first-run-06-preferences-over-welcome` | Preferences › Agent, modal over the welcome, signed out with the first-month offer, no keys yet, and the Anthropic key being entered. Drawn the way credits board 1a draws it over Home. |\n| `first-run-07-orcaslicer-import` | \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" with two printers and a filament count each, the OrcaSlicer folder path, Import, Start fresh, and Back. |\n| `first-run-08-add-printer` | Step 1 of the add-printer form (copied from board printer-14) on the first-run frame, with Back and \"Skip, use a default\" under it. |\n| `first-run-09-home-after-sign-in` | Home after sign-in and an OrcaSlicer import: an Agent group showing \"JusPrin account · Connected\", 500 credits left and the first-month bar (the credits boards' balance treatment), with a dismiss button because it shows once; the imported printers below. |\n| `first-run-10-home-after-just-slice` | Home after Just slice: \"Set up the agent\" with the three doors collapsed, and the default printer with the \"assumed\" mark (the chip's triangle and word). |\n| `first-run-11-flow` | The three steps as boxes, an arrow from each door to step 2, the four Printers cases, Back, the quit rule, and the two code facts as footnotes. |\n\nBoth code facts on the flow board were checked in the source: the sign-in callback port is `kCloudCallbackPort = 41172` (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/CloudAccount.hpp:40`), and the shell opens Preferences with `ShowModal()` and carries on when it closes (`Shell/ShellController.cpp:1438`). PNGs of all eight boards, plus the flow board in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.\n\nThe old onboarding wizard, boards `onboarding-00` to `onboarding-20` with `10a`, `11a` and `19a` (24 boards), contradicts the flow. None was deleted. They moved 9,300 px down to the bottom of the page, under a title and a purple note saying they are superseded by first-run-01 to first-run-11 as of 2026-11-02. Nothing else on the page moved, and the JusPrin v1 welcome-back boards (`onboarding-v1-01` to `03`) stay where they are because the flow uses them.\n\n### Choices I made that the decision did not cover\n\n- **Home has no agent column today.** Boards 09 and 10 put an \"AGENT\" group above \"PRINTERS\" in Home's right column. If Kenneth meant a separate column, these two boards change.\n- **Board 05 keeps the other doors dimmed** until the controller moves on. Whether they come back when the person returns with Back is not decided; I'd expect the free doors to come back, since someone signed in may still add a key.\n- **Board 06 shows the Anthropic key being entered** with the window at the top of the Agent section, not scrolled to the key group; the key form is visible either way.\n- **The words I added:** the import screen's line \"JusPrin copies these printers with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\" (a printer preset carries its connection, per `V1Import.cpp`), the folder path `~/Library/Application Support/OrcaSlicer`, the Home card heading \"JusPrin account · Connected\", and board 10's drop-zone line \"JusPrin slices it for your Bambu Lab A1 mini.\" (the usual line promises the agent, which isn't set up there). The Home printer card's mark reads \"assumed\", the chip's word.\n- **Examples, not data:** the printers (Bambu Lab P1S, Prusa MK4), the filament counts (9 and 5), the default printer (Bambu Lab A1 mini) and the filament swatch colours, which are the only colour literals on the boards.\n- **The add-printer form is brand and model menus, each with a search** (`AddPrinterForm.tsx`), not one search by model; board 08 draws it as merged in f073fdba96.\"\"\")\nsub(\"\"\"- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.\n- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.\n\"\"\", \"\"\"- **Not drawn in the flow:** the Claude Code or Claude Desktop door's Preferences state (06 draws the key door only), Home after a 3MF opened on first launch, the assumed mark on Prepare's printer chip (10 draws it on Home's printer card), the add-printer form's steps 2 and 3, and the welcome after a quit with a finished detour (it looks like 05 without the advance).\n- **The v1 title note** on this page still reads \"(shown after 00, replaces 01–09)\", which names wizard boards. I left it, since the brief was to add one note and move the boards.\n- **Credits board 1a's offer line** reads \"Your own API key stays free.\" where the welcome card reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" Board 06 uses the welcome card's wording.\n\"\"\")\np.write_text(s); print('ok')\nPYEOF\ngrep -n \"1b to 1d\\|not drawn\\|Header shows\" /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md | head","description":"Update the untracked first-run note for version 89"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgfRbcsVMFqV45ah4MMeE","requestRef":"0c510a0b-700b-4cc3-91b1-d1ae96d2800a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ec02ca25-2042-45f8-816f-744df2837245","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:15:26.347Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"ec02ca25-2042-45f8-816f-744df2837245","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3dbd4941-397f-4f1f-b100-534960d73c43","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016swjs1bYJUah9FwYV9WuxF","type":"tool_result","content":"ok","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cacbdde1-a008-4917-bd4f-9d755b745c6d","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:15:26.729Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"ok","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":6,"oldLines":7,"newStart":6,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," ## What is on the canvas now"," ","-The JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 88 (`1793681477-27e8`):","+The JusPrin v2 canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), page \"On boarding experience\", version 89 (`1793682894-b7bf`):"," "," | Board | What it shows |"," | --- | --- |"]},{"oldStart":14,"oldLines":7,"newStart":14,"newLines":35,"lines":[" | `first-run-welcome-02-clip-final-frame` | The same screen with the clip's final frame: the clean boat in the thumbnail, a green check, \"Sliced · ready · 1 h 34 min · 34 g\", and the sliced boat on the plate. |"," | `first-run-welcome-03-clip-storyboard` | The four beats with their captions and timings, a note on which parts are placeholders, and the CC BY 2.0 credit for both photos. Beat 4 is shown with the bar at 68 %, since the final frame is on 02. |"," ","-Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision and what is not drawn. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.","+Two canvas notes sit beside them: a title, and a purple note with the decision. PNGs of all three boards, plus board 01 in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.","+","+## The flow after the welcome (version 89)","+","+Kenneth approved the full first-run flow on 2026-11-02 (\"Draw them\"); the decision is the memory note `first-run-flow-sequence.md`. Onboarding is a sequence, Welcome → Printers → Home, owned by a controller, and every door on the welcome is a detour that comes back into it. Version 89 adds eight boards in three rows under the welcome row, one row per step, and the flow board beside the welcome row:","+","+| Board | What it shows |","+| --- | --- |","+| `first-run-04-welcome-sign-in-waiting` | The welcome after \"Sign in for 500 credits\": the offer card reads \"Finish signing in in your browser\" with a spinner and Cancel; the two free rows and \"Just slice for now\" are dimmed. |","+| `first-run-05-welcome-signed-in` | The card flipped to \"Signed in as kenneth@example.com · 500 credits\" (a placeholder address), the moment before the controller moves to step 2. |","+| `first-run-06-preferences-over-welcome` | Preferences › Agent, modal over the welcome, signed out with the first-month offer, no keys yet, and the Anthropic key being entered. Drawn the way credits board 1a draws it over Home. |","+| `first-run-07-orcaslicer-import` | \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" with two printers and a filament count each, the OrcaSlicer folder path, Import, Start fresh, and Back. |","+| `first-run-08-add-printer` | Step 1 of the add-printer form (copied from board printer-14) on the first-run frame, with Back and \"Skip, use a default\" under it. |","+| `first-run-09-home-after-sign-in` | Home after sign-in and an OrcaSlicer import: an Agent group showing \"JusPrin account · Connected\", 500 credits left and the first-month bar (the credits boards' balance treatment), with a dismiss button because it shows once; the imported printers below. |","+| `first-run-10-home-after-just-slice` | Home after Just slice: \"Set up the agent\" with the three doors collapsed, and the default printer with the \"assumed\" mark (the chip's triangle and word). |","+| `first-run-11-flow` | The three steps as boxes, an arrow from each door to step 2, the four Printers cases, Back, the quit rule, and the two code facts as footnotes. |","+","+Both code facts on the flow board were checked in the source: the sign-in callback port is `kCloudCallbackPort = 41172` (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/CloudAccount.hpp:40`), and the shell opens Preferences with `ShowModal()` and carries on when it closes (`Shell/ShellController.cpp:1438`). PNGs of all eight boards, plus the flow board in dark, are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`.","+","+The old onboarding wizard, boards `onboarding-00` to `onboarding-20` with `10a`, `11a` and `19a` (24 boards), contradicts the flow. None was deleted. They moved 9,300 px down to the bottom of the page, under a title and a purple note saying they are superseded by first-run-01 to first-run-11 as of 2026-11-02. Nothing else on the page moved, and the JusPrin v1 welcome-back boards (`onboarding-v1-01` to `03`) stay where they are because the flow uses them.","+","+### Choices I made that the decision did not cover","+","+- **Home has no agent column today.** Boards 09 and 10 put an \"AGENT\" group above \"PRINTERS\" in Home's right column. If Kenneth meant a separate column, these two boards change.","+- **Board 05 keeps the other doors dimmed** until the controller moves on. Whether they come back when the person returns with Back is not decided; I'd expect the free doors to come back, since someone signed in may still add a key.","+- **Board 06 shows the Anthropic key being entered** with the window at the top of the Agent section, not scrolled to the key group; the key form is visible either way.","+- **The words I added:** the import screen's line \"JusPrin copies these printers with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.\" (a printer preset carries its connection, per `V1Import.cpp`), the folder path `~/Library/Application Support/OrcaSlicer`, the Home card heading \"JusPrin account · Connected\", and board 10's drop-zone line \"JusPrin slices it for your Bambu Lab A1 mini.\" (the usual line promises the agent, which isn't set up there). The Home printer card's mark reads \"assumed\", the chip's word.","+- **Examples, not data:** the printers (Bambu Lab P1S, Prusa MK4), the filament counts (9 and 5), the default printer (Bambu Lab A1 mini) and the filament swatch colours, which are the only colour literals on the boards.","+- **The add-printer form is brand and model menus, each with a search** (`AddPrinterForm.tsx`), not one search by model; board 08 draws it as merged in f073fdba96."," "," The welcome screen fills the whole window with no shell chrome. Version 88 (Kenneth's review, same evening) removed the \"JusPrin › Agent\" header with \"Agent not connected\" and the footer sentence \"Slicing works without an account. The agent needs one, or your own API key.\", because the door rows already show the costs. In their place the JusPrin lockup sits top-left as a corner anchor: the original artwork `resources/jusprin/overlay/images/OrcaSlicer_horizontal_light.svg` (the `_dark` file in dark mode), drawn 43 px tall so it is 120 px wide, the design system's minimum, at space-24 from the left and space-16 from the top. The content is centred in the full 800 px window and the clip is unchanged. The reference render was `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/tagline/logo-d-corner-lockup.png`; the new board 01 matches its layout. The storyboard board 03 has no lockup."," "]},{"oldStart":35,"oldLines":8,"newStart":63,"newLines":9,"lines":[" ## What I left out, and the gaps"," "," - **Display type size.** The reference animatic drew the two settings, the \"Slicing NN%\" line and the bar's label at 36 to 48 px. The type scale's largest token is page-title (24 px), so the boards use that, and the settings read smaller than in the reference. If Kenneth wants the reference size, the token file needs a display size first.","-- **After the doors.** Nothing new was decided, and my variant boards didn't match the new doors' wording, so none were reused. The existing board `credits-01a-agent-setup` on the same page already shows Preferences › Agent over Home on first launch. I did not check its offer wording against the new card's \"Then paid, or your own key.\" The Agent setup boards on the \"Agent setup & Preferences\" page (`prefs-02-agent-setup-one-door`, `prefs-12-over-prepare`) cover the setup flow itself.","-- **\"Just slice for now\" to Home.** No board shows Home after it. The existing `main-08-home-first-run` on the Main Page is the nearest. No board on the canvas now shows the printer chip marked as assumed, which was on withdrawn board A-03b. The file-printer boards on \"Printer & Material Settings\" cover the \"from the file\" case.","+- **Not drawn in the flow:** the Claude Code or Claude Desktop door's Preferences state (06 draws the key door only), Home after a 3MF opened on first launch, the assumed mark on Prepare's printer chip (10 draws it on Home's printer card), the add-printer form's steps 2 and 3, and the welcome after a quit with a finished detour (it looks like 05 without the advance).","+- **The v1 title note** on this page still reads \"(shown after 00, replaces 01–09)\", which names wizard boards. I left it, since the brief was to add one note and move the boards.","+- **Credits board 1a's offer line** reads \"Your own API key stays free.\" where the welcome card reads \"Then paid, or your own key.\" Board 06 uses the welcome card's wording."," - **The clip in motion.** The canvas holds still frames only. The moving reference is `design-captures/value-prop-2026-11/animatic/animatic-stringing.mp4`."," "," ## Findings from the variant work that still apply"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ec02ca25-2042-45f8-816f-744df2837245","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
