{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","id":"05983469-225e-49bf-8e76-bfb24c1a91ad","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:15:37.706Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"4e19310124f64a883ecf3063322346e3d7bfbf2b631baea78aefde90323b69db","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"839312dc-b008-4a8f-868c-1fef94873b5b","keep":236,"tail":["f3bb1b319145e5b2f68c7c51021e95eea78ce499cb232e007987e993333626bd","b30c94dfc88ab6ade1a80b91278111aa7e23da6aa98ec2f39168d96e6f7fd007","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",238,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"33994904e8f7917b2209bdadc8383b288dade9b9091bd3f516ec6b44214165d8"}
{"parentUuid":"1fc1158e-4f4e-423a-b6dd-a33b6be6ceb8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfReLLQQ9UoZyjEYS21Z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I published version 89 of the JusPrin v2 canvas (version id `1793682894-b7bf`), labelled \"First launch: the full flow, wizard superseded\". It adds eight boards to the \"On boarding experience\" page and moves the 24 old wizard boards to the bottom of the page under a note saying they are superseded. Welcome boards 01–03 are unchanged. Nothing is committed, and I sent you the flow board and board 07.\n\n**New boards.** They sit in three rows under the welcome, one row per step. The flow board sits beside the welcome row.\n- **04:** the welcome while sign-in finishes in the browser. The card reads \"Finish signing in in your browser\" with a Cancel link, and the other doors are dimmed.\n- **05:** the welcome just before step 2, with the card reading \"Signed in as kenneth@example.com · 500 credits\".\n- **06:** Preferences › Agent opened over the welcome. It is signed out, shows the first-month offer, and has an Anthropic key being entered.\n- **07:** \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\", with two printers and a filament count for each, plus Import, Start fresh and Back.\n- **08:** the add-printer form, copied from board printer-14, with Back and \"Skip, use a default\".\n- **09:** Home after signing in and importing from OrcaSlicer. It shows the connected account and the 500-credit balance once, and the imported printers.\n- **10:** Home after \"Just slice for now\". The three doors are collapsed under \"Set up the agent\", and the default printer has the \"assumed\" mark.\n- **11:** the flow board, 1600 × 960. It shows the three steps, an arrow from each door to step 2, the four printer cases, Back, and the rule for quitting before Home. The two code facts are footnotes. I checked both in the code:\n  - The sign-in callback port is fixed at 41172 (`Agent/CloudAccount.hpp:40`).\n  - Preferences opens with `ShowModal()` (`Shell/ShellController.cpp:1438`).\n\n**The old wizard.** Boards `onboarding-00` to `onboarding-20`, plus 10a, 11a and 19a, moved 9,300 px down. None was deleted, and nothing else on the page moved.\n\n**Choices the decision didn't cover.** Each is listed in the note:\n- **Agent group on Home:** Home has no agent column today. Boards 09 and 10 put an \"AGENT\" group above \"PRINTERS\" in Home's right column. If Kenneth meant a separate column, those two boards change.\n- **Dimmed doors on 05:** the other doors stay dimmed until the app moves to step 2. Whether they come back after Back is undecided.\n- **Wording I added:**\n  - The import screen's sentence about what gets copied, including printer connections. A printer preset carries its connection, according to `V1Import.cpp`.\n  - The OrcaSlicer folder path.\n  - The \"JusPrin account · Connected\" heading.\n  - Board 10's drop-zone line, \"JusPrin slices it for your Bambu Lab A1 mini.\" The usual line promises the agent, which isn't set up there.\n- **Examples, not real data:** the printers, the filament counts, the default printer (a Bambu Lab A1 mini) and the filament colours.\n- **The add-printer form:** the code uses brand and model menus, each with a search box, not a single search by model. Board 08 draws it as built.\n\n**Not drawn:**\n- Preferences for the Claude Code or Claude Desktop door.\n- Home after a 3MF is opened on first launch.\n- The \"assumed\" mark on the printer chip in Prepare.\n- Steps 2 and 3 of the add-printer form.\n\nThe title note on the JusPrin v1 boards still says \"(shown after 00, replaces 01–09)\", which names wizard boards. I left it alone.\n\nThe PNGs are in `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/`. The note is `first-run-flow-design-2026-11.md` at the repo root."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_read_input_tokens":317790,"output_tokens":1331,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":566,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1331,"cache_read_input_tokens":317790,"cache_creation_input_tokens":566,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":566},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgfReKzKtQZ8gbEQPM6yW","requestRef":"05983469-225e-49bf-8e76-bfb24c1a91ad","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"7356d5b7-dae0-4d4c-a310-2a7b9cfb0a4c","timestamp":"2026-11-03T05:15:48.772Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
