d.md) — Hobby at their original price…; [\"1 credit\"](credit-price-needs-its-unit.md) — confusing alone; \"1 credit a…; [One kind of credit](credits-one-kind-no-ceiling.md) — 2026-11-02 evening: no…; [Credits only](balances-in-credits-only.md) — no message counts on a balance…; [Credits boards](credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages.md) — on their flows' canvas pages…\n- [Chat capture](jusprin-chat-capture-design.md) — every chat kept raw, no opt-out…\n- [Live suite](live-suite-is-part-of-done.md) — model-text changes need it before…\n- [No forcing field](no-required-field-to-force-a-question.md) — when to ask belongs in the prompt.\n- [Rebuild a request](rebuild-wire-request-from-saved-chat.md) — from current-state.json + source.\n- [Reproduce for real](reproduce-on-real-app-not-fakes.md) — a failing fake test is no repro.\n- [Chat keeps its model](chat-keeps-its-model.md) — for now no mid-chat switch; docs…\n- [Show the board](show-the-board-when-asking-kenneth.md) — no bare \"6a\": say what the person…\n- [Board PNGs](render-canvas-boards-with-render-dc.md) — render_dc.py draws dc-imports…\n- [Sign-up reason](sign-up-reason-must-be-prominent.md) — the offer is the headline; the…\n- [Print report placement](print-report-lives-on-history-entry.md) — on the history entry, not in…\n- [AppConfig set trap](appconfig-set-const-char-goes-to-bool.md) — a const char* goes to the bool…\n- [Standard titles](standard-title-answers-instead.md) — 4 of 12 refused, the model…\n- Retired: Retired, Figma gone 2026-10-20: [file](figma-jusprin-v2-file.md), [seats](figma-mcp-view-seat-limit.md), [add printer](add-printer-flow-figma-discrepancy.md); Retired: [in-file agent](drive-figma-in-file-agent-via-chrome.md), [parity](figma-dump-then-measure-parity.md), [header values, superseded](header-menu-values-kenneth-kept.md)\n- [Blank project behind Home](blank-project-behind-home-inherited.md) — inherited; Kenneth's rule: save…\n- [Printer suite traps](printer-suite-traps-usage-and-skill-rev.md) — no token log; --prompt-rev skips…\n- First run: [First-run boards](first-run-flow-boards.md) — canvas v93: 01..11 + email door…; [First-run sequence](first-run-flow-sequence.md) — Welcome → Printers → Home; doors…; [First-run proposition](first-run-value-prop-decisions.md) — 2026-11-02: expert help, not…; [Old onboarding review](old-onboarding-boards-review.md) — email code dropped by omission…\n- [New logo](new-logo-soft-serve.md) — 2026-11-03: soft serve first…\n- [allauth 65 upgrade](allauth-65-upgrade.md) — on both masters, staging…\n- [One local server](one-local-server-no-second-stack.md) — tsd-enterprise runs as one…\n- [CLI WebSearch](claude-cli-websearch-differs-from-app.md) — its result demands a Sources list; 4/117 Choices misses; judge needs the whole result, history keeps searches.\n- [Gmail code card](gmail-code-card-undocumented.md) — no card for our code email; no Google rule; self-sent confound; stopped.\n- [Full syndicate](jusprin-full-syndicate-decision.md) — own accounts; v2 = syndicate jusprinv2 on jusprinv2.obico.io, apart from v1; theme release via worktree build…\n</system-reminder>\n"},{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); first-run-flow = local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle, started by first-run-flow). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d\" from-name=\"Build the first-run flow on top of the credits branch\">\nKenneth asks whether the first-run design decided to host some of its pages in the cloud, and if so, why.\n\nHis words: \"ask them if we have made the decisions to host some of the pages in the cloud, and if so, the justifications\".\n\n\"In the cloud\" here means pages served by the gateway website (JusPrin 2's host is now jusprinv2.obico.io, staging jusprinv2-stg.obico.io) and shown in the person's web browser, as opposed to screens built into the desktop app (the Home and Agent pages bundled in the app). Example: the Google sign-in, the OAuth authorize page, any \"you're signed in, return to the app\" page.\n\nPlease answer, for each first-run board you designed (Kenneth refers to them as 01-16; say if your boards are numbered differently):\n1. Is the board in the app, or a web page served by the gateway?\n2. For each web page: was that a decision, who made it (quote Kenneth's words and where they are, if he agreed to it), and what the stated justification was. If it was never decided, but just assumed or inherited from how the app already signs in, say so plainly.\n\nKeep it short: a list, one line per board, then the justifications. Don't change the canvas.\n</cross-session-message>"}]}}
