{"parentUuid":"5ef836af-3ed6-4660-af5d-30e7e55ab379","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFW1F5ZXWbR7Tn4PLKh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":341544,"output_tokens":1002,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":84},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1002,"cache_read_input_tokens":341544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7328,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgjFVzzTLB6S3hy9Rs7Ed","requestRef":"1c5828a2-9cbc-4485-837d-3e939e2251b5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"10b14933-b68e-40cd-af94-c5ffd9a19d7f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:45:06.990Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"10b14933-b68e-40cd-af94-c5ffd9a19d7f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFW1F5ZXWbR7Tn4PLKh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The first-run design never decided to host any page in the cloud. The one web page in the flow is the account sign-in, which opens in the person's browser. That was carried over from how the app already signs in, not chosen for onboarding.\n\nMy boards are numbered 01 to 11. Boards 12 to 16 were added after my last publish, version 89, by another session, so I can't speak for them.\n\n**Board by board:**\n- **01 and 02, the welcome screen** (clip at the start, clip's last frame): in the app.\n- **03, the clip's storyboard:** a design note, not a screen.\n- **04, the welcome while sign-in finishes in the browser:** in the app. It shows \"Finish signing in in your browser\". The browser page itself is not drawn on any of my boards.\n- **05, the welcome showing \"Signed in as …\":** in the app.\n- **06, Preferences › Agent over the welcome:** in the app. It is the app's own Preferences window.\n- **07, \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\":** in the app.\n- **08, the add-printer form:** in the app.\n- **09 and 10, Home after signing in and after \"Just slice for now\":** in the app.\n- **11, the flow diagram:** a design note, not a screen.\n\n**The browser sign-in: assumed, not decided.**\n- **Where it comes from:** the app already signed in this way before the first-run work began. Commit ac55c2961a (\"Sign in to a JusPrin account, and bring a JusPrin v1 setup along\", 2026-10-24) built it.\n- **What it does:** the app opens the system browser and runs a standard OAuth sign-in there, with a security extension called PKCE. The server sends the browser back to the app on a fixed local port, 41172 (`src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Agent/CloudAccount.hpp`). The pages the person sees in the browser are the server's sign-in and authorize pages.\n- **The only stated reasoning** is in that file's comments, and it is technical:\n  - The sign-in uses the standard way for desktop apps to get a token through the system browser (RFC 8252).\n  - The port is fixed because OrcaSlicer's local callback server takes a set port rather than one the system picks.\n- **No product reason** is written down for signing in in the browser instead of inside the app.\n- **What the first-run brief said:** \"Sign in for 500 credits: the browser opens.\" That brief was relayed by the pricing session; I have no words from Kenneth himself on it. The first-run decision record says only \"sign-in in the browser then Home with the agent connected\", and gives no reason.\n\n**Not designed anywhere in my boards:** a \"You're signed in, return to the app\" page, or any other gateway page. Whatever the server shows after the browser is sent back to the app was not part of the first-run design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_read_input_tokens":341544,"output_tokens":1002,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":84},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1002,"cache_read_input_tokens":341544,"cache_creation_input_tokens":491,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":491},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgjFVzzTLB6S3hy9Rs7Ed","requestRef":"1c5828a2-9cbc-4485-837d-3e939e2251b5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7034f9a7-f970-49ca-a6d9-47ec6fa58fab","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:45:09.224Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurn