{"parentUuid":"cfc927fd-faef-487b-93ca-3e9cec30ab7c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6ddd4fe3-2020-42b5-8d67-2ce66edb3f4e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KQf1u8xUwEgCLdeZySGMQn","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: first-run-flow-sequence\ndescription: \"Kenneth's 2026-11-02 first-run flow after the welcome: a sequence Welcome → Printers → Home owned by a controller, with the agent doors as detours that return (sign-in waits on the card, Preferences closes back, Just slice skips the detour not the sequence); Printers step imports OrcaSlicer or adds/assumes a printer; what the canvas still lacks.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nDecided 2026-11-02, late, after Kenneth asked how Preferences gets back to the OrcaSlicer import and how \"Just slice for now\" returns to onboarding (\"I don't think you have thought through\").\n\n- **Shape:** onboarding is a sequence, Welcome → Printers → Home. A controller owns the step. Preferences (a modal `PreferencesWindow`, returns on close) and the browser sign-in (loopback callback on port 41172, polled by `CloudSignIn::poll()`) are detours off step 1; when one finishes the controller advances. Nothing a detour does strands the person outside the sequence.\n- **Welcome doors:** Sign in → browser; the card shows \"Finish signing in in your browser\" with Cancel, other doors dimmed; on the callback the card flips to \"Signed in as … · 500 credits\", then step 2. Own key / MCP → Preferences › Agent opens modal on that section; saving a verified key or Done closes it and advances; closing unfinished returns to the welcome with nothing chosen. Just slice → step 2 at once.\n- **Printers step:** the app needs one printer (an empty data folder has none). OrcaSlicer folder found → \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" with Import (copies user presets like `V1Import`, but asked, not silent) and Start fresh. JusPrin v1 found → step skipped, the existing welcome-back window shows over Home. Neither → the add-printer form with \"Skip, use a default\", which installs the default and marks the chip assumed. Back returns to the welcome; finished detours stay done. A 3MF opened on first launch still shows the welcome, then skips this step (\"from the file\").\n- **Home:** first-run state reflects the choices: agent connected and the 500 credits shown once, or the three doors collapsed in the agent column after Just slice; the Printers column lists imported/added/assumed.\n- **Quit mid-flow:** done is marked only when Home is reached; next launch shows the welcome again with finished detours reflected.\n\n**Why:** the first design named destinations and skipped transitions; Kenneth wants every door to come back into one flow.\n\n**How to apply:** build the controller first, then the screens. Drawn on the canvas in version 89 (2026-11-02) as first-run-04 to first-run-11 (11 is the flow board); the old wizard boards onboarding-00 to 20 sit at the bottom of the page under a superseded note. Choices the decision didn't cover, made by the design session and not ruled: an \"AGENT\" group above \"PRINTERS\" in Home's right column (boards 09, 10; if Kenneth meant a separate column, they change); the other doors stay dimmed on the signed-in card until the controller moves on, and whether they come back after Back is undecided. Related: [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]], [[first-run-flow-boards]], [[agent-setup-one-flow-decisions]].\n\n**Built 2026-11-03** on `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` (four commits ending 914e48b77f, off `credits-integration-2026-11`, not pushed, no PR; worktree `.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35`, owned by session local_cea7b182). Tests and the shell harness (`--fresh-example`, 40 checks) pass. Checked in the built app: welcome, sign-in door, add-printer form. Not run there: own-key, MCP, Just slice, Import, Skip, Home. Live checks left as of 2026-11-03 morning: own key (Preferences opens on Agent; closing unfinished leaves the welcome); Claude Code/Desktop (Done moves to Printers; send `shell_action {action:'close', done:'tool'}` from the Preferences page instead of really connecting, which writes the real Claude config); Just slice → import step, then Back, Start fresh, and \"Skip, use a default\" (Home with the doors and an assumed Generic Klipper); Import → Home with the imported printers. The import step shows only when a folder `OrcaSlicer` sits next to the data folder (`--datadir X/JusPrin` → `X/OrcaSlicer` with `user/`, `system/` and an `OrcaSlicer.conf` holding only `app.preset_folder`). Not built: a 3MF opened on first launch skipping Printers. The clip is the placeholder animatic at `resources/jusprin/welcome/welcome-clip.mp4`; CC BY credits sit in a \"Photo credits\" disclosure under the clip, not the About box. Never press \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on Kenneth's Mac during a check: the browser is signed in and it completes by itself.\n\n**2026-11-03 afternoon:** the sign-in door is now Google + email (code or password), with an import result screen and the v1 line; see [[old-onboarding-boards-review]] for commits, tests and gaps. App branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` (3df2ed9c24), gateway branch `claude/email-sign-in` in tsd-enterprise (81efc6fd43). Not pushed.\ncalibration-generators-replace-project.md\nfirst-run-flow-sequence.md\nfirst-run-flow-boards.md\nfirst-run-value-prop-decisions.md\npricing-brainstorm-corrections.md\nprinter-live-harness-lessons.md\nprompt-principles-vs-state-channels.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1025975b-9cf3-4541-8a4d-fb1710d0f66d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:24:57.992Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: first-run-flow-sequence\ndescription: \"Kenneth's 2026-11-02 first-run flow after the welcome: a sequence Welcome → Printers → Home owned by a controller, with the agent doors as detours that return (sign-in waits on the card, Preferences closes back, Just slice skips the detour not the sequence); Printers step imports OrcaSlicer or adds/assumes a printer; what the canvas still lacks.\"\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nDecided 2026-11-02, late, after Kenneth asked how Preferences gets back to the OrcaSlicer import and how \"Just slice for now\" returns to onboarding (\"I don't think you have thought through\").\n\n- **Shape:** onboarding is a sequence, Welcome → Printers → Home. A controller owns the step. Preferences (a modal `PreferencesWindow`, returns on close) and the browser sign-in (loopback callback on port 41172, polled by `CloudSignIn::poll()`) are detours off step 1; when one finishes the controller advances. Nothing a detour does strands the person outside the sequence.\n- **Welcome doors:** Sign in → browser; the card shows \"Finish signing in in your browser\" with Cancel, other doors dimmed; on the callback the card flips to \"Signed in as … · 500 credits\", then step 2. Own key / MCP → Preferences › Agent opens modal on that section; saving a verified key or Done closes it and advances; closing unfinished returns to the welcome with nothing chosen. Just slice → step 2 at once.\n- **Printers step:** the app needs one printer (an empty data folder has none). OrcaSlicer folder found → \"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\" with Import (copies user presets like `V1Import`, but asked, not silent) and Start fresh. JusPrin v1 found → step skipped, the existing welcome-back window shows over Home. Neither → the add-printer form with \"Skip, use a default\", which installs the default and marks the chip assumed. Back returns to the welcome; finished detours stay done. A 3MF opened on first launch still shows the welcome, then skips this step (\"from the file\").\n- **Home:** first-run state reflects the choices: agent connected and the 500 credits shown once, or the three doors collapsed in the agent column after Just slice; the Printers column lists imported/added/assumed.\n- **Quit mid-flow:** done is marked only when Home is reached; next launch shows the welcome again with finished detours