{"parentUuid":"ff1ae511-5448-4f90-937d-3ae39986463d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6ddd4fe3-2020-42b5-8d67-2ce66edb3f4e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XLtFbqVuLjmKinHWA58vAk","type":"tool_result","content":"3:> **2026-10-20: Figma is retired and out of date.** The two Claude artifacts are now the up-to-date JusPrin\n7:> `project/ds/jusprin/` (tokens and component styles): change both artifacts together. `tools/composer/` holds\n9:> board's height in its file and in `canvas.json`; `build_filament_step.py` draws the Add-a-printer step-3 boards and their spec files, `measure_sheets.py` measures their sheet heights with headless Chrome). Before publishing to either artifact, do a plain `read` of its url: a publish after only `path` reads is refused as \"haven't viewed the latest version\". The Figma re-sync steps below are kept as history.\n12:This folder keeps what is needed to re-sync two Claude artifacts with the Figma file \"JusPrin v2\"\n15:- Canvas \"JusPrin v2\": https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v\n16:- JusPrin Design System: https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL\n57:6. Publish only the changed files to the same artifact URLs, check the live pages, then replace `published/`.\n67:The artifact service keeps every published version and the Artifact tool can copy a file from an earlier version by its id (`files: {\"<path>\": {\"artifact\": \"<url>\", \"path\": \"<path>\", \"ver\": \"<id>\"}}`), so a rollback is one publish from the version named here, with no copy made by hand. It cannot list versions, which is why they are written down here before each publish.\n74:- Prepare header gear menu (Kenneth, 2026-10-27, decided in a side session): on the current canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), before `1793143270-86c0`, after `1793143597-61ea`, label \"Prepare header gear menu (2026-10-27)\". New board `main-10-prepare-header-gear-menu.dc.html` (Main Page, under home-first-run) with an orange sticky `prepare-header-open-item` beside it; `prefs-13-entry-points.dc.html` \"In a project\" stage redrawn with the gear. Work copies in `work-gear-menu/`. The full-screen Prepare boards still draw the ⋯ button; not swept.\n86:`work-file-printer/render/`. Canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ: before 1793188946-1f2e,\n107:copies and the render in `work-chat-trust/`. Canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ: before\n118:https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ: before 1793509143-618e, after 1793589476-97cc (version 54), label \"Add\n161:https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ before 1793743067-978a, after 1793744174-5990 (version 93), label \"First-run\n---\nname: first-run-flow-boards\ndescription: \"First-launch boards on the canvas onboarding page: variants A/B withdrawn 2026-11-02; Kenneth's one split welcome screen drawn as first-run-welcome-01..03 (version 87; no chrome + corner lockup in 88; the flow 04-11 in 89); builder build_first_run_page.py.\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438\n  modified: 2026-11-03T03:48:37.053Z\n---\n\n2026-11-02: the no-wizard variants A and B (`first-run-a-*`, `first-run-b-*`) were withdrawn at Kenneth's request and removed in canvas version 87. Nothing else on the page had moved for them. In their place, `first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1`, `-02-clip-final-frame` and `-03-clip-storyboard` draw the welcome screen from [[first-run-value-prop-decisions]]. Version 88 made it a full-window screen with no shell header or footer and the JusPrin lockup in the top-left corner (43 px tall, space-24/space-16), Kenneth's \"Lockup\" choice. They are built by `figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`.\n\nGaps at the time: the type scale has no display size for the clip's big settings (page-title is used); there are no boards after \"Just slice for now\"; and nothing on the canvas now shows the \"assumed\" printer chip.\n\nFacts from the variant work that still apply: `printer_from_file` (`!is_named_printer`) would label an assumed default \"from the file\"; an empty data folder has no printers; the project chat can't add a printer; Home has no agent pane.\n\n**Why:** later sessions may find references to A/B and assume they are current.\n\n**How to apply:** treat A/B as history. Build the first launch from the welcome boards and the decision memory. Related: [[jusprin-claude-design-system-artifact]], [[credits-boards-live-on-flow-pages]].\n\n**2026-11-03, version 93 (1793744174-5990), canvas ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ:** the boards now draw the built sign-in door. 01/02: Continue with Google, \"or\", email field + Continue with email, Terms line; 04: the browser-wait card (\"Nothing happened? Open the browser again\", \"Use an email code instead\"); 05: \"Signed in as alex@example.com · 500 credits\"; 10: Home's \"Set up the agent\" with the same door. New row y 7100: 12 email choice (Email me a 6-digit code, or password + Sign in), 13 wrong password, 14 typing the code, 15 wrong code, 16 code no longer works. Rows 07-08 and 09-10 and the superseded wizard moved down 940. The free doors dim only once signed in. Work copy `figma-mirror/work-first-run-door/`. Home's narrow column truncates the email field placeholder (\"you@exar\") — the app has the same CSS, so it likely looks the same there.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e06697c9-2589-41e2-96dd-ffa412329c8a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:25:21.394Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"3:> **2026-10-20: Figma is retired and out of date.** The two Claude artifacts are now the up-to-date JusPrin\n7:> `project/ds/jusprin/` (tokens and component styles): change both artifacts together. `tools/composer/` holds\n9:> board's height in its file and in `canvas.json`; `build_filament_step.py` draws the Add-a-printer step-3 boards and their spec files, `measure_sheets.py` measures their sheet heights with headless Chrome). Before publishing to either artifact, do a plain `read` of its url: a publish after only `path` reads is refused as \"haven't viewed the latest version\". The Figma re-sync steps below are kept as history.\n12:This folder keeps what is needed to re-sync two Claude artifacts with the Figma file \"JusPrin v2\"\n15:- Canvas \"JusPrin v2\": https://claude.ai/artifact/VCEppdwfT7v32W4beUxL1v\n16:- JusPrin Design System: https://claude.ai/artifact/3zgiix8rAw3rXextQnR5UL\n57:6. Publish only the changed files to the same artifact URLs, check the live pages, then replace `published/`.\n67:The artifact service keeps every published version and the Artifact tool can copy a file from an earlier version by its id (`files: {\"<path>\": {\"artifact\": \"<url>\", \"path\": \"<path>\", \"ver\": \"<id>\"}}`), so a rollback is one publish from the version named here, with no copy made by hand. It cannot list versions, which is why they are written down here before each publish.\n74:- Prepare header gear menu (Kenneth, 2026-10-27, decided in a side session): on the current canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ), before `1793143270-86c0`, after `1793143597-61ea`, label \"Prepare header gear menu (2026-10-27)\". New board `main-10-prepare-header-gear-menu.dc.html` (Main Page, under home-first-run) with an orange sticky `prepare-header-open-item` beside it; `prefs-13-entry-points.dc.html` \"In a project\" stage redrawn with the gear. Work copies in `work-gear-menu/`. The full-screen Prepare boards still draw the ⋯ button; not swept.\n86:`work-file-printer/render/`. Canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ: before 1793188946-1f2e,\n107:copies and the render in `work-chat-trust/`. Canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ: before\n118:https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ: before 1793509143-618e, after 1793589476-97cc (version 54), label \"Add\n161:https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ before 1793743067-978a, after 1793744174