4Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"e7498b2f-c7c4-4b44-a54f-b4aae2f9a164","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6ddd4fe3-2020-42b5-8d67-2ce66edb3f4e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011H3zdxcWbchVeQNXMkECY9","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: new-logo-soft-serve\ndescription: \"2026-11-03 Kenneth picked a new JusPrin logo: layered soft-serve cone first, layered J second; old star-and-ring mark to be replaced after he reviews the file list\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 0cc17b3e-3060-410c-bea9-62fa336c00c6\n  modified: 2026-11-04T01:37:48.323Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-03 Kenneth said he likes the brand colours and type but not the logo (the purple four-point star crossing an open ring). Concepts are on the Claude Design canvas \"JusPrin Logo Concepts\" (https://claude.ai/artifact/Qroq8EdcQDSPkCAyFceDtQ). His words: \"go with the Soft serve idea, with the layered j idea as the 2nd option.\"\n\n- First choice: soft serve: a swirl of four stacked rounded layers on a waffle cone, curl on top (board FSoftServe.dc.html).\n- Second choice: layered J: a \"J\" built from stacked rounded bars, top bar still being laid down with a dot (board LayerJ.dc.html).\n- He asked for a list of every place the current logo lives and said: \"don't replace them just yet until I review the list.\" He then approved the list; the swap that followed is commit 0cda0677eb.\n- Name next to the cone: he picked \"Printing the dot\" (board NameOptions.dc.html, row C): the bold name cut into print layers (7 for capitals, 5 for small letters), with a small nozzle above the i whose dot is the last layer. Small-size behaviour (24 px) was not yet checked.\n- 2026-11-03: committed as 0cda0677eb on jusprin-newui (main checkout, not pushed); Kenneth builds and tests it himself. Generator: src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Brand/brand_logo.py (needs skia-pathops + fonttools). Kenneth tested the build: \"it looks good\". Same day the design system (v60: six Logos assets, Logos README, README Logo section, cover art redrawn as print layers) and the v2 canvas (v97: new lockup ids 1877578c…/47e844c7… in 15 first-run boards) were switched. Splash timing measured on this Mac, 3 warm launches: on screen 0.06–0.73 s, appearing 1.6–7.9 s after launch. Kenneth then decided: \"Leave splash as is\" (no redesign, no Windows measurement). Design system v61 added the layered J as three alternate files (jusprin-alt-layered-j{,-ink,-white}.svg) with a \"Second choice\" section in the Logos README. Kenneth asked to delete the concepts canvas; the delete tool could not get his confirmation in this session, so it was not deleted; Kenneth then chose to keep it for now.\n\n**Why:** the old mark was \"supplied by the user\" and docs say never redraw it; those rules (resources/jusprin/README.md, agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md, the design system's Logos README) must change with the swap.\n\n**How to apply:** don't touch logo files until Kenneth approves the list. 0cda0677eb added overlays for the Dock icon and OrcaSlicer.svg. By the 2026-11-03 code reading, three places still show OrcaSlicer's whale: resources/images/OrcaSlicer.png (Linux desktop integration, DesktopIntegrationDialog.cpp), resources/images/OrcaSlicer_192px.png read by full path in SendSystemInfoDialog.cpp (skips the overlay), and resources/web/image/logo.png (old web home and setup guide pages; unknown whether JusPrin still shows them). Not checked: the Obico website, app-store listings, emails, JusPrin Cloud web pages, other repositories. See [[jusprin-rebrand-seams]].\nallauth-0.63.6-to-65.21.1-changes.md\nallauth-65-1-upgrade.patch\nallauth-65-2-client-ip.patch\nfirst-run-flow-live-checks-left.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f7d0391c-2639-4d44-ab03-440cbe0e3f36","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:26:16.344Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: new-logo-soft-serve\ndescription: \"2026-11-03 Kenneth picked a new JusPrin logo: layered soft-serve cone first, layered J second; old star-and-ring mark to be replaced after he reviews the file list\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 0cc17b3e-3060-410c-bea9-62fa336c00c6\n  modified: 2026-11-04T01:37:48.323Z\n---\n\nOn 2026-11-03 Kenneth said he likes the brand colours and type but not the logo (the purple four-point star crossing an open ring). Concepts are on the Claude Design canvas \"JusPrin Logo Concepts\" (https://claude.ai/artifact/Qroq8EdcQDSPkCAyFceDtQ). His words: \"go with the Soft serve idea, with the layered j idea as the 2nd option.\"\n\n- First choice: soft serve: a swirl of four stacked rounded layers on a waffle cone, curl on top (board FSoftServe.dc.html).\n- Second choice: layered J: a \"J\" built from stacked rounded bars, top bar still being laid down with a dot (board LayerJ.dc.html).\n- He asked for a list of every place the current logo lives and said: \"don't replace them just yet until I review the list.\" He then approved the list; the swap that followed is commit 0cda0677eb.\n- Name next to the cone: he picked \"Printing the dot\" (board NameOptions.dc.html, row C): the bold name cut into print layers (7 for capitals, 5 for small letters), with a small nozzle above the i whose dot is the last layer. Small-size behaviour (24 px) was not yet checked.\n- 2026-11-03: committed as 0cda0677eb on jusprin-newui (main checkout, not pushed); Kenneth builds and tests it himself. Generator: src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Brand/brand_logo.py (needs skia-pathops + fonttools). Kenneth tested the build: \"it looks good\". Same day the design system (v60: six Logos assets, Logos README, README Logo section, cover art redrawn as print layers) and the v2 canvas (v97: new lockup ids 1877578c…/47e844c7… in 15 first-run boards) were switched. Splash timing measured on this Mac, 3 warm launches: on screen 0.06–0.73 s, appearing 1.6–7.9 s after launch. Kenneth then decided: \"Leave splash as is\" (no redesign, no Windows measurement). Design system v61 added the layered J as three alternate files (jusprin-alt-layered-j{,-ink,-white}.svg) with a \"Second choice\" section in the Logos README. Kenneth asked to delete the concepts canvas; the delete tool could not get his confirmation in this session, so it was not deleted; Kenneth then chose to keep it for now.\n\n**Why:** the old mark was \"supplied by the user\" and docs say never redraw it; those rules (resources/jusprin/README.md, agent-docs/jusprin/design-system.md, the design system's Logos README) must change with the swap.\n\n**How to apply:** don't touch logo files until Kenneth approves the list. 0cda0677eb added overlays for the Dock icon and OrcaSlicer.svg. By the 2026-11-03 code reading, three places still show OrcaSlicer's whale: resources/images/OrcaSlicer.png (Linux desktop integration, DesktopIntegrationDialog.cpp), resources/images/OrcaSlicer_192px.png read by full path in SendSystemInfoDialog.cpp (skips the overlay), and resources/web/image/logo.png (old web home and setup guide pages; unknown whether JusPrin still shows them). Not checked: the Obico website, app-store listings, emails, JusPrin Cloud web pages, other repositories. See [[jusprin-rebrand-seams]].\nallauth-0.63.6-to-65.21.1-changes.md\nallauth-65-1-upgrade.patch\nallauth-65-2-client-ip.patch\nfirst-run-flow-live-checks-left.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e7498b2f-c7c4-4b44-a54f-b4aae2f9a164","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
