{"parentUuid":"08f37234-dd53-4d31-9c5b-ffd08fae8d63","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkaFbVuDLSieAPzxW6Jq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2201,"cache_read_input_tokens":250016,"output_tokens":3267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1306},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2201,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3267,"cache_read_input_tokens":250016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2201},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":13123,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgkaFbDmtSFqWdk75wFcY","requestRef":"23d8834c-45e6-485f-bbaf-6f2ce641bc8d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"91a633bf-684a-4486-86a5-7306a3846aba","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:31:42.716Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"91a633bf-684a-4486-86a5-7306a3846aba","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkaFbVuDLSieAPzxW6Jq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y47MZHAVpZRsQxQ37Dp9CL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","content":"# First launch: the printer step and the skipped-printer Home card\n\nBuild spec for the session building the first launch (branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35`). Written 2026-11-05 by the design session after Kenneth signed up in the built app, landed on the add-printer dialog and found it confusing, and then found the \"assumed\" printer card on Home confusing too.\n\n**Status: proposal. Kenneth has not approved these screens yet. Do not build until he says go.**\n\nThe screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 104), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`.\n\n## Why the built screens confuse\n\nVersion 89 of my board 08 drew the add-printer dialog standing alone on the frame, and the app built it faithfully. A person who just signed in goes from the welcome straight to a dialog headed \"STEP 1 OF 3 · Which printer?\". Nothing says why the app asks. The dialog shows a step counter of its own inside onboarding. It offers four ways out: Cancel, Back, \"Skip, use a default\" and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\". The \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" link was added in the code; no board shows it.\n\nSkipping then installs Generic Klipper Printer, and Home shows it as one of the person's printers. The card has a warning triangle, the word \"assumed\", \"Not connected\" and a Connect… button. To someone new it reads as an error with a printer they don't own.\n\n## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n\nA screen of its own, laid out like board 07, the OrcaSlicer import screen: lockup top-left, one centred column 520 px wide.\n\n1. **What the welcome finished**, one line with a green check, only when there is something to say:\n   - signed in: \"Signed in as {email} · {balance} credits\"\n   - own key saved: \"The agent uses your Anthropic key\" (name the provider that was saved)\n   - Just slice for now: no line.\n2. **Headline** (page-title): \"Which printer do you have?\"\n3. **Lead** (body, secondary): \"JusPrin plans every print for your printer: its bed, its nozzle and the filament it starts with. You can add more printers later.\"\n4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.\n5. **Nozzle**: a segmented choice of the chosen model's nozzles, starting on `startingNozzle()` (0.4 where offered). Under it: \"Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.\"\n6. **Continue** (primary) and **Skip for now** (link) on one row. Under them, tertiary label: \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".\n\nContinue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened.\n\n## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n\nAlready built (`ImportResult` in `HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx`); the board now draws it so the canvas matches the app. No change asked.\n\n## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n\nThe skipped printer is not shown as a printer. In `HomeUI/src/components/PrinterCard.tsx`, a printer with `assumed: true` renders as a \"No printer yet\" card instead:\n\n- printer icon (secondary) and \"No printer yet\" (body-bold)\n- \"Files slice for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\" (body-small, secondary)\n- **Add your printer** (small primary button), which opens the same add-printer path as \"+ Add printer\"\n\nIt has no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no connection line, no Connect… and no ⋯ menu. The \"+ Add printer\" row is hidden while this card shows. Once the person adds a printer of their own, Home stops listing the generic one. The app keeps the preset so files still slice. The drop-zone line under \"Drop a model or project to start\" says \"JusPrin slices it for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n\n## Same problem elsewhere, not drawn yet\n\nThe printer chip in a project also shows the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). My proposal, not drawn: the chip names it \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\" with no warning. Kenneth decides.\n\n## Board 09\n\nHome after signing in and choosing a printer now shows the one printer picked on 08 (Bambu Lab A1 mini). Same layout as before.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2201,"cache_read_input_tokens":250016,"output_tokens":3267,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1306},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2201,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3267,"cache_read_input_tokens":250016,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2201,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2201},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Y47MZHAVpZRsQxQ37Dp9CL":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","content":"# First launch: the printer step and the skipped-printer Home card\n\nBuild spec for the session building the first launch (branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35`). Written 2026-11-05 by the design session after Kenneth signed up in the built app, landed on the add-printer dialog and found it confusing, and then found the \"assumed\" printer card on Home confusing too.\n\n**Status: proposal. Kenneth has not approved these screens yet. Do not build until he says go.**\n\nThe screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 104), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`.\n\n## Why the built screens confuse\n\nVersion 89 of my board 08 drew the add-printer dialog standing alone on the frame, and the app built it faithfully. A person who just signed in goes from the welcome straight to a dialog headed \"STEP 1 OF 3 · Which printer?\". Nothing says why the app asks. The dialog shows a step counter of its own inside onboarding. It offers four ways out: Cancel, Back, \"Skip, use a default\" and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\". The \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" link was added in the code; no board shows it.\n\nSkipping then installs Generic Klipper Printer, and Home shows it as one of the person's printers. The card has a warning triangle, the word \"assumed\", \"Not connected\" and a Connect… button. To someone new it reads as an error with a printer they don't own.\n\n## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n\nA screen of its own, laid out like board 07, the OrcaSlicer import screen: lockup top-left, one centred column 520 px wide.\n\n1. **What the welcome finished**, one line with a green check, only when there is something to say:\n   - signed in: \"Signed in as {email} · {balance} credits\"\n   - own key saved: \"The agent uses your Anthropic key\" (name the provider that was saved)\n   - Just slice for now: no line.\n2. **Headline** (page-title): \"Which printer do you have?\"\n3. **Lead** (body, secondary): \"JusPrin plans every print for your printer: its bed, its nozzle and the filament it starts with. You can add more printers later.\"\n4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.\n5. **Nozzle**: a segmented choice of the chosen model's nozzles, starting on `startingNozzle()` (0.4 where offered). Under it: \"Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.\"\n6. **Continue** (primary) and **Skip for now** (link) on one row. Under them, tertiary label: \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".\n\nContinue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened.\n\n## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n\nAlready built (`ImportResult` in `HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx`); the board now draws it so the canvas matches the app. No change asked.\n\n## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n\nThe skipped printer is not shown as a printer. In `HomeUI/src/components/PrinterCard.tsx`, a printer with `assumed: true` renders as a \"No printer yet\" card instead:\n\n- printer icon (secondary) and \"No printer yet\" (body-bold)\n- \"Files slice for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\" (body-small, secondary)\n- **Add your printer** (small primary button), which opens the same add-printer path as \"+ Add printer\"\n\nIt has no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no connection line, no Connect… and no ⋯ menu. The \"+ Add printer\" row is hidden while this card shows. Once the person adds a printer of their own, Home stops listing the generic one. The app keeps the preset so files still slice. The drop-zone line under \"Drop a model or project to start\" says \"JusPrin slices it for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n\n## Same problem elsewhere, not drawn yet\n\nThe printer chip in a project also shows the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). My proposal, not drawn: the chip names it \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\" with no warning. Kenneth decides.\n\n## Board 09\n\nHome after signing in and choosing a printer now shows the one printer picked on 08 (Bambu Lab A1 mini). Same layout as before.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkaFbDmtSFqWdk75wFcY","requestRef":"23d8834c-45e6-485f-bbaf-6f2ce641bc8d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3e90cf76-4adb-4434-b0b1-9ae362f96be7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:32:00.896Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userTy