en installs Generic Klipper Printer, and Home shows it as one of the person's printers. The card has a warning triangle, the word \"assumed\", \"Not connected\" and a Connect… button. To someone new it reads as an error with a printer they don't own.\n\n## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n\nA screen of its own, laid out like board 07, the OrcaSlicer import screen: lockup top-left, one centred column 520 px wide.\n\n1. **What the welcome finished**, one line with a green check, only when there is something to say:\n   - signed in: \"Signed in as {email} · {balance} credits\"\n   - own key saved: \"The agent uses your Anthropic key\" (name the provider that was saved)\n   - Just slice for now: no line.\n2. **Headline** (page-title): \"Which printer do you have?\"\n3. **Lead** (body, secondary): \"JusPrin plans every print for your printer: its bed, its nozzle and the filament it starts with. You can add more printers later.\"\n4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.\n5. **Nozzle**: a segmented choice of the chosen model's nozzles, starting on `startingNozzle()` (0.4 where offered). Under it: \"Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.\"\n6. **Continue** (primary) and **Skip for now** (link) on one row. Under them, tertiary label: \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".\n\nContinue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened.\n\n## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n\nAlready built (`ImportResult` in `HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx`); the board now draws it so the canvas matches the app. No change asked.\n\n## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n\nThe skipped printer is not shown as a printer. In `HomeUI/src/components/PrinterCard.tsx`, a printer with `assumed: true` renders as a \"No printer yet\" card instead:\n\n- printer icon (secondary) and \"No printer yet\" (body-bold)\n- \"Files slice for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\" (body-small, secondary)\n- **Add your printer** (small primary button), which opens the same add-printer path as \"+ Add printer\"\n\nIt has no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no connection line, no Connect… and no ⋯ menu. The \"+ Add printer\" row is hidden while this card shows. Once the person adds a printer of their own, Home stops listing the generic one. The app keeps the preset so files still slice. The drop-zone line under \"Drop a model or project to start\" says \"JusPrin slices it for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n\n## Same problem elsewhere, not drawn yet\n\nThe printer chip in a project also shows the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). My proposal, not drawn: the chip names it \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\" with no warning. Kenneth decides.\n\n## Board 09\n\nHome after signing in and choosing a printer now shows the one printer picked on 08 (Bambu Lab A1 mini). Same layout as before.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3e90cf76-4adb-4434-b0b1-9ae362f96be7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reas