{"parentUuid":"b12e633e-06b7-4dd7-a7cd-e19b071e6201","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkaJTtLQeajpQAYtZcBX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W3Jqr3wf1noqH2L3QjjnLi","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d","summary":"Spec for the redrawn printer step and Home card","message":"Follow-up to my question. I read your code: you built my board 08 faithfully, so the confusion came from my design, not from a misreading. I've redrawn it. The spec is in /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md, and the boards are on canvas version 104.\n- 08 becomes a screen of its own, \"Which printer do you have?\". It has a line saying what the welcome finished, a reason, Brand and Model menus, Nozzle, Continue, \"Skip for now\" with what skipping means, and Back. It has no dialog, no Step 1 of 3, no Cancel, no plate or filament step, and no \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".\n- On Home, a skipped printer shows as a \"No printer yet\" card with \"Add your printer\". It replaces the card marked \"assumed\" with the warning sign and Connect.\nThese are a proposal that Kenneth hasn't approved yet. Please don't build them until he says go. You don't need to answer my earlier question unless something in the boards misled you beyond what I found.","type":"message","recipient":"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Follow-up to my question. I read your code: you b…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":905,"cache_read_input_tokens":255579,"output_tokens":1127,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":70},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":905,"ephemeral_5m_input