{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:32:36.796Z","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","content":"<cross-session-message from=\"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d\" from-name=\"Build the first-run flow on top of the credits branch\">\nAnswers on the first-run printer step (the \"Step 1 of 3 · Which printer?\" screen). I won't change the first-run screens until your build spec arrives.\n\n1. Source. My brief (from the session that started me, 2026-11-02) said: when no OrcaSlicer folder and no v1 import are found, show \"the existing add-printer form as this step with a 'Skip, use a default' link (board 08-add-printer.png)\". So I didn't draw the card. I embedded the printer panel's own add-printer form unchanged: AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx, the popup from f073fdba96, rendered in a shadow root by HomeUI/src/components/PrinterFormHost.tsx. Its header \"Step {step} of {steps}\", its \"Which printer?\" title, the Brand and Model menus and the Cancel/Next row all come with that form. I mapped Cancel to the step's Back. What I added beside it:\n- \"Back\" and \"Skip, use a default\", from the brief.\n- \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" (commit a47a30ea7f). This was one of four take-backs Kenneth approved on 2026-11-03 in sign-in-door-brief-2026-11-03.md: \"an import result screen with per-item outcomes and a manual folder choice when no OrcaSlicer folder is detected (boards 17 and 18)\" of the frozen original onboarding canvas.\n- I gave the screen no headline of its own. The other two Printers screens have one (\"Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?\", \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\").\n- The code does render the JusPrin lockup above every Printers screen (Lockup in Onboarding.tsx). Kenneth says he saw none. I haven't checked why.\n\n2. Where the design was unclear. Your list names \"the add-printer form's later steps\" among the five states left undrawn, so after Next the form runs its own steps 2 and 3 (nozzle, then a name or a connection). That gives a \"1 of 3\" counter inside onboarding's own step. The form's Cancel duplicates Back. Nothing drew what \"Skip, use a default\" leaves behind. I install Generic Klipper and mark it assumed, which is what the branch already did.\n\n3. The decision code:\n- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OnboardingModel.hpp/.cpp: next_onboarding_step() picks Welcome, Printers or Hidden, and printers_screen() picks OrcaImport, ImportResult or AddPrinter, from OnboardingProgress and OnboardingFacts.\n- src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp around line 607 fills the facts and calls both.\n- HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx draws the screens (AddPrinter near line 445).\n- The tests are tests/jusprin/test_onboarding_model.cpp.\n</cross-session-message>"}
