"2026-11-05T22:32:46.189Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"7be68364-c71b-40ab-94a4-d58b1ff87f19","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9b47b004-8428-4132-a478-23fbb4e91264","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BZSJmYPKqoPtZJEz1sW81h","type":"tool_result","content":"18:- OrcaSlicer import: choose the folder manually or a preset bundle when nothing is detected; a partial-result screen (conflicts renamed \"(Orca copy)\", failures with reasons, Retry failed items). New flow: one list, Import / Start fresh / Back; conflicts go through a yes/no dialog mid-import.\n37:**Ruled and built, 2026-11-03 afternoon.** Kenneth: \"Yes, build it\" on the conventional door (Google first, one email field, then a 6-digit code in the app or a password for an address that has one), and \"Tail that subsession to build this\": the existing implementation session did both halves. App: five commits on `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` ending 3df2ed9c24 (door states, `CodeField.tsx`, import result screen with \"Retry failed items\" and the folder-picker link, v1 line, scale-line fix, harness email checks; 3df2ed9c24 fixes Home's poll, which only reported a phase change and left the page on \"busy\" between email steps). Gateway: 81efc6fd43 on `claude/email-sign-in` in tsd-enterprise (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/sign_in.py`, four endpoints under `auth/`, codes as HMAC in Redis, tokens minted for client id \"JusPrin2\", templates under `web_ent/jusprin/templates/jusprin/v2/email/`). One deviation from the brief, kept: an account made through Google gets a code, not the password step, because its password is random. Tests: 155 gateway tests passed (23 new), 515 + 160 Catch2 cases, 141 Vitest; a mutation run with the ordering and social-account logic removed failed 4 tests, so they bite. Built app against the local compose stack: code path (wrong, expired, resent, right) and password path (wrong, right) both saved the account. Not verified: Windows, Linux, Continue with Google, the import result screen in the real app, a real v1 import. Known gaps: renamed imported printers leave their filaments' `compatible_printers` on the old name; no hidden username field for password managers; the welcome's clip card stays white in dark mode. Nothing pushed, no PR.\n39:**Later the same day, driven by Kenneth in the implementation session:** aa70569e4f rebuilt `sign_in.py` on what the website already runs (SyndicateSpecificBackend lookup, allauth adapter sign-up and `authenticate()`, allauth's rate limiter for codes, django-oauth-toolkit's own token server); only the Redis code store stays custom, because allauth 0.63's login-by-code looks across syndicates and makes no account. d799b57e37 dropped the duplicate-address test: production's 251,485 accounts have no two in one syndicate sharing an address, so the lookup raises like the website instead of picking one. Kenneth then asked (through the session \"btw: Why not?\") for a task card to upgrade django-allauth to 65.x on the same branch and worktree first, with the rebuild on allauth's flows after; the card could not carry the folder, so it was offered as a question instead.\nfirst-run-flow-sequence.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b5d952eb-1e86-42da-b97d-c4db006a3761","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:32:46.260Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"18:- OrcaSlicer import: choose the folder manually or a preset bundle when nothing is detected; a partial-result screen (conflicts renamed \"(Orca copy)\", failures with reasons, Retry failed items). New flow: one list, Import / Start fresh / Back; conflicts go through a yes/no dialog mid-import.\n37:**Ruled and built, 2026-11-03 afternoon.** Kenneth: \"Yes, build it\" on the conventional door (Google first, one email field, then a 6-digit code in the app or a password for an address that has one), and \"Tail that subsession to build this\": the existing implementation session did both halves. App: five commits on `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` ending 3df2ed9c24 (door states, `CodeField.tsx`, import result screen with \"Retry failed items\" and the folder-picker link, v1 line, scale-line fix, harness email checks; 3df2ed9c24 fixes Home's poll, which only reported a phase change and left the page on \"busy\" between email steps). Gateway: 81efc6fd43 on `claude/email-sign-in` in tsd-enterprise (`web_ent/jusprin/v2/sign_in.py`, four endpoints under `auth/`, codes as HMAC in Redis, tokens minted for client id \"JusPrin2\", templates under `web_ent/jusprin/templates/jusprin/v2/email/`). One deviation from the brief, kept: an account made through Google gets a code, not the password step, because its password is random. Tests: 155 gateway tests passed (23 new), 515 + 160 Catch2 cases, 141 Vitest; a mutation run with the ordering and social-account logic removed failed 4 tests, so they bite. Built app against the local compose stack: code path (wrong, expired, resent, right) and password path (wrong, right) both saved the account. Not verified: Windows, Linux, Continue with Google, the import result screen in the real app, a real v1 import. Known gaps: renamed imported printers leave their filaments' `compatible_printers` on the old name; no hidden username field for password managers; the welcome's clip card stays white in dark mode. Nothing pushed, no PR.\n39:**Later the same day, driven by Kenneth in the implementation session:** aa70569e4f rebuilt `sign_in.py` on what the website already runs (SyndicateSpecificBackend lookup, allauth adapter sign-up and `authenticate()`, allauth's rate limiter for codes, django-oauth-toolkit's own token server); only the Redis code store stays custom, because allauth 0.63's login-by-code looks across syndicates and makes no account. d799b57e37 dropped the duplicate-address test: production's 251,485 accounts have no two in one syndicate sharing an address, so the lookup raises like the website instead of picking one. Kenneth then asked (through the session \"btw: Why not?\") for a task card to upgrade django-allauth to 65.x on the same branch and worktree first, with the rebuild on allauth's flows after; the card could not carry the folder, so it was offered as a question instead.\nfirst-run-flow-sequence.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7be68364-c71b-40ab-94a4-d58b1ff87f19","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/memory","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
