{"parentUuid":"5687aa45-4aec-4428-ae36-b765e57fadca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkaQKmM2DgBmNbvHNsiC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LPuCcPGmK3owHdVKkdMEeb","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","old_string":"7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".","new_string":"7. **The OrcaSlicer folder choice**, one quiet line: \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder?\" (label, secondary) and the link \"Choose the folder…\". It does what \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" does today (a47a30ea7f). Kenneth approved this manual folder choice on 2026-11-03, so it stays; only its wording and place change.\n8. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, and the plate and filament steps."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1780,"cache_read_input_tokens":269653,"output_tokens":1175,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1780,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1175,"cache_read_input_tokens":269653,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1780,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1780},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LPuCcPGmK3owHdVKkdMEeb":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","old_string":"7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".","new_string":"7. **The OrcaSlicer folder choice**, one quiet line: \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder?\" (label, secondary) and the link \"Choose the folder…\". It does what \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" does today (a47a30ea7f). Kenneth approved this manual folder choice on 2026-11-03, so it stays; only its wording and place change.\n8. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, and the plate and filament steps."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkaQKXxQiBPk2othqyEp","requestRef":"c34ea302-7eda-4ca5-8250-c5356db393ee","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b065daf7-29c7-4786-81b5-dca3ce131272","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:33:31.481Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"b065daf7-29c7-4786-81b5-dca3ce131272","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9b47b004-8428-4132-a478-23fbb4e91264","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LPuCcPGmK3owHdVKkdMEeb","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"bca400a2-b1ec-4928-a748-8dfcc9a9668b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:33:31.514Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","oldString":"7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".","newString":"7. **The OrcaSlicer folder choice**, one quiet line: \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder?\" (label, secondary) and the link \"Choose the folder…\". It does what \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" does today (a47a30ea7f). Kenneth approved this manual folder choice on 2026-11-03, so it stays; only its wording and place change.\n8. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, and the plate and filament steps.","originalFile":"# First launch: the printer step and the skipped-printer Home card\n\nBuild spec for the session building the first launch (branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35`). Written 2026-11-05 by the design session after Kenneth signed up in the built app, landed on the add-printer dialog and found it confusing, and then found the \"assumed\" printer card on Home confusing too.\n\n**Status: proposal. Kenneth has not approved these screens yet. Do not build until he says go.**\n\nThe screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 104), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`.\n\n## Why the built screens confuse\n\nVersion 89 of my board 08 drew the add-printer dialog standing alone on the frame, and the app built it faithfully. A person who just signed in goes from the welcome straight to a dialog headed \"STEP 1 OF 3 · Which printer?\". Nothing says why the app asks. The dialog shows a step counter of its own inside onboarding. It offers four ways out: Cancel, Back, \"Skip, use a default\" and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\". The \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" link was added in the code; no board shows it.\n\nSkipping then installs Generic Klipper Printer, and Home shows it as one of the person's printers. The card has a warning triangle, the word \"assumed\", \"Not connected\" and a Connect… button. To someone new it reads as an error with a printer they don't own.\n\n## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n\nA screen of its own, laid out like board 07, the OrcaSlicer import screen: lockup top-left, one centred column 520 px wide.\n\n1. **What the welcome finished**, one line with a green check, only when there is something to say:\n   - signed in: \"Signed in as {email} · {balance} credits\"\n   - own key saved: \"The agent uses your Anthropic key\" (name the provider that was saved)\n   - Just slice for now: no line.\n2. **Headline** (page-title): \"Which printer do you have?\"\n3. **Lead** (body, secondary): \"JusPrin plans every print for your printer: its bed, its nozzle and the filament it starts with. You can add more printers later.\"\n4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.\n5. **Nozzle**: a segmented choice of the chosen model's nozzles, starting on `startingNozzle()` (0.4 where offered). Under it: \"Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.\"\n6. **Continue** (primary) and **Skip for now** (link) on one row. Under them, tertiary label: \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".\n\nContinue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened.\n\n## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n\nAlready built (`ImportResult` in `HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx`); the board now draws it so the canvas matches the app. No change asked.\n\n## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n\nThe skipped printer is not shown as a printer. In `HomeUI/src/components/PrinterCard.tsx`, a printer with `assumed: true` renders as a \"No printer yet\" card instead:\n\n- printer icon (secondary) and \"No printer yet\" (body-bold)\n- \"Files slice for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\" (body-small, secondary)\n- **Add your printer** (small primary button), which opens the same add-printer path as \"+ Add printer\"\n\nIt has no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no connection line, no Connect… and no ⋯ menu. The \"+ Add printer\" row is hidden while this card shows. Once the person adds a printer of their own, Home stops listing the generic one. The app keeps the preset so files still slice. The drop-zone line under \"Drop a model or project to start\" says \"JusPrin slices it for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n\n## Same problem elsewhere, not drawn yet\n\nThe printer chip in a project also shows the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). My proposal, not drawn: the chip names it \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\" with no warning. Kenneth decides.\n\n## Board 09\n\nHome after signing in and choosing a printer now shows the one printer picked on 08 (Bambu Lab A1 mini). Same layout as before.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":25,"oldLines":9,"newStart":25,"newLines":10,"lines":[" 4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog."," 5. **Nozzle**: a segmented choice of the chosen model's nozzles, starting on `startingNozzle()` (0.4 where offered). Under it: \"Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.\""," 6. **Continue** (primary) and **Skip for now** (link) on one row. Under them, tertiary label: \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"","-7. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.","+7. **The OrcaSlicer folder choice**, one quiet line: \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder?\" (label, secondary) and the link \"Choose the folder…\". It does what \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" does today (a47a30ea7f). Kenneth approved this manual folder choice on 2026-11-03, so it stays; only its wording and place change.","+8. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now."," ","-Removed from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, the plate and filament steps, and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\".","+Removed from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, and the plate and filament steps."," "," Continue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b065daf7-29c7-4786-81b5-dca3ce131272","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
