{"parentUuid":"06e8b7b1-5b2a-460b-9ff3-dfb5df7c416c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d09d41a2-5472-4350-8d3d-c5d7d30749d9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C9qrMXYAiehrPLA2qXeLv2","type":"tool_result","content":"5:**Status: the printer chip change is agreed (Kenneth, 2026-11-05). Board 08 and the \"No printer yet\" card on 10 are still a proposal: do not build those until he says go.**\n49:## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c9cb27f7-706b-4cf2-8007-5138c34b06ff","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:39:12.379Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"5:**Status: the printer chip change is agreed (Kenneth, 2026-11-05). Board 08 and the \"No printer yet\" card on 10 are still a proposal: do not build those until he says go.**\n49:## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":7,"newStart":2,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," Build spec for the session building the first launch (branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35`). Written 2026-11-05 by the design session after Kenneth signed up in the built app, landed on the add-printer dialog and found it confusing, and then found the \"assumed\" printer card on Home confusing too."," ","-**Status: proposal. Kenneth has not approved these screens yet. Do not build until he says go.**","+**Status: the printer chip change is agreed (Kenneth, 2026-11-05). Board 08 and the \"No printer yet\" card on 10 are still a proposal: do not build those until he says go.**"," "," The screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 105), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`."," "]},{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":9,"newStart":46,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," It has no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no connection line, no Connect… and no ⋯ menu. The \"+ Add printer\" row is hidden while this card shows. Once the person adds a printer of their own, Home stops listing the generic one. The app keeps the preset so files still slice. The drop-zone line under \"Drop a model or project to start\" says \"JusPrin slices it for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\""," ","-## Same problem elsewhere, not drawn yet","+## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)"," ","-The printer chip in a project also shows the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). My proposal, not drawn: the chip names it \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\" with no warning. Kenneth decides.","+The printer chip also showed the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). Kenneth's answer on 2026-11-05: yes. The chip names the generic printer \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\", with no warning triangle and no \"assumed\". Not drawn on the canvas; this line is the spec."," "," ## Board 09"," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"06e8b7b1-5b2a-460b-9ff3-dfb5df7c416c","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
