{"parentUuid":"fa4154a3-ee1f-4de0-b2e4-6f57fe132f46","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"311f729d-bca2-4ba5-aa2d-f8cb729b5bc1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DcbjcTiSFTNwtQtSctJtrc","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 4 of 5 is in progress."}]}]},"uuid":"432776b5-b628-47f9-a53d-3ebd84d8bb2f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:58:19.294Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 4 of 5 is in progress."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fa4154a3-ee1f-4de0-b2e4-6f57fe132f46","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2/render","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"432776b5-b628-47f9-a53d-3ebd84d8bb2f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkcJDBHj7dBAcY4h8FiJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LvJLhkZGPhGZPtTbPgBnNy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert old in s, old[:70]; s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep('**Status: the printer chip change is agreed (Kenneth, 2026-11-05). Board 08 and the \"No printer yet\" card on 10 are still a proposal: do not build those until he says go.**',\n    '**Status: agreed. Kenneth said yes to the printer chip on 2026-11-05, then \"Go with your recommendations\" for the rest: the printer step (08), the \"No printer yet\" card (10), \"Ask the agent\", and reading the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer. Build it.**')\nrep('(https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 105)', '(https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 106)')\nrep('''4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.''',\n'''4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.\n   Under the menus, only when the agent is set up (signed in with credits, or a saved key): \"Can't find your printer?\" (label, secondary) and the link **Ask the agent**. It finishes onboarding and opens Home with the printer chat, the same thing Home's \"+ Add printer\" does today (`OrcaHomeBackend::add_printer()`, which calls `m_open_conversation({}, false)`). After \"Just slice for now\" the line is not shown.''')\nrep('## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"', '''## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n\nToday `detect_orca_profiles()` (`Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`) counts only the printers saved as presets under OrcaSlicer's `user/<account>/machine`. Printers a person only ticked in OrcaSlicer's printer list are recorded in `OrcaSlicer.conf` under `\"models\"`, as entries like `{\"vendor\": \"BBL\", \"model\": \"Bambu Lab A1 mini\", \"nozzle_diameter\": \"0.4\"}`. Most OrcaSlicer users never save a preset, so the import screen misses them and the person lands on the manual form. On Kenneth's Mac, OrcaSlicer.conf lists six ticked printers (A1 mini, Kobra 3, Ender-3 V2 Neo, K1C, Generic Klipper Printer at 0.6, Qidi X-Plus 4), and `user/` holds three saved copies.\n\nKenneth agreed on 2026-11-05 to include the ticked printers:\n- Read `\"models\"` from OrcaSlicer.conf as well. Map each entry to JusPrin's own system printer for that vendor, model and nozzle. Skip any that JusPrin's profiles don't have, and any already covered by a saved preset of the same printer.\n- List them on 07 with the saved ones, one line per printer. The filament count shows only for saved presets.\n- Import installs and selects each ticked printer from JusPrin's own profiles, as `SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer()` does for the default printer. The saved presets import as now.\n- `orca_printers` is true when either list is non-empty.\n- Add a test with an OrcaSlicer folder that has only ticked printers.\n\n## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"''')\nrep('''Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"''','''Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"''')\nrep('''## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)''','''## Connecting a printer on Home\n\nKenneth agreed the agent handles connecting a printer after this step. That's already built: the printer card's Connect… calls `connect_printer()`, which opens the printer chat (`m_open_conversation(name, true)`). No change needed.\n\n## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^## \\|^\\*\\*Status\" /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","description":"Write both decisions into the build spec and mark it agreed"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1905,"cache_read_input_tokens":309108,"output_tokens":1810,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1905,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1810,"cache_read_input_tokens":309108,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1905,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1905},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LvJLhkZGPhGZPtTbPgBnNy":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert old in s, old[:70]; s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep('**Status: the printer chip change is agreed (Kenneth, 2026-11-05). Board 08 and the \"No printer yet\" card on 10 are still a proposal: do not build those until he says go.**',\n    '**Status: agreed. Kenneth said yes to the printer chip on 2026-11-05, then \"Go with your recommendations\" for the rest: the printer step (08), the \"No printer yet\" card (10), \"Ask the agent\", and reading the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer. Build it.**')\nrep('(https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 105)', '(https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 106)')\nrep('''4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.''',\n'''4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.\n   Under the menus, only when the agent is set up (signed in with credits, or a saved key): \"Can't find your printer?\" (label, secondary) and the link **Ask the agent**. It finishes onboarding and opens Home with the printer chat, the same thing Home's \"+ Add printer\" does today (`OrcaHomeBackend::add_printer()`, which calls `m_open_conversation({}, false)`). After \"Just slice for now\" the line is not shown.''')\nrep('## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"', '''## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n\nToday `detect_orca_profiles()` (`Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`) counts only the printers saved as presets under OrcaSlicer's `user/<account>/machine`. Printers a person only ticked in OrcaSlicer's printer list are recorded in `OrcaSlicer.conf` under `\"models\"`, as entries like `{\"vendor\": \"BBL\", \"model\": \"Bambu Lab A1 mini\", \"nozzle_diameter\": \"0.4\"}`. Most OrcaSlicer users never save a preset, so the import screen misses them and the person lands on the manual form. On Kenneth's Mac, OrcaSlicer.conf lists six ticked printers (A1 mini, Kobra 3, Ender-3 V2 Neo, K1C, Generic Klipper Printer at 0.6, Qidi X-Plus 4), and `user/` holds three saved copies.\n\nKenneth agreed on 2026-11-05 to include the ticked printers:\n- Read `\"models\"` from OrcaSlicer.conf as well. Map each entry to JusPrin's own system printer for that vendor, model and nozzle. Skip any that JusPrin's profiles don't have, and any already covered by a saved preset of the same printer.\n- List them on 07 with the saved ones, one line per printer. The filament count shows only for saved presets.\n- Import installs and selects each ticked printer from JusPrin's own profiles, as `SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer()` does for the default printer. The saved presets import as now.\n- `orca_printers` is true when either list is non-empty.\n- Add a test with an OrcaSlicer folder that has only ticked printers.\n\n## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"''')\nrep('''Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"''','''Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"''')\nrep('''## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)''','''## Connecting a printer on Home\n\nKenneth agreed the agent handles connecting a printer after this step. That's already built: the printer card's Connect… calls `connect_printer()`, which opens the printer chat (`m_open_conversation(name, true)`). No change needed.\n\n## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"^## \\|^\\*\\*Status\" /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","description":"Write both decisions into the build spec and mark it agreed"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgkcJCtBPPbd6EQ4xGLzB","requestRef":"4d31e70f-0e27-42d8-a72f-968fe04dde8d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"87d99c77-2416-4df7-8050-68ae5c7379ed","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:58:32.749Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2/render","sessionId":