{"parentUuid":"87d99c77-2416-4df7-8050-68ae5c7379ed","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"311f729d-bca2-4ba5-aa2d-f8cb729b5bc1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LvJLhkZGPhGZPtTbPgBnNy","type":"tool_result","content":"5:**Status: agreed. Kenneth said yes to the printer chip on 2026-11-05, then \"Go with your recommendations\" for the rest: the printer step (08), the \"No printer yet\" card (10), \"Ask the agent\", and reading the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer. Build it.**\n9:## Why the built screens confuse\n15:## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n36:## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n47:## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n51:## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n61:## Connecting a printer on Home\n65:## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)\n69:## Board 09","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7613f61a-c419-454f-9d5a-08d6965f2ca8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:58:33.055Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"5:**Status: agreed. Kenneth said yes to the printer chip on 2026-11-05, then \"Go with your recommendations\" for the rest: the printer step (08), the \"No printer yet\" card (10), \"Ask the agent\", and reading the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer. Build it.**\n9:## Why the built screens confuse\n15:## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n36:## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n47:## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n51:## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n61:## Connecting a printer on Home\n65:## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)\n69:## Board 09","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":2,"oldLines":9,"newStart":2,"newLines":9,"lines":[" "," Build spec for the session building the first launch (branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35`). Written 2026-11-05 by the design session after Kenneth signed up in the built app, landed on the add-printer dialog and found it confusing, and then found the \"assumed\" printer card on Home confusing too."," ","-**Status: the printer chip change is agreed (Kenneth, 2026-11-05). Board 08 and the \"No printer yet\" card on 10 are still a proposal: do not build those until he says go.**","+**Status: agreed. Kenneth said yes to the printer chip on 2026-11-05, then \"Go with your recommendations\" for the rest: the printer step (08), the \"No printer yet\" card (10), \"Ask the agent\", and reading the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer. Build it.**"," ","-The screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 105), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`.","+The screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 106), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`."," "," ## Why the built screens confuse"," "]},{"oldStart":23,"oldLines":6,"newStart":23,"newLines":7,"lines":[" 2. **Headline** (page-title): \"Which printer do you have?\""," 3. **Lead** (body, secondary): \"JusPrin plans every print for your printer: its bed, its nozzle and the filament it starts with. You can add more printers later.\""," 4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.","+   Under the menus, only when the agent is set up (signed in with credits, or a saved key): \"Can't find your printer?\" (label, secondary) and the link **Ask the agent**. It finishes onboarding and opens Home with the printer chat, the same thing Home's \"+ Add printer\" does today (`OrcaHomeBackend::add_printer()`, which calls `m_open_conversation({}, false)`). After \"Just slice for now\" the line is not shown."," 5. **Nozzle**: a segmented choice of the chosen model's nozzles, starting on `startingNozzle()` (0.4 where offered). Under it: \"Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.\""," 6. **Continue** (primary) and **Skip for now** (link) on one row. Under them, tertiary label: \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\""," 7. **The OrcaSlicer folder choice**, one quiet line: \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder?\" (label, secondary) and the link \"Choose the folder…\". It does what \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" does today (a47a30ea7f). Kenneth approved this manual folder choice on 2026-11-03, so it stays; only its wording and place change."]},{"oldStart":32,"oldLines":6,"newStart":33,"newLines":17,"lines":[" "," Continue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened."," ","+## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones","+","+Today `detect_orca_profiles()` (`Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`) counts only the printers saved as presets under OrcaSlicer's `user/<account>/machine`. Printers a person only ticked in OrcaSlicer's printer list are recorded in `OrcaSlicer.conf` under `\"models\"`, as entries like `{\"vendor\": \"BBL\", \"model\": \"Bambu Lab A1 mini\", \"nozzle_diameter\": \"0.4\"}`. Most OrcaSlicer users never save a preset, so the import screen misses them and the person lands on the manual form. On Kenneth's Mac, OrcaSlicer.conf lists six ticked printers (A1 mini, Kobra 3, Ender-3 V2 Neo, K1C, Generic Klipper Printer at 0.6, Qidi X-Plus 4), and `user/` holds three saved copies.","+","+Kenneth agreed on 2026-11-05 to include the ticked printers:","+- Read `\"models\"` from OrcaSlicer.conf as well. Map each entry to JusPrin's own system printer for that vendor, model and nozzle. Skip any that JusPrin's profiles don't have, and any already covered by a saved preset of the same printer.","+- List them on 07 with the saved ones, one line per printer. The filament count shows only for saved presets.","+- Import installs and selects each ticked printer from JusPrin's own profiles, as `SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer()` does for the default printer. The saved presets import as now.","+- `orca_printers` is true when either list is non-empty.","+- Add a test with an OrcaSlicer folder that has only ticked printers.","+"," ## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\""," "," Already built (`ImportResult` in `HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx`); the board now draws it so the canvas matches the app. No change asked."]},{"oldStart":46,"oldLines":6,"newStart":58,"newLines":10,"lines":[" "," It has no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no connection line, no Connect… and no ⋯ menu. The \"+ Add printer\" row is hidden while this card shows. Once the person adds a printer of their own, Home stops listing the generic one. The app keeps the preset so files still slice. The drop-zone line under \"Drop a model or project to start\" says \"JusPrin slices it for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\""," ","+## Connecting a printer on Home","+","+Kenneth agreed the agent handles connecting a printer after this step. That's already built: the printer card's Connect… calls `connect_printer()`, which opens the printer chat (`m_open_conversation(name, true)`). No change needed.","+"," ## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)"," "," The printer chip also showed the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). Kenneth's answer on 2026-11-05: yes. The chip names the generic printer \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\", with no warning triangle and no \"assumed\". Not drawn on the canvas; this line is the spec."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"87d99c77-2416-4df7-8050-68ae5c7379ed","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2/render","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
