{"parentUuid":"5fbf4b45-9da7-40f3-9c2a-d08673ba414b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkcLQbSZ213yoPBdL1Sq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both recommendations are drawn, the spec is updated, and the coding session has your go-ahead. I took \"Go with your recommendations\" to cover all of my picks. That includes building the redrawn printer step and the \"No printer yet\" card, since \"Yes, build them\" was my pick on that question too.\n\n**Changes on the canvas** (version 106):\n- **New link on the printer step.** \"Can't find your printer? Ask the agent\" now sits right under the Brand and Model menus. It only appears when the agent is set up, either signed in with credits or with a saved key. It opens Home with the printer chat, the same chat Home's \"+ Add printer\" already opens. Someone who chose \"Just slice for now\" doesn't see the line.\n- **The map at the top of the page** lists the new link under the printer step. It also says the OrcaSlicer import screen will include printers ticked in OrcaSlicer.\n- **Labels.** The notes beside the printer and Home rows now say these screens are agreed, not proposals.\n\n**Connecting a printer with the agent on Home is already built.** The Connect… button on a printer card opens the printer chat, so nothing changes there.\n\n**What the coding session builds next**, all in [first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md](first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md):\n1. **The printer step as its own screen.** It reuses the dialog's brand and model menus and adds the ask-the-agent link.\n2. **The OrcaSlicer fix.** The import screen will also list the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer's printer list, not only saved copies. The spec asks for a test with an OrcaSlicer folder that has only ticked printers.\n3. **\"No printer yet\" on Home** in place of the \"assumed\" card.\n4. **The printer chip in a project** will say \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\" with no warning.\n\nNothing is built or tested yet. Once the coding session reports back, the next step is to run the first launch in the real app and check each path."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":315273,"output_tokens":655,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":655,"cache_read_input_tokens":315273,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgkcLQM4MJD91dvuwBnX3","requestRef":"26f8ae68-3640-460f-a6aa-5be179f950e4","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"1cd13e99-0e1a-42a1-805b-ae0aabf4e833","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:58:54.179Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
