{"parentUuid":"4a4fbad6-1aab-4f71-b116-da074132effb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkcey4Zv12o5pgP3PoQ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0153Fug3YboJrAJTHwzxSYNX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\\n'\nnew='''## Board 07: the same carried-over line as 08\n\nWhichever printer screen comes first, 07 or 08, it opens with the line saying what the welcome finished (\"Signed in as … · … credits\", or the saved key), placed above its headline. Kenneth asked for this in a canvas comment on 2026-11-05 (canvas version 107). The import result screen (17) comes after 07, so it doesn't repeat the line.\n\n## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1); s=s.replace('version 106)','version 107)')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncp /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2/render/first-run-07-orcaslicer-import.png /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/; echo \"Same day, version 107 (1793919779-0ea7), Kenneth's canvas comment: 07 carries the signed-in line above its headline, as 08 does.\" >> /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/README.md","description":"Add the carried-over line on the import screen to the spec and log"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_read_input_tokens":329325,"output_tokens":1027,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1703,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1027,"cache_read_input_tokens":329325,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1703,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1703},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0153Fug3YboJrAJTHwzxSYNX":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\\n'\nnew='''## Board 07: the same carried-over line as 08\n\nWhichever printer screen comes first, 07 or 08, it opens with the line saying what the welcome finished (\"Signed in as … · … credits\", or the saved key), placed above its headline. Kenneth asked for this in a canvas comment on 2026-11-05 (canvas version 107). The import result screen (17) comes after 07, so it doesn't repeat the line.\n\n## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n'''\nassert old in s; s=s.replace(old,new,1); s=s.replace('version 106)','version 107)')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncp /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2/render/first-run-07-orcaslicer-import.png /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/; echo \"Same day, version 107 (1793919779-0ea7), Kenneth's canvas comment: 07 carries the signed-in line above its headline, as 08 does.\" >> /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/README.md","description":"Add the carried-over line on the import screen to the spec and log"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgkcexowDq9pZNQ58eDjL","requestRef":"7bdd0d66-4f33-4959-8f94-36b0c0a21d76","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a548e5f0-8156-489b-a8c3-f645f029d893","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:03:05.416Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"a548e5f0-8156-489b-a8c3-f645f029d893","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"523b7f74-ec3b-4b3f-a4be-eeb70beb6b3e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0153Fug3YboJrAJTHwzxSYNX","type":"tool_result","content":"(Bash completed with no output)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"84a6e9cb-6f46-48bd-816b-def896df768a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:03:05.742Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":4,"oldLines":7,"newStart":4,"newLines":7,"lines":[" "," **Status: agreed. Kenneth said yes to the printer chip on 2026-11-05, then \"Go with your recommendations\" for the rest: the printer step (08), the \"No printer yet\" card (10), \"Ask the agent\", and reading the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer. Build it.**"," ","-The screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 106), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`.","+The screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 107), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`."," "," ## Why the built screens confuse"," "]},{"oldStart":33,"oldLines":6,"newStart":33,"newLines":10,"lines":[" "," Continue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened."," ","+## Board 07: the same carried-over line as 08","+","+Whichever printer screen comes first, 07 or 08, it opens with the line saying what the welcome finished (\"Signed in as … · … credits\", or the saved key), placed above its headline. Kenneth asked for this in a canvas comment on 2026-11-05 (canvas version 107). The import result screen (17) comes after 07, so it doesn't repeat the line.","+"," ## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones"," "," Today `detect_orca_profiles()` (`Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`) counts only the printers saved as presets under OrcaSlicer's `user/<account>/machine`. Printers a person only ticked in OrcaSlicer's printer list are recorded in `OrcaSlicer.conf` under `\"models\"`, as entries like `{\"vendor\": \"BBL\", \"model\": \"Bambu Lab A1 mini\", \"nozzle_diameter\": \"0.4\"}`. Most OrcaSlicer users never save a preset, so the import screen misses them and the person lands on the manual form. On Kenneth's Mac, OrcaSlicer.conf lists six ticked printers (A1 mini, Kobra 3, Ender-3 V2 Neo, K1C, Generic Klipper Printer at 0.6, Qidi X-Plus 4), and `user/` holds three saved copies."]}]}],"moreFiles":1,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/first-run-07-orcaslicer-import.png","/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a548e5f0-8156-489b-a8c3-f645f029d893","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
