ult.dc.html\", \"project/check-print-02-legend-and-moves.dc.html\", \"project/check-print-03-finding-selected.dc.html\", \"project/check-print-04-report-states.dc.html\" and 177 more. The type's files are fixed and not listed here.\n\nStored — contract 0.2.47 (newest 0.2.96) · capabilities [10 total]; flags; paste; sample; artifact; assets; comments; db[1 rule]; downloads · readable by only you · access rules (root) write admin; the declaration comes from its Artifact type and can't be changed here.\n\nLive subscription: skipped — watching this artifact was stopped earlier in this session; do not retry on your own. If the user asks you to resume watching it, call the watch action (in permission modes that prompt, they confirm it there).\n\nTo update it again, publish to the same `url` (or the same `file_path` in this conversation) with `root`: \"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/work-first-run-v2\", the folder its served path is relative to. This artifact is private: only its owner and the people the owner has given access can open the link. You cannot change sharing; that is done from the page's Share menu. If the page is meant for someone else, tell the user when you present the page that those people cannot open it until it is shared with them.\n\nThe files you sent are still on disk. For a small, specific change to a file whose text is in this conversation, send the Edit call(s) and an Artifact publish of the same file_path together in one response, with no Read and no shell command that edits the file: these calls run one after another in the order given, so the publish sends the edited file. If an Edit reports that it did not apply, correct it and publish again. If the file's text is no longer in this conversation, or you cannot place the change exactly from the text you have, Read it first."}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","hash":"13808ad582b18f27954568578c57081034b9d0d5841e7c680be7a314f914d623","message":{"role":"system","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md\"}\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# First launch: the printer step and the skipped-printer Home card\n2\t\n3\tBuild spec for the session building the first launch (branch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35`). Written 2026-11-05 by the design session after Kenneth signed up in the built app, landed on the add-printer dialog and found it confusing, and then found the \"assumed\" printer card on Home confusing too.\n4\t\n5\t**Status: agreed. Kenneth said yes to the printer chip on 2026-11-05, then \"Go with your recommendations\" for the rest: the printer step (08), the \"No printer yet\" card (10), \"Ask the agent\", and reading the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer. Build it.**\n6\t\n7\tThe screens are on the \"JusPrin v2\" canvas (https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, version 107), page \"On boarding experience\". The page now starts with a map board, `first-run-11-flow`, showing the usual path and every other way through each step. PNGs: `design-captures/first-run-2026-11/v104/`.\n8\t\n9\t## Why the built screens confuse\n10\t\n11\tVersion 89 of my board 08 drew the add-printer dialog standing alone on the frame, and the app built it faithfully. A person who just signed in goes from the welcome straight to a dialog headed \"STEP 1 OF 3 · Which printer?\". Nothing says why the app asks. The dialog shows a step counter of its own inside onboarding. It offers four ways out: Cancel, Back, \"Skip, use a default\" and \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\". The \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" link came from a choice Kenneth approved on 2026-11-03; none of my boards showed it until version 105.\n12\t\n13\tSkipping then installs Generic Klipper Printer, and Home shows it as one of the person's printers. The card has a warning triangle, the word \"assumed\", \"Not connected\" and a Connect… button. To someone new it reads as an error with a printer they don't own.\n14\t\n15\t## Board 08: \"Which printer do you have?\" (replaces the dialog on the Printers step)\n16\t\n17\tA screen of its own, laid out like board 07, the OrcaSlicer import screen: lockup top-left, one centred column 520 px wide.\n18\t\n19\t1. **What the welcome finished**, one line with a green check, only when there is something to say:\n20\t   - signed in: \"Signed in as {email} · {balance} credits\"\n21\t   - own key saved: \"The agent uses your Anthropic key\" (name the provider that was saved)\n22\t   - Just slice for now: no line.\n23\t2. **Headline** (page-title): \"Which printer do you have?\"\n24\t3. **Lead** (body, secondary): \"JusPrin plans every print for your printer: its bed, its nozzle and the filament it starts with. You can add more printers later.\"\n25\t4. **Brand** and **Model** menus side by side. Use the same searchable ActionMenus as `AgentUI/src/components/AddPrinterForm.tsx` step 1. Reuse them by moving step 1's fields into a shared component, not by copying them. Printers found on the network show above the menus as they do in the dialog.\n26\t   Under the menus, only when the agent is set up (signed in with credits, or a saved key): \"Can't find your printer?\" (label, secondary) and the link **Ask the agent**. It finishes onboarding and opens Home with the printer chat, the same thing Home's \"+ Add printer\" does today (`OrcaHomeBackend::add_printer()`, which calls `m_open_conversation({}, false)`). After \"Just slice for now\" the line is not shown.\n27\t5. **Nozzle**: a segmented choice of the chosen model's nozzles, starting on `startingNozzle()` (0.4 where offered). Under it: \"Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.\"\n28\t6. **Continue** (primary) and **Skip for now** (link) on one row. Under them, tertiary label: \"Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n29\t7. **The OrcaSlicer folder choice**, one quiet line: \"OrcaSlicer printers in another folder?\" (label, secondary) and the link \"Choose the folder…\". It does what \"Import from an OrcaSlicer folder…\" does today (a47a30ea7f). Kenneth approved this manual folder choice on 2026-11-03, so it stays; only its wording and place change.\n30\t8. **Back** (link) last, as on board 07. Back returns to the welcome, as now.\n31\t\n32\tRemoved from this step: the \"Step 1 of 3\" marker, Cancel, and the plate and filament steps.\n33\t\n34\tContinue adds the printer with its profile's own default plate and filament, through the existing `onboarding_printer_form` / `form_finish` path with `plate` and `filament` left out. Check that the host accepts that. If it needs them, the host picks the profile's default plate and its first suggested filament. The dialog Home opens from \"+ Add printer\" keeps all three steps; only the onboarding step is shortened.\n35\t\n36\t## Board 07: the same carried-over line as 08\n37\t\n38\tWhichever printer screen comes first, 07 or 08, it opens with the line saying what the welcome finished (\"Signed in as … · … credits\", or the saved key), placed above its headline. Kenneth asked for this in a canvas comment on 2026-11-05 (canvas version 107). The import result screen (17) comes after 07, so it doesn't repeat the line.\n39\t\n40\t## Board 07: find the printers ticked in OrcaSlicer, not only the saved ones\n41\t\n42\tToday `detect_orca_profiles()` (`Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp`) counts only the printers saved as presets under OrcaSlicer's `user/<account>/machine`. Printers a person only ticked in OrcaSlicer's printer list are recorded in `OrcaSlicer.conf` under `\"models\"`, as entries like `{\"vendor\": \"BBL\", \"model\": \"Bambu Lab A1 mini\", \"nozzle_diameter\": \"0.4\"}`. Most OrcaSlicer users never save a preset, so the import screen misses them and the person lands on the manual form. On Kenneth's Mac, OrcaSlicer.conf lists six ticked printers (A1 mini, Kobra 3, Ender-3 V2 Neo, K1C, Generic Klipper Printer at 0.6, Qidi X-Plus 4), and `user/` holds three saved copies.\n43\t\n44\tKenneth agreed on 2026-11-05 to include the ticked printers:\n45\t- Read `\"models\"` from OrcaSlicer.conf as well. Map each entry to JusPrin's own system printer for that vendor, model and nozzle. Skip any that JusPrin's profiles don't have, and any already covered by a saved preset of the same printer.\n46\t- List them on 07 with the saved ones, one line per printer. The filament count shows only for saved presets.\n47\t- Import installs and selects each ticked printer from JusPrin's own profiles, as `SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer()` does for the default printer. The saved presets import as now.\n48\t- `orca_printers` is true when either list is non-empty.\n49\t- Add a test with an OrcaSlicer folder that has only ticked printers.\n50\t\n51\t## Board 17: \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\"\n52\t\n53\tAlready built (`ImportResult` in `HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx`); the board now draws it so the canvas matches the app. No change asked.\n54\t\n55\t## Board 10: Home after \"Skip for now\"\n56\t\n57\tThe skipped printer is not shown as a printer. In `HomeUI/src/components/PrinterCard.tsx`, a printer with `assumed: true` renders as a \"No printer yet\" card instead:\n58\t\n59\t- printer icon (secondary) and \"No printer yet\" (body-bold)\n60\t- \"Files slice for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\" (body-small, secondary)\n61\t- **Add your printer** (small primary button), which opens the same add-printer path as \"+ Add printer\"\n62\t\n63\tIt has no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no connection line, no Connect… and no ⋯ menu. The \"+ Add printer\" row is hidden while this card shows. Once the person adds a printer of their own, Home stops listing the generic one. The app keeps the preset so files still slice. The drop-zone line under \"Drop a model or project to start\" says \"JusPrin slices it for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.\"\n64\t\n65\t## Connecting a printer on Home\n66\t\n67\tKenneth agreed the agent handles connecting a printer after this step. That's already built: the printer card's Connect… calls `connect_printer()`, which opens the printer chat (`m_open_conversation(name, true)`). No change needed.\n68\t\n69\t## The printer chip in a project (agreed by Kenneth, 2026-11-05)\n70\t\n71\tThe printer chip also showed the \"assumed\" warning (`HomeUI/src/styles.css`, `.printer-chip .printer-assumed`; board file-printer-05). Kenneth's answer on 2026-11-05: yes. The chip names the generic printer \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\", with no warning triangle and no \"assumed\". Not drawn on the canvas; this line is the spec.\n72\t\n73\t## Board 09\n74\t\n75\tHome after signing in and choosing a printer now shows the one printer picked on 08 (Bambu Lab A1 mini). Same layout as before.\n76\t\n\nThe following deferred tools are now available via ToolSearch. Their schemas are NOT loaded — calling them directly will fail with InputValidationError. Use ToolSearch with query \"select:<name>[,<name>...]\" to load tool schemas before calling them:\nArtifactComments\nArtifactData\nCronCreate\nCronDelete\nCronList\nDesignSync\nEnterPlanMode\nEnterWorktree\nExitPlanMode\nExitWorktree\nListMcpResourcesTool\nListPlugins\nListSkills\nMonitor\nNotebookEdit\nPushNotification\nReadMcpResourceDirTool\nReadMcpResourceTool\nRemoteTrigger\nSearchSkills\nSendMessage\nTaskStop\nWebFetch\nWebSearch\nmcp__1a59c906-04da-521d-bda7-7f71b9f9e01c__create\nmcp__1a59c906-04da-521d-bda7-7f71b9f9e01c__delete\nmcp__1a59c906-04da-521d-bda7-7f71b9f9e01c__export\nmcp__1a59c906-04da-521d-bda7-7f71b9f9e01c__query\nmcp__1a59c906-04da-521d-bda7-7f71b9f9e01c__read\nmcp__6d1092c0-9521-478c-803f-a5a5d76eedd7__fetch\nmcp__6d1092c0-9521-478c-803f-a5a5d76eedd7__list_tags\nmcp__6d1092c0-9521-478c-803f-a5a5d76eedd7__search\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__apply_sensitive_message_label\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__apply_sensitive_thread_label\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__create_draft\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__create_label\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__delete_draft\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__delete_label\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__forward\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__get_draft\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__get_message\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__get_thread\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__label_message\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__label_thread\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__list_drafts\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__list_labels\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__mark_message_spam\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__mark_thread_spam\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__reply\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__search_threads\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__send_message\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__trash_message\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__trash_thread\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__unlabel_message\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__unlabel_thread\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__unmark_message_spam\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__unmark_thread_spam\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__untrash_message\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__untrash_thread\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__update_draft\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__update_label\nmcp__80b2b8bf-408b-48cd-ac08-73e36beb51fd__update_message_labels\nmcp__Claude_Code_iOS_Simulator__build\nmcp__ccd_connectors__reconnect_session_connector\nmcp__ccd_connectors__session_connectors_status\nmcp__ccd_connectors__set_session_connector_enabled\nmcp__ccd_directory__change_directory\nmcp__ccd_directory__request_directory\nmcp__ccd_host__clean_up_worktrees\nmcp__ccd_host__discard_kept_worktree\nmcp__ccd_host__get_storage_usage\nmcp__ccd_host__open_in_editor\nmcp__ccd_host__request_keep_awake\nmcp__ccd_host__reveal_path\nmcp__ccd_host__sync_with_base_branch\nmcp__ccd_pr__bind_pr\nmcp__ccd_pr__get_status\nmcp__ccd_pr__set_auto_merge\nmcp__ccd_pr__set_monitor\nmcp__ccd_pr__unbind_pr\nmcp__ccd_session__list_start_targets\nmcp__ccd_session__move_to_cloud\nmcp__ccd_session__start_session\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__archive_session\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__clear_session\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__delete_session\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__detach_session\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__export_transcript\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__get_session\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__get_usage\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__list_events\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__list_sessions\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__search_session_transcripts\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__send_message\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__set_remote_control\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__set_session_effort\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__set_session_fast_mode\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__set_session_model\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__set_session_output_style\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__set_session_permission_mode\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__set_session_title\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__stop_session\nmcp__ccd_session_mgmt__unarchive_session\nmcp__ccd_settings__get_settings\nmcp__ccd_settings__set_setting\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__create_group\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__create_section\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__delete_group\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__delete_section\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__list_groups\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__list_sections\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__mark_completed\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__move_sessions\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__rename_group\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__rename_section\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__set_pinned\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__set_unread\nmcp__ccd_sidebar__set_view\nmcp__ccd_view__close_pane\nmcp__ccd_view__get_layout\nmcp__ccd_v