{"parentUuid":"ab500dfd-880a-4f31-bfcc-135c0b961a0c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkd2X2m4A4HBkWC3PrBu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01W4gM2nAiAFwQ1bpDnuKYMk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"B=$(find /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror -maxdepth 3 -name build_first_run_page.py | head -1); echo $B; grep -n \"def import_result\" -A45 \"$B\" | grep -oE \"'[A-Z][^']{6,}'\" | head; grep -n \"def orca_import\" -A60 \"$B\" | grep -oE \"'[A-Z0-9][^']{6,}'\" | head -20; cat \"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c/first-run-flow-live-checks-left.md\" | head -40"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2294,"cache_read_input_tokens":124842,"output_tokens":295,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2294,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":295,"cache_read_input_tokens":124842,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2294,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2294},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01W4gM2nAiAFwQ1bpDnuKYMk":{"command":"B=$(find /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror -maxdepth 3 -name build_first_run_page.py | head -1); echo $B; grep -n \"def import_result\" -A45 \"$B\" | grep -oE \"'[A-Z][^']{6,}'\" | head; grep -n \"def orca_import\" -A60 \"$B\" | grep -oE \"'[A-Z0-9][^']{6,}'\" | head -20; cat \"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c/first-run-flow-live-checks-left.md\" | head -40"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgkd2WoMfemSEaPaaRWvC","requestRef":"0970a393-c043-4da4-b5fa-ede1b49e4f05","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1328002-ceb3-499f-909d-25b5c8094b91","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:08:00.115Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"f1328002-ceb3-499f-909d-25b5c8094b91","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"57b8a240-2346-4052-9b4a-2e21da0c2a34","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4gM2nAiAFwQ1bpDnuKYMk","type":"tool_result","content":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py\n'Imported from OrcaSlicer'\n'OrcaSlicer’s own files were not changed.'\n'Continue'\n'Import result'\n'Imported from OrcaSlicer'\n'STL, 3MF, STEP, OBJ, AMF, SVG or ZIP. JusPrin asks what the part is for, then plans the print for your Bambu Lab A1.'\n'JusPrin account'\n'Connected'\n'First-month credits'\n'Expires 2 Dec'\n'Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?'\n'JusPrin copies these printers with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.'\n'Start fresh'\n'Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer'\n'Add a printer'\n'Skip, use a default'\n'Add printer'\n'Signed in as {EMAIL} · 500 credits'\n'The agent uses your Anthropic key'\n'Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.'\n'Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.'\n'Done on the welcome'\n'Which printer do you have?'\n# First-run flow: live checks still to do\n\nBranch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` (commits ae9cf1f2ac, b8fd2727d9, 7d68c4f91b, 914e48b77f). The build is at\n`.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64/src/Release/OrcaSlicer.app`.\n\nThe screen was locked for most of the run. WebKit does not run the pages of a hidden window, so the built app's Home page could not be driven. These doors were not run in the built app:\n\n1. Your own API key. Preferences should open on Agent. Closing it unfinished should leave the welcome.\n2. Claude Code or Claude Desktop. Done should move to Printers. Pressing Done for real means connecting a tool, which writes to the real Claude config, so send `shell_action {action:'close', done:'tool'}` from the Preferences page instead.\n3. Just slice. This should show the OrcaSlicer import step. Then test Back, Start fresh, and \"Skip, use a default\", which should land on Home with the doors and an \"assumed\" Generic Klipper.\n4. Import. This should land on Home with the imported printers.\n\nThe OrcaSlicer import step appears only when a folder named `OrcaSlicer` sits next to the data folder. With `--datadir X/JusPrin`, put a copy at `X/OrcaSlicer`, holding `user/`, `system/`, and an `OrcaSlicer.conf` that contains only `app.preset_folder`.\n\nThe method: set `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` and `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL` to copies of the bundled pages, with an injected script that polls a local server for commands. The scripts are in this session's scratchpad: `drive/server.py`, `drive/run.sh`, and `drive/watch.sh`.\n\nDo NOT press \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on this Mac. The default browser is already signed in to JusPrin as k@obico.io, so the sign-in finishes on its own.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"475a6149-7463-4cdb-86b2-412fffee080d","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:08:00.323Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py\n'Imported from OrcaSlicer'\n'OrcaSlicer’s own files were not changed.'\n'Continue'\n'Import result'\n'Imported from OrcaSlicer'\n'STL, 3MF, STEP, OBJ, AMF, SVG or ZIP. JusPrin asks what the part is for, then plans the print for your Bambu Lab A1.'\n'JusPrin account'\n'Connected'\n'First-month credits'\n'Expires 2 Dec'\n'Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer?'\n'JusPrin copies these printers with their filaments, settings and printer connections. OrcaSlicer keeps its own copy.'\n'Start fresh'\n'Bring your printers from OrcaSlicer'\n'Add a printer'\n'Skip, use a default'\n'Add printer'\n'Signed in as {EMAIL} · 500 credits'\n'The agent uses your Anthropic key'\n'Skip, and JusPrin slices for a generic 0.4 mm printer until you add yours.'\n'Most printers ship with 0.4 mm.'\n'Done on the welcome'\n'Which printer do you have?'\n# First-run flow: live checks still to do\n\nBranch `claude/first-run-flow-f7be35` (commits ae9cf1f2ac, b8fd2727d9, 7d68c4f91b, 914e48b77f). The build is at\n`.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35/build/arm64/src/Release/OrcaSlicer.app`.\n\nThe screen was locked for most of the run. WebKit does not run the pages of a hidden window, so the built app's Home page could not be driven. These doors were not run in the built app:\n\n1. Your own API key. Preferences should open on Agent. Closing it unfinished should leave the welcome.\n2. Claude Code or Claude Desktop. Done should move to Printers. Pressing Done for real means connecting a tool, which writes to the real Claude config, so send `shell_action {action:'close', done:'tool'}` from the Preferences page instead.\n3. Just slice. This should show the OrcaSlicer import step. Then test Back, Start fresh, and \"Skip, use a default\", which should land on Home with the doors and an \"assumed\" Generic Klipper.\n4. Import. This should land on Home with the imported printers.\n\nThe OrcaSlicer import step appears only when a folder named `OrcaSlicer` sits next to the data folder. With `--datadir X/JusPrin`, put a copy at `X/OrcaSlicer`, holding `user/`, `system/`, and an `OrcaSlicer.conf` that contains only `app.preset_folder`.\n\nThe method: set `JUSPRIN_HOME_DEV_URL` and `JUSPRIN_AGENT_DEV_URL` to copies of the bundled pages, with an injected script that polls a local server for commands. The scripts are in this session's scratchpad: `drive/server.py`, `drive/run.sh`, and `drive/watch.sh`.\n\nDo NOT press \"Sign in for 500 credits\" on this Mac. The default browser is already signed in to JusPrin as k@obico.io, so the sign-in finishes on its own.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f1328002-ceb3-499f-909d-25b5c8094b91","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
