{"parentUuid":"ac9c0bdb-44da-4cc6-95d8-a30971c2480d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkd52Z59WHNiZovffkNy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_read_input_tokens":135438,"output_tokens":2220,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":29},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2220,"cache_read_input_tokens":135438,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":649,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgkd52LBQvAkZHWYaNBhm","requestRef":"1a71a816-e7d9-452a-b73f-a1b2aa0ca361","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5bbb6ac-c38d-4277-a9bc-2923b4eb2e82","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:08:28.479Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"c5bbb6ac-c38d-4277-a9bc-2923b4eb2e82","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkd52Z59WHNiZovffkNy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DnADfSwvCdQoC5WAbmXTg1","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d","summary":"First-run flow: final build and test instructions","message":"First-run flow: the design is final on canvas version 108. Please build it and prove every path in the built app, especially the OrcaSlicer import.\n\nKenneth wrote this to the design session at 2026-11-05 23:08: \"The new flow looks good now. After you have processed all of my comments, sent the instructions to the coding agents to make sure the flow works as expected, especially the logic around importing from orcaslicer\". All of his canvas comments are now answered.\n\nThe spec is /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md. It is untracked; read it from the main checkout. I just added a \"Details the design session settled\" list under the ticked-printers section, and changed what Back does on 08. The canvas version 108 change itself was layout only: the old JusPrin v1 boards are marked superseded. Nothing else on the screens changed.\n\nOrcaSlicer import: what to build\n\n1. detect_orca_profiles() in Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp reads only the saved presets under user/<account>/machine. Add the printers in OrcaSlicer.conf \"models\", plus the printer OrcaSlicer has selected (\"presets\": {\"machine\": ...}). Map each one to JusPrin's own system printer for that vendor, model and nozzle. Drop any JusPrin doesn't have.\n   - A saved preset whose `inherits` names that system printer already covers it. In that case list only the saved preset.\n   - orca_printers is true when either list is non-empty.\n2. Board 07 lists the saved printers and the ticked ones together, one line each. Only saved presets show a filament count. 07 also gets the \"Signed in as … · N credits\" line (or \"The agent uses your <provider> key\") above its headline, the same line 08 has.\n3. Import does two things:\n   - Saved presets go through import_orca_files() as now.\n   - Ticked or selected printers are installed and selected from JusPrin's profiles, the way SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer() installs the default printer.\n   After the import, select OrcaSlicer's selected printer if it came over, otherwise the first one imported. Board 17 gets one line per printer. A ticked printer that fails to install shows as not imported, and Retry covers it.\n4. Back on 08 returns to 07 when the person reached 08 through 07's Start fresh (clear fresh_start). Otherwise it returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nFacts from Kenneth's Mac, checked just now (read only; don't modify that folder)\n\n~/Library/Application Support/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer.conf:\n- app.preset_folder is \"\".\n- \"models\" lists Anycubic Kobra 3 0.4, Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4, Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo 0.4, Creality K1C 0.4, Generic Klipper Printer 0.6 and Qidi X-Plus 4 0.4.\n- presets.machine is \"Bambu Lab P1S 0.4 nozzle\", which is not in \"models\".\n\nThe user/ folder holds four account folders:\n- 444387230: 3 saved printers (\"Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo 0.4 nozzle - Copy\", \"Elegoo Neptune 3 Pro 0.4 nozzle - Copy\", \"Qidi X-Plus 4 0.4 nozzle - Copy\").\n- 51a48320-…: the same three. Its Elegoo has a .json but no .info.\n- 75143534 and default: empty.\n\norca_account_folder() takes the account with the newest printer file, so only one of the two accounts is read. That's fine, but test it.\n\nKenneth still got the manual form, not 07, even though this Mac has saved presets. Find out why before calling the import done.\n- My guess (unverified): the app he ran used a scratch --datadir, so it looked for X/OrcaSlicer, found none, and showed 08.\n- Check which data folder that run used and what detect_orca_profiles() returned.\n- Then run the default data folder against the real OrcaSlicer folder: launch with a scratch JusPrin datadir whose parent holds a copy of Kenneth's OrcaSlicer folder.\n\nPaths to prove in the built app (screenshots or the Home snapshot JSON for each)\n\nA. Orca printers found, signed in. Welcome, then 07 with the signed-in line and the saved, ticked and selected printers, then Import, then 17 with one line each, then Continue, then Home 09. Check that the selected printer is OrcaSlicer's P1S and that files slice.\nB. Orca folder with only ticked printers and no saved presets. 07 still shows and the import installs them. Add this as a unit test too.\nC. 07, then Start fresh, then 08, then Back. You should land on 07, not the welcome.\nD. No OrcaSlicer folder. You should go straight to 08. 08's \"Choose the folder…\" with a valid folder should go to 07 for that folder. With a folder holding no printers, the error line should show and you stay on 08.\nE. 08 Continue. The printer is added with its profile's default plate and filament, and no \"Step 1 of 3\", plate or filament steps show. Then Home 09.\nF. 08 \"Ask the agent\". It shows only when signed in with credits or with a saved key, and is hidden after \"Just slice for now\". Pressing it finishes onboarding and opens Home with the printer chat.\nG. 08 \"Skip for now\". Home shows the \"No printer yet\" card (board 10): no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no Connect…, and \"+ Add printer\" hidden. The project printer chip reads \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\". Adding a real printer afterwards removes the generic one from Home.\nH. An import that brings no printer, for example when every printer fails. Continue on 17 should go to 08.\nI. Quit at 07, 08 and 17, and relaunch each time. It should resume on the same screen.\nJ. JusPrin v1 imported, or a file opened during the sequence. The Printers step should be skipped.\n\nReport back which paths you saw pass in the built app. For each path you could only cover with tests or the fake host page, say so and give the reason.","type":"message","recipient":"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d","recipient_kind":"session","content":"First-run flow: the design is final on canvas ver…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_read_input_tokens":135438,"output_tokens":2220,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":29},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2220,"cache_read_input_tokens":135438,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1564,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1564},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DnADfSwvCdQoC5WAbmXTg1":{"to":"local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d","summary":"First-run flow: final build and test instructions","message":"First-run flow: the design is final on canvas version 108. Please build it and prove every path in the built app, especially the OrcaSlicer import.\n\nKenneth wrote this to the design session at 2026-11-05 23:08: \"The new flow looks good now. After you have processed all of my comments, sent the instructions to the coding agents to make sure the flow works as expected, especially the logic around importing from orcaslicer\". All of his canvas comments are now answered.\n\nThe spec is /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/first-run-printer-step-spec-2026-11-05.md. It is untracked; read it from the main checkout. I just added a \"Details the design session settled\" list under the ticked-printers section, and changed what Back does on 08. The canvas version 108 change itself was layout only: the old JusPrin v1 boards are marked superseded. Nothing else on the screens changed.\n\nOrcaSlicer import: what to build\n\n1. detect_orca_profiles() in Home/OrcaHomeBackend.cpp reads only the saved presets under user/<account>/machine. Add the printers in OrcaSlicer.conf \"models\", plus the printer OrcaSlicer has selected (\"presets\": {\"machine\": ...}). Map each one to JusPrin's own system printer for that vendor, model and nozzle. Drop any JusPrin doesn't have.\n   - A saved preset whose `inherits` names that system printer already covers it. In that case list only the saved preset.\n   - orca_printers is true when either list is non-empty.\n2. Board 07 lists the saved printers and the ticked ones together, one line each. Only saved presets show a filament count. 07 also gets the \"Signed in as … · N credits\" line (or \"The agent uses your <provider> key\") above its headline, the same line 08 has.\n3. Import does two things:\n   - Saved presets go through import_orca_files() as now.\n   - Ticked or selected printers are installed and selected from JusPrin's profiles, the way SetupCommands::install_and_select_printer() installs the default printer.\n   After the import, select OrcaSlicer's selected printer if it came over, otherwise the first one imported. Board 17 gets one line per printer. A ticked printer that fails to install shows as not imported, and Retry covers it.\n4. Back on 08 returns to 07 when the person reached 08 through 07's Start fresh (clear fresh_start). Otherwise it returns to the welcome, as now.\n\nFacts from Kenneth's Mac, checked just now (read only; don't modify that folder)\n\n~/Library/Application Support/OrcaSlicer/OrcaSlicer.conf:\n- app.preset_folder is \"\".\n- \"models\" lists Anycubic Kobra 3 0.4, Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4, Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo 0.4, Creality K1C 0.4, Generic Klipper Printer 0.6 and Qidi X-Plus 4 0.4.\n- presets.machine is \"Bambu Lab P1S 0.4 nozzle\", which is not in \"models\".\n\nThe user/ folder holds four account folders:\n- 444387230: 3 saved printers (\"Creality Ender-3 V2 Neo 0.4 nozzle - Copy\", \"Elegoo Neptune 3 Pro 0.4 nozzle - Copy\", \"Qidi X-Plus 4 0.4 nozzle - Copy\").\n- 51a48320-…: the same three. Its Elegoo has a .json but no .info.\n- 75143534 and default: empty.\n\norca_account_folder() takes the account with the newest printer file, so only one of the two accounts is read. That's fine, but test it.\n\nKenneth still got the manual form, not 07, even though this Mac has saved presets. Find out why before calling the import done.\n- My guess (unverified): the app he ran used a scratch --datadir, so it looked for X/OrcaSlicer, found none, and showed 08.\n- Check which data folder that run used and what detect_orca_profiles() returned.\n- Then run the default data folder against the real OrcaSlicer folder: launch with a scratch JusPrin datadir whose parent holds a copy of Kenneth's OrcaSlicer folder.\n\nPaths to prove in the built app (screenshots or the Home snapshot JSON for each)\n\nA. Orca printers found, signed in. Welcome, then 07 with the signed-in line and the saved, ticked and selected printers, then Import, then 17 with one line each, then Continue, then Home 09. Check that the selected printer is OrcaSlicer's P1S and that files slice.\nB. Orca folder with only ticked printers and no saved presets. 07 still shows and the import installs them. Add this as a unit test too.\nC. 07, then Start fresh, then 08, then Back. You should land on 07, not the welcome.\nD. No OrcaSlicer folder. You should go straight to 08. 08's \"Choose the folder…\" with a valid folder should go to 07 for that folder. With a folder holding no printers, the error line should show and you stay on 08.\nE. 08 Continue. The printer is added with its profile's default plate and filament, and no \"Step 1 of 3\", plate or filament steps show. Then Home 09.\nF. 08 \"Ask the agent\". It shows only when signed in with credits or with a saved key, and is hidden after \"Just slice for now\". Pressing it finishes onboarding and opens Home with the printer chat.\nG. 08 \"Skip for now\". Home shows the \"No printer yet\" card (board 10): no warning triangle, no \"assumed\", no Connect…, and \"+ Add printer\" hidden. The project printer chip reads \"Generic printer · 0.4 mm\". Adding a real printer afterwards removes the generic one from Home.\nH. An import that brings no printer, for example when every printer fails. Continue on 17 should go to 08.\nI. Quit at 07, 08 and 17, and relaunch each time. It should resume on the same screen.\nJ. JusPrin v1 imported, or a file opened during the sequence. The Printers step should be skipped.\n\nReport back which paths you saw pass in the built app. For each path you could only cover with tests or the fake host page, say so and give the reason."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgkd52LBQvAkZHWYaNBhm","requestRef":"1a71a816-e7d9-452a-b73f-a1b2aa0ca361","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"636d0a4c-2b57-44b3-9773-95f95c692287","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:08:48.393Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
