{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","id":"bca8eb20-2120-4abd-bbd4-d956e658dcf2","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:14:10.952Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"318adc7d46bd3e88aa2b9d30a92d623f0be6da8efb8ec77b24b2e6d0031e31f9","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"72082503-cf06-47df-8c8f-10d1cc87f7de","keep":77,"tail":["babca19da2bbf0138850d2d56588abf7fd421fd9a890d8b262d32f881d8e2109","8510bea8a0073b41da56ae1a8bae7b6bcc967d5be0ad2bd8c3e1830cd62218e7","8d5417819870814c986d7076932ad2dcad28287bdd05a674772b4c6ce5fb42e5"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",79,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"0fc319bf973a794053fe1aa54d78d8273855d0cab063eff49ff512909915ff47"}
{"parentUuid":"102b52f0-2e80-4416-97fa-924610d7ef56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgknfCVMr3tGddioTziaC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Mostly yes: reuse what the screen shows, but not the screen as it stands. Someone who picks the menu item is already working in the app. They might have a project open, and printers they set up last week. The OrcaSlicer import screen was designed as one step of the first launch, so three of its parts make no sense outside it:\n\n- The full window covers whatever the person was doing. Show the same content in a dialog over the app instead: the list of printers found, the Import button, then the \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\" result with Continue.\n- The \"Signed in as … · 500 credits\" line at the top, \"Start fresh\" and Back are all about the first launch. In the dialog, drop all three and use Cancel.\n- If the app finds no OrcaSlicer folder, the dialog should say so and offer \"Choose the folder…\" right away. It shouldn't fall through to the add-printer form.\n\n**One real problem to fix first.** I checked the import code on the coding branch (`plan_orca_import` in [OrcaImport.cpp:136](src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/Home/OrcaImport.cpp:136)). When a preset with the same name is already in JusPrin, the import doesn't skip it. It saves another copy named \"… (Orca copy)\", then \"(Orca copy 2)\", and so on. That never mattered during the first launch, which runs once. With a menu item, running it twice doubles every printer, filament and process. **Proposed:** in the dialog's list, mark printers already in JusPrin \"Already in JusPrin\" and skip them, and import only the new ones. If nothing is new, the dialog says so and has only a Close button.\n\n**Where the menu item goes.** OrcaSlicer's File › Import submenu already has \"Import Configs…\". It loads single config files, and that is OrcaSlicer's own code. Add \"Import from OrcaSlicer…\" next to it, in [MainFrame.cpp:2768](src/slic3r/GUI/MainFrame.cpp:2768). MainFrame.cpp is an OrcaSlicer file, so this should be one added line that calls into the fork's code, as the fork's stewardship rules require."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":567,"cache_read_input_tokens":144993,"output_tokens":702,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":567,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":702,"cache_read_input_tokens":144993,"cache_creation_input_tokens":567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":567},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgknfCFEbiPDHAutaqw5u","requestRef":"bca8eb20-2120-4abd-bbd4-d956e658dcf2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a79cb98-f7ff-4b76-bd68-0b9beb0dc68f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:14:19.154Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/.claude/worktrees/first-run-flow-f7be35","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
